\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 New \u8216\'20\'18Striketober\u8217\'20\'19 looms as US walkouts increase amid surge in union activity\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,054 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 September 2022\par 07:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Support for unions is on the rise as workers take action to raise pay and conditions amid booming company profits\par \par \uc2 Thousands of workers around the US are going on strike or threatening to do so heading into October, amid a recent surge of labor action activity in America and just one month before crucial midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Support for labor unions in the US has grown over the past year, as a surge in organizing has resulted in workers winning union elections at major corporations including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/28/starbucks-workers-buffalo-ny-organizing-union-first-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starbucks}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/apr/09/amazon-union-organization-staten-island"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/19/apple-workers-vote-to-join-union-a-first-for-the-tech-giant-in-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Apple}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.eater.com/23327054/chipotle-union-michigan-location-teamsters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chipotle}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/04/trader-joes-union-workers-labor-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/01/04/technology/google-employees-union.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Google}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/27/us-union-boom-starbucks-amazon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 REI}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mynorthwest.com/3437537/verizon-stores-in-everett-lynnwood-vote-to-join-union/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Verizon}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Union election petitions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/news-outreach/news-story/correction-first-three-quarters-union-election-petitions-up-58-exceeding"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased 58%}}}\uc2  in the first three quarters of fiscal year 2022, compared with 2021. Public support for labor unions is at its highest point since 1965, according to the most recent Gallup poll, with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/398303/approval-labor-unions-highest-point-1965.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 71% approval }}}\uc2  of labor unions in the US.\par \par \uc2 According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://striketracker.ilr.cornell.edu/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 labor action tracker}}}\uc2  at \uc2 Cornell University\uc2 , strikes in 2022 so far have significantly outpaced strike activity in 2021, with 180 strikes involving 78,000 workers in the first six months of 2022, compared with 102 strikes involving 26,500 workers in the first six months of 2021. The tracker recorded 41 strikes that started between 15 August and 15 September 2022, involving 35,250 workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStrikes appear to be increasing as we head into the fall,\u8221\'20\'1D said Johnnie Kallas, project director for the Cornell University ILR labor action tracker. \u8220\'20\'1CThese strikes are being led by workers in the service sector. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers have organized over 70 strikes so far this year in response to poor working conditions and employer retaliation. Over the past month, thousands of healthcare workers and educators have gone on strike to protest understaffing, low pay and poor conditions for patients and students.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last October was also dubbed \u8220\'20\'1CStriketober\u8221\'20\'1D by the US labor movement as a number of high-profile labor strikes and strike threats occurred throughout the month.\par \par \uc2 Some of the largest strikes in recent weeks in the US have included {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/sep/12/minnesota-nurses-three-day-strike-pay-understaffing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 15,000 nurses}}}\uc2  who went on a three-day strike in Minnesota, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kptv.com/2022/09/14/over-1100-timber-workers-strike-across-oregon-washington/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over 1,100 timber workers }}}\uc2  in Oregon and Washington, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://spectrumnews1.com/oh/columbus/news/2022/08/25/ohio-teachers--union--school-board-reach-agreement--end-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over 4,500 teachers and staff }}}\uc2  in Columbus, Ohio, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2022/09/12/1122481696/6-000-seattle-teachers-and-school-staff-remain-on-strike-after-failed-weekend-ta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 6,000 teachers}}}\uc2  and staff in Seattle, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://danvillesanramon.com/news/2022/09/18/no-agreement-reached-yet-as-kaiser-mental-health-worker-strike-reaches-one-month"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2,000 mental healthcare workers}}}\uc2  in California, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.detroitnews.com/story/business/autos/chrysler/2022/09/10/uaw-members-stellantis-casting-plant-kokomo-indiana-strike-local-contract/8047999001/?gnt-cfr=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 1,200 casting plant workers}}}\uc2  at \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  in Indiana, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mcall.com/business/mc-nws-easton-nursing-home-strike-20220902-ierv2pcejzao5et2h3pfnzu7iq-story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 700 nursing home workers }}}\uc2  in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Among the groups of workers that have recently authorized strikes include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://spectrumnews1.com/ma/worcester/news/2022/09/12/clark-university-graduate-workers-union-strike-authorization-vote-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 graduate workers}}}\uc2  at Clark University, while graduate workers at \uc2 Indiana University\uc2  will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heraldtimesonline.com/story/news/education/campus/2022/09/15/iu-makes-more-concessions-with-graduate-workers-strike-vote-upcoming/69492764007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 soon decide}}}\uc2  whether to resume a strike from earlier this year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vindy.com/news/local-news/2022/09/union-recognition-sought-at-ultium-cells/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 800 auto workers}}}\uc2  at the Ultium Cells electric vehicle plant in \uc2 Lordstown\uc2 , Ohio, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wkbn.com/news/local-news/battery-plant-workers-could-strike-over-unionization/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to authorize a strike }}}\uc2  for union recognition this month, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://inthesetimes.com/article/rail-strike-biden-union-labor-tentative-agreement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 115,000 railroad workers could still strike }}}\uc2  if they decide to vote down tentative contract agreements in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 UFCW\uc2  Local 1059, representing about 12,500 workers at \uc2 Kroger\uc2  grocery stores in the Columbus, Ohio, area {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.10tv.com/article/news/local/kroger-workers-union-votes-strike-authorization/530-4c1da990-d93a-43cf-8ea3-186cf9b35983"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to authorize a strike}}}\uc2  on 16 September after rejecting the third contract proposal offered to members, \uc2 Kroger\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s latest and final offer.\par \par \uc2 A strike date hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been set yet. A \uc2 Kroger\uc2  employee who voted in favor of authorizing the strike, but requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation, explained they feel they have no choice due to many longtime workers still receiving poverty wages while working short-staffed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe should be making a living wage right now,\u8221\'20\'1D the worker said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve made a ton of money for the higher-ups, they\u8217\'20\'19ve made a ton of money for their shareholders. But once again they\u8217\'20\'19re saying that they can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to pay us the wages that we just need to survive.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The worker argued the proposed wage increases didn\u8217\'20\'19t align with prices that have increased on customers and with \uc2 Kroger\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s profits, which have soared throughout the pandemic, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ir.kroger.com/CorporateProfile/press-releases/press-release/2022/Kroger-Reports-Fourth-Quarter-and-Full-Year-2021-Results/default.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with $3.5bn}}}\uc2  in operating profit in 2021 and projections of at least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/kroger-reports-second-quarter-2022-results-and-raises-full-year-guidance-301621163.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $4.6bn in operating profit}}}\uc2  in 2022, in addition to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ir.kroger.com/CorporateProfile/press-releases/press-release/2021/Kroger-Board-of-Directors-Approves-1-Billion-Share-Repurchase-Authorization/default.aspx#:~:text=CINCINNATI%2C%20Dec.,as%20of%20December%2029%2C%202021."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 authorizing}}}\uc2  a $1bn stock buyback.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know for a lot of people that this strike is a really huge personal sacrifice to them, but we don\u8217\'20\'19t have any other options,\u8221\'20\'1D the worker added. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not trying to be greedy. But we\u8217\'20\'19re just really tired and we sacrificed a whole lot during the pandemic.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In Boston, about 300 workers at \uc2 Sysco\uc2  have a strike vote scheduled for 25 September as their contract is set to expire at the end of the month, with the union alleging \uc2 Sysco\uc2  has been dragging out negotiations, which \uc2 Sysco\uc2  has denied. \uc2 Sysco\uc2  workers have gone on strike so far this year in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wbaltv.com/article/sysco-workers-strike-jessup/39863587#"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Baltimore, Maryland, area}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://knsiradio.com/2022/02/10/teamsters-local-120-on-strike-alleging-sysco-western-minnesota-violated-labor-law-practices/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 St Cloud, Minnesota}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been called essential workers for the longest time and now it\u8217\'20\'19s just empty words,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trevor Ashley, a driver at \uc2 Sysco\uc2  in Boston for over 20 years.\par \par \uc2 In Buffalo, New York, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://buffalonews.com/business/local/votes-are-in-kaleida-health-union-workers-authorize-a-strike-if-contract-cant-be-reached/article_ec145d56-3509-11ed-8e87-bfc85a9a25dd.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over 6,300 healthcare workers}}}\uc2  at \uc2 Kaleida Health\uc2  voted to authorize a strike on 15 September amid their new union contract negotiations, with 96% in support. In the event of a strike, the unions representing workers will have to issue a 10-day notice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey left us no choice but to authorize a strike. For them to say they\u8217\'20\'19re listening is not accurate,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kim Kornowski, a registered nurse at Millard Fillmore Suburban hospital.\par \par \uc2 Workers at \uc2 Kaleida Health\uc2  claimed staffing shortages and cuts have increased workloads and worsened working conditions throughout the pandemic, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.1199seiu.org/media-center/breaking-kaleida-health-workers-vote-authorize-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hundreds of vacant positions}}}\uc2  that still need to be filled.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re there to help take care of patients, but when there\u8217\'20\'19s only one of me and a nurse that has seven or eight patients, it\u8217\'20\'19s hard for us to take care of patients,\u8221\'20\'1D said Betty Thompson, a patient care assistant at \uc2 Kaleida Health\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kaleida Health\uc2  has said it is making strike contingency preparations as they continue working to reach a contract with the union, but claimed the recent union proposal was too expensive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we want is a fair contract that appropriately rewards our workforce and positions the organization for the future. That includes no concessionary bargaining, addressing staffing needs, and once again becoming the market leader in wages,\u8221\'20\'1D said a \uc2 Kaleida Health\uc2  spokesperson.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220926ei9q0015p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
