\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re ready to strike\u8217\'20\'19: \uc2 UPS\uc2  workers and \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  prepare for contract fight\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 792 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 September 2022\par 09:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Employees are pushing for better overtime protections, improved pay for part-time employees and heat protections\par \par \uc2 For eight years, Rob Becker worked as a delivery driver for \uc2 UPS\uc2  in Queens, New York. About five years ago, he was terminated. He got involved in his local union, Teamsters Local 804, and fought, successfully, to get reinstated.\par \par \uc2 While pushing for changes and collecting signatures in recent months at \uc2 UPS\uc2  as the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  prepare for a new union contract fight across at the company in 2023, Becker, an alternate union steward, was again fired from his job.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI guess I was costing the company too much money,\u8221\'20\'1D said Becker. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are constantly harassed and intimidated by our management. It\u8217\'20\'19s never-ending, we do go through some calm periods, but inevitably it turns back up at some point when they decide to crack the whip.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said his termination noted that he was fired for taking a two- to three-minute break in the morning to get a drink of water.\par \par \uc2 In the new union contract, Becker and other workers have been pushing for better overtime protections, an elimination of a second tier of delivery drivers who are paid less and provided with less protections for doing the same work, better pay for part-time employees and heat protection.\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2  workers and the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have signaled preparations to strike to win these demands in the next union contract.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are ready to strike 100%. It\u8217\'20\'19s obviously a weapon of last resort,\u8221\'20\'1D said Becker.\par \par \uc2 In August, Teamsters International launched the contract fight at \uc2 UPS\uc2 , as the union leadership {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/teamsters-union-elects-sean-obrien-as-new-leader-11637334914"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newly elected}}}\uc2  in 2021 has signaled an end to accepting concessions in union contracts with \uc2 UPS\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The union is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2022/08/6-issues-that-could-push-ups-drivers-to-strike-as-they-gear-up-to-negotiate-a-new-contract/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fighting}}}\uc2  for the end of misclassifying workers as a means to pay them less, such as personal vehicle drivers who work as temporary contractors. They also want the increasing surveillance of drivers on the job, a two-tier employee system of drivers, at least a $20 an hour starting pay for part-time employees and heat protections as \uc2 UPS\uc2  vehicles are not equipped with air conditioning.\par \par \uc2 UPS{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/26/ups-part-time-workers-pay-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut}}}\uc2  hourly pay for many part-time workers earlier this year, as the company reported record profits of nearly $13bn in 2021.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur union is resolved to win the best contract for \uc2 UPS\uc2  members and to reset the standards for wages and benefits in this industry by August 1, 2023. We won\u8217\'20\'19t extend negotiations by a single day. We\u8217\'20\'19ll either have a signed agreement that day or be hitting the pavement,\u8221\'20\'1D the Teamsters International president, Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://teamster.org/2022/08/ups-teamsters-kick-off-contract-fight/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Ben Douglass, another \uc2 UPS\uc2  driver in Queens, New York for two years, was also fired on 24 August, the same day as Becker, while serving as an alternate union steward. He said over the past six months, retaliation and harassment has ramped up.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMyself and other worker activists have become thorns in the side of management. In the lead up to the contract fight, management has a strategy of trying to scare the workforce so people aren\u8217\'20\'19t fully prepared to fight against accepting a subpar contract,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Douglass is one of the delivery drivers who is classified as a 22.4 driver, in the second tier of delivery drivers where pay is much lower and they don\u8217\'20\'19t receive overtime protections. He\u8217\'20\'19s also fighting to improve pay and working conditions for part-time workers and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/08/ups-drivers-union-heat-temperatures-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heat protections}}}\uc2  in the wake of drivers requiring medical attention and the heat-related death of 24-year-old driver Esteban Chavez in California earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 Douglass and Becker have both filed grievances to push to be reinstated to their positions view their firings as part of targeting of union activists and organizers in the workplace ahead of the new union contract fight.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think there\u8217\'20\'19s a systematic policy from the \uc2 UPS\uc2  management to target activists in the workplace and there\u8217\'20\'19s a culture of harassment and retaliation,\u8221\'20\'1D added Douglass.\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2  did not comment on the firings and claims of retaliation.\par \par \uc2 In regards to the union contract negotiations, a \uc2 UPS\uc2  spokesperson said in an email: \u8220\'20\'1CThese, and many others, are important topics that we will discuss as part of our negotiation. \uc2 UPS\uc2  and the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have worked cooperatively for almost 100 years to meet the needs of \uc2 UPS\uc2  employees, customers, and the communities where we live and work. We have built \uc2 UPS\uc2  into the world\u8217\'20\'19s leading package delivery company together, which has also bolstered \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  membership over the years. We believe we\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to find common ground with the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  and reach an agreement that\u8217\'20\'19s good for everyone involved.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220905ei95001gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
