\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s broke labor laws in effort to stop stores unionizing, workers say\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 935 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 September 2022\par 09:45 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Situation is notable as the company has cultivated a liberal brand ethos and anti-union moves are likely to dent that public image\par \par \uc2 Workers at Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s successfully won union elections this year at stores in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.boston.com/news/local-news/2022/07/28/trader-joes-workers-in-hadley-approve-union-drive/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hadley, Massachusetts}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://minnesotareformer.com/2022/08/12/minneapolis-trader-joes-becomes-countrys-2nd-unionized-store/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minneapolis, Minnesota}}}\uc2 , but workers now have numerous filed unfair labor practice charges against the specialty US supermarket chain, alleging the company has violated labor laws in trying to prevent further stores from unionizing.\par \par \uc2 The move comes as a wave of unionizing efforts sweeps through sections of the US economy, including at household names like \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon\uc2 . The situation at Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s is especially notable as the firm has cultivated a liberal brand ethos and anti-union moves are likely to dent that public image.\par \par \uc2 In Boulder, Colorado, workers at a Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.denverpost.com/2022/07/27/boulder-trader-joes-unionization/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  a petition with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  to hold a union election in July to join United Food and Commercial Workers Local 7.\par \par \uc2 The same month, Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s announced company-wide increases to compensation and benefits, including an increase to discounts for employees from 10 to 20%, a $10 an hour premium pay for Sundays, an increase to paid time off and market rate pay adjustments over complaints about pay disparities between longer term employees and new hires.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe that was in response to union activity not only in this store, but the other stores around the country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jim Hammons, organizing director at UFCW Local 7. \u8220\'20\'1CThat in itself is illegal, they can\u8217\'20\'19t do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union pulled the election petition recently and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/27-CA-301841"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  unfair labor practice charges over the announcement of new pay and benefits during their unionization campaign and have alleged several other instances of retaliation. They include the use of company property used by some workers at the store to create anti-union buttons and retaliating against a union supporting worker by removing them from their regular Sunday shift and replacing them with an anti-union worker.\par \par \uc2 Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/18-RC-298414"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retained}}}\uc2 Littler Mendelson\uc2 , a union avoidance law firm that \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has also retained as dozens of stores around the US have unionized over the past year.\par \par \uc2 Aspen McKinzie, a Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s worker at the Boulder store, explained the union organizing campaign started earlier this year over complaints from workers about pay increases and benefits that were enacted at the company during the pandemic being taken away without any input from workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very much a shallow attempt to discourage people from unionizing by trying to make them feel like their employer is actually taking care of them. But none of this is secured and they can take it away whenever they want,\u8221\'20\'1D said McKinzie. \u8220\'20\'1CIf they really care that much about us, they\u8217\'20\'19d be paying us a lot more rather than paying a bunch of union busting lawyers to feed lines to our management.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the beginning of the Covid pandemic, Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s chief executive Dan Bane issued a company-wide {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/apr/23/labor-unions-trader-joes-workers-coronavirus-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 memo}}}\uc2  calling union organizing efforts a \u8220\'20\'1Cdistraction\u8221\'20\'1D amid calls for hazard pay and safety protections.\par \par \uc2 That memo was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/23/trader-joes-workers-massachusetts-push-for-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited}}}\uc2  by workers who launched the first union campaign at Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s in Massachusetts earlier this year, claiming that retirement benefits for workers were unilaterally cut in half by the company and pay bumps provided during the pandemic were rescinded despite high inflation concerns.\par \par \uc2 Keenan Dailey, who has worked at Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s for 14 years in Boulder, also cited those cuts as inspiring the union organizing campaign, as workers were disgruntled over those sudden cuts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey were worried that without that extra money they weren\u8217\'20\'19t sure how they were going to pay their bills. Some of them had re-signed up on leases with their apartment, expecting to have that extra $2 an hour,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dailey. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd then to add insult to injury, we found out that the new hires were making $2 more per hour.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He noted that the pay and benefits announcement in July severely disrupted the union campaign, but emphasized that those benefits can be taken away at the whim of the employer without a contract.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you\u8217\'20\'19re union busting, you can do it through the carrot or the stick, so to speak, and Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s was trying to use the carrot,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dailey. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need a contract to keep this. And we might be able to get more stuff too, but if we don\u8217\'20\'19t have a contract, we\u8217\'20\'19re probably losing this in the next year or two, at least some of it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In New York City, the \uc2 United Food and Commercial Workers Union\uc2  (\uc2 UFCW\uc2 ) have filed charges alleging that Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s abruptly closed a wine shop in New York City just days before workers had planned to file for a union election. \uc2 UFCW\uc2  has launched a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://p2a.co/tAPVlMM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 petition}}}\uc2  to demand Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s reopen the store and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gothamist.com/news/workers-were-taking-steps-to-unionize-when-trader-joes-shuttered-union-square-wine-shop"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signaled intent}}}\uc2  to pursue legal action.\par \par \uc2 Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trader-joes-wine-store-closed-new-york-city-union/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied}}}\uc2  the store closure was linked to the unionization efforts, and said the store was closed due to underperformance. But employees were given no prior notice to the store closure and the location had several years left on its lease.\par \par \uc2 Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s did not reply to multiple requests for comment on this story in response to the allegations made by workers in Boulder. In previous comments on unionization efforts, a spokesperson for Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gothamist.com/news/workers-were-taking-steps-to-unionize-when-trader-joes-shuttered-union-square-wine-shop"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CTrader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s respects our crew\u8217\'20\'19s right to support a union \u8211\'20\'13 or not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220904ei94000p1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
