\par\par \uc2 Media\par \b \uc2 Express and Mirror owner plans new US editions as UK staff strike over pay\b0\par\par\uc2 Jim Waterson Media editor \par \uc2 558 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 September 2022\par 20:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Employees at Reach titles yet to be informed of expansion entailing dozens of journalists hired for American websites\par \par \uc2 The Daily Express and Daily Mirror are planning to launch online editions in the US, even though their British journalists are currently on strike over low pay.\par \par \uc2 Staff at the UK news titles have yet to be informed of the proposals to expand across the Atlantic, which have been the subject of internal discussion for some time.\par \par \uc2 Sources at the company said the project would involve hiring dozens of staff to work on a US version of the right-wing Express, with a similar number working on a US edition of the left-leaning Mirror.\par \par \uc2 Despite their differing political outlooks, both publications are owned by the publisher Reach, which declined to comment on the plans.\par \par \uc2 Jim Mullen\uc2 , the chief executive of Reach, who has become the focus of staff anger over his \u163\'00\'A34m pay deal, is said to be eyeing US audiences who read the MailOnline (DailyMail to US readers) and the Sun. Those outlets have attracted substantial online audiences by taking British tabloid values over the Atlantic with a heavy focus on celebrity news.\par \par \uc2 The prospect of new staff in the US being hired to write stories for the Express and Mirror is unlikely to improve relations between British employees and their bosses.\par \par \uc2 Journalists at Reach\u8217\'20\'19s UK and Ireland publications \u8211\'20\'13 which include the Mirror, Express, Daily Star and dozens of local newspapers \u8211\'20\'13 have complained of low morale and pay, with junior employees earning less than \u163\'00\'A320,000 a year even after years of training.\par \par \uc2 Despite high inflation and a cost-of-living crisis, Reach\u8217\'20\'19s management is refusing to consider raising the existing pay offer beyond a 3% increase. After an initial day of strike action on Wednesday, when hundreds of journalists walked out, the \uc2 National Union of Journalists\uc2  has ordered its members to work to rule and not do overtime. A further three-day strike is scheduled to start on 13 September.\par \par \uc2 Offices of Reach were picketed by staff on Wednesday, including at the company\u8217\'20\'19s Canary Wharf headquarters, in London, with employees from all publications standing together.\par \par \uc2 Richard Palmer, the Daily Express royal correspondent and leader of the newspaper\u8217\'20\'19s union chapel, said staff needed more money. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are struggling, particularly the younger digital journalists,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m aware of people who are taking second jobs to try and make ends meet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He blamed senior managers, especially Mullen. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s all about screwing us on labour costs so they can make more money for themselves and shareholders,\u8221\'20\'1D Palmer added.\par \par \uc2 Express staff have received a message of solidarity from the \uc2 RMT union\uc2 , which is currently organising strikes on the rail network.\par \par \uc2 Palmer said this support had been noted in the Express newsroom, despite the publication\u8217\'20\'19s editorials regularly warning that trade unions risked \u8220\'20\'1Cbringing the country to its knees\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of younger people have said \uc2 Mick Lynch\uc2  [secretary general of the RMT] and the RMT have made them realise what unions are about. All papers have editorial lines, journalists working for the papers don\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily always agree with the editorial line. In any walk of life who agrees with their employer on everything?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220901ei91002ha\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
