\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 California fast-food workers close to winning historic protections\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agency \par \uc2 675 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 August 2022\par 22:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 New fast-food council would have power to set standards for wages and working conditions for half a million employees\par \par \uc2 California lawmakers approved a nation-leading measure that would give more than half a million fast-food workers more power and protections, over the objections of restaurant owners who warn it would drive up consumers\u8217\'20\'19 costs.\par \par \uc2 The bill will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/california-minimum-wage-government-and-politics-822a69d5ad48eb2864d6a1e3b5b7a208"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 create a new 10-member Fast Food Council}}}\uc2  with equal numbers of workers\u8217\'20\'19 delegates and employers\u8217\'20\'19 representatives, along with two state officials, empowered to set minimum standards for wages, hours and working conditions in California.\par \par \uc2 A late amendment would cap any minimum wage increase for fast-food workers at chains with more than 100 restaurants at $22 an hour next year, compared with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/california-gavin-newsom-minimum-wage-inflation-686b6c1ddc9240f76e8e61613717edd8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statewide minimum}}}\uc2  of $15.50 an hour, with cost of living increases thereafter.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe made history today,\u8221\'20\'1D said the \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2  president, \uc2 Mary Kay Henry\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThis legislation is a huge step forward for workers in California and all across the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/01/california-fast-food-workers-bill-fast-recovery-act"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Guardian}}}\uc2  earlier this year they hoped the legislation would help fight low pay, poor working conditions, and a lack of safety protections, problems that have worsened during the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are a lot of laws protecting workers but nobody is implementing or doing anything about it. We are essential workers but not treated like that. With the Fast Recovery Act, we\u8217\'20\'19ll be heard,\u8221\'20\'1D Maria Yolanda Torres, who has worked at a Subway store in San Jose, California, since May 2018, said in March.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.labor.ucla.edu/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Fast-Food-Frontline-Report-1-3-22.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey }}}\uc2  of fast-food workers in Los Angeles published by the UCLA Labor Center in January found workers reported lack of paid sick leave, widespread lack of enforcement of Covid safety protocols and economic insecurity.\par \par \uc2 More than 40% of workers surveyed reported not having enough money to afford groceries during the pandemic, and nearly half said they were doing more than one job to try to make ends meet. Among workers who said they had expressed workplace concerns to their managers, 25% said they had experienced retaliation for doing so.\par \par \uc2 The senate approved Monday\u8217\'20\'19s measure on a 21-12 vote, over bipartisan opposition. Hours later the assembly sent it to the California governor on a final 41-16 vote, both chambers acting with no votes to spare.\par \par \uc2 Debate split along party lines, with Republicans opposed, although three Democratic senators voted against the measure and several did not vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s innovative, it\u8217\'20\'19s bringing industry and workers together at the table,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Democratic senator \uc2 Maria Elena Durazo\uc2 , who carried the bill in the Senate. She called it a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery, very well-balanced method of addressing both the employers, the franchisees, as well as the workers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Almost every Republican senator spoke in opposition, including Senator Brian Dahle, who also is the Republican nominee for governor in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a stepping stone to unionize all these workers. At the end of the day, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to drive up the cost of the products that they serve,\u8221\'20\'1D Dahle said.\par \par \uc2 He added later: \u8220\'20\'1CThere are no slaves that work for California businesses, period. You can quit any day you want and you can go get a job someplace else if you don\u8217\'20\'19t like your employer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Restaurant owners and franchisers cited {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ucreconomicforecast.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/08/WorkerCompensation_Impact_On_Prices_Limited_Service_Restaurant_8_18_2022pdf.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an analysis}}}\uc2  they commissioned by the UC Riverside Center for Economic Forecast and Development saying that the legislation would increase consumers\u8217\'20\'19 costs. The administration of Governor \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://htv-prod-media.s3.amazonaws.com/files/ab-257-20220802051014pm-ab00257-1660194068.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fears the measure}}}\uc2  would create \u8220\'20\'1Ca fragmented regulatory and legal environment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The debate has drawn attention nationwide, including on Capitol Hill where the Democratic congressman \uc2 Ro Khanna{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://khanna.house.gov/sites/khanna.house.gov/files/Final%20Letter%20Khanna.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has expressed hope}}}\uc2  it will trigger similar efforts elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 It was \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the most significant pieces of employment legislation passed in a generation\u8221\'20\'1D, said Columbia Law School labor law expert Kate Andrias. She called it \u8220\'20\'1Ca huge step forward for some of the most vulnerable workers in the country, giving them a collective voice in their working conditions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220830ei8u002pj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
