\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Strippers are standing up\u8217\'20\'19: Los Angeles dancers move to unionize with actors group\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levin in Los Angeles \par \uc2 964 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 August 2022\par 13:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Star Garden workers would be the first strippers to join \uc2 Actors\u8217\'20\'19 Equity Association\uc2 , a national theater actors union\par \par \uc2 Dancers at a Los Angeles strip club have filed to unionize with \uc2 Actors\u8217\'20\'19 Equity Association\uc2 , a move that would make them the first group of strippers to join the national union that represents theater actors.\par \par \uc2 Performers at Star Garden in North Hollywood submitted a petition on Wednesday with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  seeking a union election. The initiative comes after months of staging {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kcrw.com/news/shows/greater-la/star-garden-bar-monarch-butterflies-money-savings/strippers-strike-union-north-hollywood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protests outside the venue}}}\uc2  raising concerns about workplace safety and labor rights. Actors\u8217\'20\'19 Equity \u8211\'20\'13 which represents Broadway actors, stage managers, Disney World performers and other regional theater actors \u8211\'20\'13 said it was supporting the effort and that if it is successful, the Star Garden workers would become the only strippers in the US represented by a union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe like what we do,\u8221\'20\'1D said Velveeta, a Star Garden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kcrw.com/news/shows/greater-la/star-garden-bar-monarch-butterflies-money-savings/strippers-strike-union-north-hollywood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dancer}}}\uc2  who goes by her stage name, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.actorsequity.org/news/PR/StarGarden/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a statement}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe would like our jobs even more if we had basic worker protections. We\u8217\'20\'19re like so many other workers who have learned that it\u8217\'20\'19s not a choice between suffering abuse or quitting. With a union, together, we can make needed improvements to our workplace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The performers first launched the unionization campaign in March in response to the club security guards\u8217\'20\'19 repeated failures to protect the dancers from abuse and threats, \uc2 Actors Equity\uc2  said in a statement. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://knock-la.com/strippers-strike-north-hollywood/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 petition}}}\uc2  to management that month, 15 out of 23 dancers called for workplace safety improvements, including enforcing policies barring customers from filming them and lingering after the club closes for the night, and urging the bar to stop serving customers who become belligerent, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/business/story/2022-08-17/strippers-unionize-star-garden-north-hollywood-union-actors-equity-association"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LA Times reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After the dancers submitted that petition, most were barred from returning to work the next day, according to the paper, which interviewed eight dancers who said they were wrongfully terminated and reviewed signed affidavits submitted to the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  alleging that managers failed to protect them from unwanted touching. The workers have regularly picketed outside the establishment, telling arriving customers about their struggle for better working conditions and discouraging them from patronizing the establishment.\par \par \uc2 An attorney for the club did not immediately respond to a request for comment on Thursday and club management could not immediately be reached.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Actors\u8217\'20\'19 Equity Association\uc2  president, Kate Shindle, said in a statement that the dancers have \u8220\'20\'1Creported consistent compensation issues \u8211\'20\'13 including significant wage theft \u8211\'20\'13 along with health and safety risks and violations\u8221\'20\'1D, adding, \u8220\'20\'1CThey want health insurance and other benefits, like workers\u8217\'20\'19 compensation. They need protection from sexual harassment, discrimination and unjust terminations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shindle said while some aspects of the Star Garden strippers\u8217\'20\'19 jobs were unique, they have much in common with other dancers represented by the union: \u8220\'20\'1CWe applaud their efforts to seize their collective power and unionize, like so many others across the country who are fed up with toxic workplaces. When they approached us for support, we did what unions should do: we said yes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I hope this will help all other parts of the sex industry see that there is a benefit to being collectivized and to laying out specific job standards\par \par \uc2 Maxine Doogan\par \par \uc2 The move comes amid a wave of labor organizing and unionization efforts across the US, including by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/aug/16/mcdonalds-sexual-harassment-retaliation-firings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fast-food workers}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  employees, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/aug/03/delta-flights-attendants-union-push"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flight attendants}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/12/amazon-workers-union-push-north-carolina-kentucky"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon workers}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Although the Star Garden workers would be the first strippers in Actors\u8217\'20\'19 Equity\u8217\'20\'19s 109-year history, the union noted that there was a history of labor activism among club dancers. In San Francisco, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2013/sep/02/lusty-lady-unionized-peep-show-in-trouble"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strippers at the Lusty Lady}}}\uc2  organized the Exotic Dancers Union in 1996 and were affiliated with the \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2 . That establishment closed in 2013.\par \par \uc2 After the filing this week, which the union said was backed by a majority of Star Garden dancers, the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  will schedule an election for roughly 30 performers eligible to vote. If a majority of them support joining Actors\u8217\'20\'19 Equity, the union will begin negotiating its first contract. The effort could be complicated by the fact that some of the strippers have not worked at the venue since March, which means the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  may have to determine they were wrongfully terminated before they can vote, the LA Times reported.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re no longer going to be discriminated against, oppressed, coerced, assaulted, or robbed on the shop floor\par \par \uc2 Antonia Crane\par \par \uc2 Maxine Doogan, a longtime California sex worker rights advocate, said the Star Garden effort was a significant moment: \u8220\'20\'1CI hope this will help all other parts of the sex industry see that there is a benefit to being collectivized and to laying out specific job standards.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Doogan, who organizes with the with the Erotic Service Provider Legal, Educational and Research Project, noted that strippers have long faced challenges, including managers siding with violent customers or strippers having to pay high fees to perform at a club. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is about having their work recognized as employees and to be issued all of those protections that contracted labor doesn\u8217\'20\'19t get. It\u8217\'20\'19s about your right to be able to negotiate for your own workplace safety.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Antonia Crane, founder of Strippers United, a group that has worked with the Star Garden strippers, said the union petition sent a powerful message. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re no longer going to be discriminated against, oppressed, coerced, assaulted, or robbed on the shop floor. Strippers are standing up and resisting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said she has been waiting years for this kind of victory: \u8220\'20\'1CStrippers sit at the crossroads of several kinds of oppression \u8211\'20\'13 complete powerlessness in the workplace and facing a culture of intimidation, misogyny, whorephobia, racism \u8230\'20\'26 This is a really important moment for labor and for feminism.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220818ei8i0035y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
