\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers hold strikes in at least 17 states amid union drive\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 969 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 August 2022\par 13:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers allege over 75 people have been fired in retaliation for organizing this year\par \par \uc2 Workers at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  have held over 55 different strikes in at least 17 states in the US in recent months over the company\u8217\'20\'19s aggressive opposition to a wave of unionization.\par \par \uc2 According to an estimate by Starbucks Workers United, the strikes have cost \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  over $375,000 in lost revenue. The union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bing.com/ck/a?!&&p=f16540133022ace0JmltdHM9MTY1OTc0NDAwMCZpZ3VpZD0wODQyZGNhZC01ODRjLTYyYTEtMzk2NC1jZDg5NTk2NTYzOTAmaW5zaWQ9NTE4MA&ptn=3&hsh=3&fclid=0842dcad-584c-62a1-3964-cd8959656390&u=a1aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuY25iYy5jb20vMjAyMi8wNi8wMi9zdGFyYnVja3MtdW5pb24tY3JlYXRlcy0xLW1pbGxpb24tZnVuZC10by1jb3Zlci1sb3N0LXBheS1mb3Itc3RyaWtpbmctYmFyaXN0YXMuaHRtbA&ntb=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 created}}}\uc2  a $1m strike fund in June 2022 to support \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers through their strikes and several {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://secure.actblue.com/donate/starbucksworkersfund"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 relief funds}}}\uc2  have been established for strikes and to support workers who have lost their jobs.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  employees have alleged over 75 workers have been fired in retaliation for union organizing this year, and hundreds of allegations of misconduct by \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  related to the union campaign are currently under review at the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 , including claims of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/13/starbucks-close-16-us-stores-concern-employee-safety"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shutting down stores}}}\uc2  to bust unions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jul/09/us-starbucks-workers-fired-union-organizing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 firing workers}}}\uc2  and intimidating and threatening workers from unionizing. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has denied all allegations.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthout.org/articles/starbucks-workers-officially-reach-200-union-election-victories/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than 200}}}\uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores around the US have won their union votes, with dozens of stores currently waiting for their election votes.\par \par \uc2 Sam Amato worked at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  for 13 years in Buffalo, New York, before he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gofundme.com/f/support-sam-fired-13-year-starbucks-union-leader?utm_campaign=p_cp+share-sheet&utm_medium=social&utm_source=twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 terminated}}}\uc2  on 5 August, a decision he argues is retaliatory for his strong support for unionization at his store and other \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  locations around the US.\par \par \uc2 He first became involved in the union organizing efforts in the Buffalo area in August 2021 as the first \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores in the US and his own store won their union election in early 2022.\par \par \uc2 In June, Amato and his co-workers were transferred to different stores while their own store underwent remodeling, where he said workers were heavily scrutinized by the store manager through disciplinary actions and write-ups.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy store manager pulled me aside and said that due to an incident when I closed the lobby I was being separated,\u8221\'20\'1D said Amato. \u8220\'20\'1CAny questions I asked, my manager said they were unable to answer and that I would have to call \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  corporate to get an answer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He described that throughout the union organizing efforts, there had been a high turnover of store managers in the Buffalo area, as well as many firings and resignations of workers that have created understaffing issues, which resulted in closing the lobby and operating just the drive-thru in 3 July.\par \par \uc2 Immediately following his firing, several co-workers and other union supporters, shocked at his firing, began an indefinite strike at the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  location in Buffalo to demand his reinstatement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was fired because I\u8217\'20\'19m a union leader and I was very vocal about it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Amato. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Starbucks\uc2  pretends to be an ally and so progressive but they are the opposite and I genuinely have been shocked at how low they\u8217\'20\'19re willing to go.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  did not comment on Sam Amato\u8217\'20\'19s firing.\par \par \uc2 Amid the wave of union elections at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , the company has rolled out new wage increases and benefits corporate wide, but has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bing.com/ck/a?!&&p=902a0d07bc826a3aJmltdHM9MTY1OTc0NDAwMCZpZ3VpZD0wODQyZGNhZC01ODRjLTYyYTEtMzk2NC1jZDg5NTk2NTYzOTAmaW5zaWQ9NTI4Nw&ptn=3&hsh=3&fclid=0842dcad-584c-62a1-3964-cd8959656390&u=a1aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuY25iYy5jb20vMjAyMi8wOC8wMS9zdGFyYnVja3MtdW5pb24tYXNrcy1jb2ZmZWUtZ2lhbnQtdG8tZXh0ZW5kLXBheS1oaWtlcy1iZW5lZml0cy10by11bmlvbml6ZWQtc3RvcmVzLmh0bWw&ntb=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withheld}}}\uc2  the new pay increases and benefits from unionized workers despite the calls from these workers to enact these changes for them as they push for the company to negotiate a first contract with the unionized stores.\par \par \uc2 On 1 August, a unionized \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  store in Jacksonville, Florida, went on strike for one day to demand they also receive the new pay increases and benefits, the day they were implemented company wide.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the last week of July, I think people in my store were really starting to get really aggravated and pissed off that we weren\u8217\'20\'19t receiving the raises,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mason Boykin, a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  worker at the store.\par \par \uc2 Boykin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jacksonville.com/story/business/employment/2022/08/01/jacksonville-starbucks-employees-strike-one-day-delaying-opening/10202709002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  that since their store unionized, workers had experienced schedule changes and hour cuts, which they allege are unfair labor practices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs far as striking goes, I think unionized stores recognize that the only way we\u8217\'20\'19re going to receive what we\u8217\'20\'19re worth is by uniting together and demanding it and that\u8217\'20\'19s through striking,\u8221\'20\'1D added Boykin.\par \par \uc2 Several \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores in Massachusetts also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BostonSBWU/status/1553964052904218624"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held}}}\uc2  a one-day strike over the wage and benefits issue and two stores have continued the strike, while one store in Boston has been on an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BostonSBWU/status/1555759198062927875/photo/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indefinite strike}}}\uc2  since mid-July in demand a store manager be removed or reprimanded for training over allegations of threats and retaliation against workers.\par \par \uc2 Jordie Adams, a \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  worker for six years currently at a non-unionized store in Boston, Massachusetts, after transferring from a unionized store in Connecticut, has been heavily involved in the strike and union organizing in Boston.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWithholding of benefits is definitely affecting people from trying to pursue organizing their stores, which is obviously what \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  corporate is looking to do,\u8221\'20\'1D said Adams.\par \par \uc2 After working for \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  for six years, she said it had been eye-opening to see a different side of corporate that has aggressively opposed unionization.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe all love \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , we love coffee and we think that we can make it better if we\u8217\'20\'19re just given the shot to do it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  said in an email: \u8220\'20\'1CWe currently have strikes happening outside store locations in specific locations in the US. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has great partners and we value their contributions. We respect our partners\u8217\'20\'19 right to engage in any legally protected activity or protest without retaliation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They added: \u8220\'20\'1COnce a store unionizes, no changes to benefits are legally allowed to be made without good faith collective bargaining. Partners still have access to all \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  benefits already in place when the petition was filed, but any changes to wages, benefits and working conditions that \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  establishes after that time would not apply to and would have to be reviewed in bargaining.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220811ei8b001gu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
