\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US sees union boom despite big companies\u8217\'20\'19 aggressive opposition\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,043 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 July 2022\par 11:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Wins for Amazon and \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers shows labor movement surging after years of decline \u8211\'20\'13 but pushback has been fierce\par \par \uc2 After years of decline, the American labor movement is experiencing a resurgence, with an increase in popularity of unions and of workers organizing.\par \par \uc2 But the corporate pushback in America has been fierce, and has come amid allegations of union-busting, and brutal campaigns to try and discourage workers from organizing.\par \par \uc2 An August 2021 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/354455/approval-labor-unions-highest-point-1965.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll }}}\uc2  conducted by Gallup found support for labor unions at their highest point in the US since 1965, with 68% support in the US. Labor unions were the only institution for whom Americans\u8217\'20\'19 approval did not decline over the past year, in a June {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/394283/confidence-institutions-down-average-new-low.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll }}}\uc2  on confidence for 16 major US institutions.\par \par \uc2 During the first three-quarters of the fiscal year, the \uc2 National Labor Relations{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/news-outreach/news-story/correction-first-three-quarters-union-election-petitions-up-58-exceeding"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported }}}\uc2  an increase of union election petitions by 58%, up to 1,892 from 1,197.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NLRB\uc2  is now pushing for increased funding to handle the surge in labor activity. But labor law reform has not been able to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/senate-bill/420?q=%7B%22search%22%3A%5B%22S.420%22%5D%7D&s=1&r=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 get through}}}\uc2  the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , despite being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/842"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed}}}\uc2  in the House.\par \par \uc2 Some of the largest US corporations and brands have seen workers organize for the first time ever.\par \par \uc2 After the first corporate-run \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in the US won its union election in Buffalo in December, about 200 stores have since voted to unionize, leading the resurgence of labor union election petition filings.\par \par \uc2 These victories have come despite aggressive opposition from \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In early June, Austin Locke, a barista at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  for about six years, three at the Ditmars location in Queens, New York, alleged a manager put his hand on him over an issue with completing a Covid check-in before working his shift. He reported the incident to human resources, who he claims were dismissive and defensive.\par \par \uc2 A few weeks later, shortly after his store voted to unionize, he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://qns.com/2022/07/ditmars-boulevard-starbucks-employee-fired-union/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 informed}}}\uc2  his job was terminated over claims he did not complete the Covid check-in, and an allegation that the incident he reported to human resources over the manager was false.\par \par \uc2 Locke is in the process of filing an unfair labor practice charge with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 . He is one of several dozen workers who have done so amid a surge of union organizing at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores.\par \par \uc2 Locke\u8217\'20\'19s dismissal has incited several local groups, workers and community members to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DitmarsSBWU/status/1545452906316500993"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protest}}}\uc2  against his dismissal and rally public support in favor of the union organizing efforts at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re basically out on the street every day to pass out flyers, to let everybody in the community, and the customers that come in that store \u8211\'20\'13 the regulars that I used to see every day \u8211\'20\'13 know that I was illegally fired,\u8221\'20\'1D added Locke.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has denied all allegations of retaliation against workers involved in union organizing, and said there was no physical altercation between Locke and the manager.\par \par \uc2 In April this year, Amazon warehouse staff in Staten Island, New York, won their union election, and union organizing campaigns have gone public at other Amazon warehouses in North Carolina, Kentucky and upstate New York.\par \par \uc2 Heather Goodall, started working at an Amazon warehouse near Albany, New York, in February. \u8220\'20\'1CWithin a week, I was shocked at what I found. There were not enough harnesses for people, they didn\u8217\'20\'19t fit, there were injuries, and it just was overwhelming,\u8221\'20\'1D said Goodall.\par \par \uc2 She started asking co-workers about their thoughts on forming a union, and found there was significant interest, but also fear. But that fear began to dissipate after the Staten Island warehouse won,and other workers saw her success in advocating on behalf of co-workers with their problems at Amazon.\par \par \uc2 After joining the Amazon Labor Union, the independent union that won the union election in Staten Island, Goodall is pushing to gather enough union authorization signatures to merit a union election with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  in the coming weeks. Amazon is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bing.com/ck/a?!&&p=ae3befa44f0cce82cbbe6ae50cb1d73ef19f22a8841367423c3c5f572dff3792JmltdHM9MTY1ODE1NTI0OSZpZ3VpZD04ODAzOWFlMi00MDI1LTQ3MzUtYjcxYi1jNGM0ZDZkZDE1M2YmaW5zaWQ9NTE5OQ&ptn=3&fclid=9d9a399b-06a7-11ed-babe-adb95e63d99d&u=a1aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZW5nYWRnZXQuY29tL2FtYXpvbi1hbGItMS1hbnRpLXVuaW9uLXNpZ25hZ2UtYWx1LTAwNDIwNzgxNC5odG1s&ntb=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposing }}}\uc2  workers doing so.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the first \uc2 Apple\uc2  retail store in the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bing.com/ck/a?!&&p=02d24fc1049902f6792195f96f09c19e365516599d4df632407fc71c542bd44dJmltdHM9MTY1Nzg3NDEyNCZpZ3VpZD02ZTNlNjk2YS00NmQ1LTQ3NGItYmQ5Yy03N2Q2NjcyZjY5MTMmaW5zaWQ9NTE5NA&ptn=3&fclid=11a48bd5-0419-11ed-83f8-d0795ba18fdd&u=a1aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cucmV1dGVycy5jb20vYnVzaW5lc3MvYXBwbGUtd2lsbC1ub3QtY2hhbGxlbmdlLW1hcnlsYW5kLXN0b3JlLXVuaW9uaXphdGlvbi12b3RlLTIwMjItMDYtMjQv&ntb=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won }}}\uc2  its union election in June. Workers at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/23/trader-joes-workers-massachusetts-push-for-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s stores}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nrn.com/fast-casual/workers-michigan-chipotle-mexican-grill-petition-organize-union-affiliation-teamsters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two Chipotle locations}}}\uc2 , and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bing.com/ck/a?!&&p=fd1ddb3980a553f6JmltdHM9MTY1ODQ4NzcwMyZpZ3VpZD0wMTFkODQ0MS0xOTk2LTQ4YzItYmNjYS1hYzZjYjExYjYyZGEmaW5zaWQ9NTE2OQ&ptn=3&hsh=3&fclid=ab7f5a6c-09ad-11ed-8784-6a5aee343d47&u=a1aHR0cHM6Ly90cnV0aG91dC5vcmcvYXJ0aWNsZXMvbHVsdWxlbW9uLXdvcmtlcnMtaW4tZGMtYmVjb21lLXRoZS1sYXRlc3QtdG8tam9pbi1yZXRhaWwtdW5pb24td2F2ZS8&ntb=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lululemon }}}\uc2  retail store have recently filed for union elections, where, if successful, they would be the first locations at these corporations to unionize.\par \par \uc2 The first REI retail store {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bing.com/ck/a?!&&p=157766783bd3f5ce166620d4e2f8a4446ce301eb8abdb64c0373d0420870824eJmltdHM9MTY1Nzg3NDIwMyZpZ3VpZD0wZDFiMzVmZC1iNjM1LTRjNjItYWViNy1hZTUyZjgwZjhhMGMmaW5zaWQ9NTE4Mg&ptn=3&fclid=40d9285c-0419-11ed-aadd-b98e6d6d3a43&u=a1aHR0cHM6Ly9hYmNuZXdzLmdvLmNvbS9CdXNpbmVzcy93aXJlU3RvcnkvcmVpLXN0b3JlLXlvcmstY2l0eS0xc3QtdW5pb25pemUtODMyNDAyMTY&ntb=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 successfully unionized }}}\uc2  in New York City in March, and a second store in Berkeley, California, is holding its union election on 27 July.\par \par \uc2 Jules Gerlitz, an employee at the Berkeley store, said customers are often surprised at the lack of union representation at \uc2 REI\uc2 , given the company is a cooperative and brands itself as progressive.\par \par \uc2 Gerlitz said a common anti-union talking point from \uc2 REI\uc2  managers is to claim that a union contract does not guarantee anything, and could potentially decrease pay and benefits for workers \u8211\'20\'13 which Gerlitz said was an illogical argument because workers would never agree to that ever being on the negotiating table.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CREI has released information that purports to be from a neutral stance. But it\u8217\'20\'19s very clearly anti-union in what it purports to do, in terms of generating this fear, or uncertainty, about all of these things,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gerlitz.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after the store in New York won its union election, \uc2 REI\uc2  corporate released a rollout of new pay and benefits company-wide, though \uc2 REI\uc2  has denied it was in response to the union election win.\par \par \uc2 Workers also claim managers from other stores brought in to the Berkeley store have been giving misinformation to employees about unions.\par \par \uc2 REI\uc2  has denied claims of union opposition. It said managers from outside stores were brought in to support store functions and cover management time off. \uc2 REI\uc2  also claimed HR understaffing issues were resolved and they have no record of unaddressed complaints from the Berkeley store.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will fully support the petition process in Berkeley, including the right of every employee to vote for or against union representation,\u8221\'20\'1D said an \uc2 REI\uc2  spokesperson in an email.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 27 July 2022. Staff at the Amazon warehouse in Staten Island, New York, won their union election in April this year, not last year as an earlier version said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220727ei7r001e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
