\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Six staffers arrested after climate sit-in at \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 425 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 July 2022\par 14:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 On Monday, 17 people sat in the Senate majority leader\u8217\'20\'19s office to demand he reopen climate negotiations\par \par \uc2 Six staffers were reportedly arrested in Congress on Monday afternoon for staging a sit-in at Senate majority leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office and protesting about a lack of legislative action on the environment.\par \par \uc2 The congressional staffers and activists had started the demonstration earlier on Monday, with 17 staffers sitting in Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s office to demand that he reopen climate negotiations, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/saaaauuull/status/1551584941410230272?s=20&t=6fIIY-wq5KU-hr5GZ-gS1Q"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according}}}\uc2  to Saul Levin, a policy adviser for the progressive congresswoman Cori Bush.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, we Hill staffers are peacefully protesting Dem leaders INSIDE. To my knowledge, this has never been done,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 HAPPENING NOW: We\u8217\'20\'19re asking Senator Schumer to negotiate like this is the coldest summer of the rest of our lives (it is). {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wjXnHfTQqn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wjXnHfTQqn}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Saul (@saaaauuull) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/saaaauuull/status/1551584941410230272?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Some also protested outside the building.\par \par \uc2 Schumer, Senate majority leader, had been under pressure to negotiate a climate deal, especially after the supreme court struck down a key protection of the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But Schumer, and Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s, efforts to advance climate legislation have been thwarted largely because of the opposition of the Democratic West Virginia senator Joe Manchin, who has been called a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-condemned-us-climate-action"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 modern-day villain}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D for his ties to the fossil fuel industry and killing off the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/15/joe-manchin-climate-funding-tax-hikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 president\u8217\'20\'19s environmental proposals}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Later in the day the sit-in at Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s office seemed to turn more contentious.\par \par \uc2 A tweet posted by NBC News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JulesJester/status/1551616214937620480"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reporter Julia Jester}}}\uc2  features a short video purporting to show one of the staff members in handcuffs, explaining why the group jeopardized their careers to take the action.\par \par \uc2 The reporter asked the male staffer what they were demanding of the senior Democrat. He replied: \u8220\'20\'1Cto reopen negotiations on the climate reconciliation package... and pass climate legislation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Christian Hall, a congressional reporter for Punchbowl News, also tweeted that Philip Bennet, president of the Congressional Workers Union, had been taken away in handcuffs.\par \par \uc2 Philip Bennet, President of the Congressional Workers Union is among one of the arrested protesters. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JG1oNKgHbg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JG1oNKgHbg}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Christian Hall (@christianjhall) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/christianjhall/status/1551593439560622080?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 July 25, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The reporter asked why the group had chosen Schumer\u8217\'20\'19s office, and not that of Manchin. (Earlier on Monday, Manchin announced he had tested positive for Covid-19 and was working remotely.)\par \par \uc2 The staffer replied cryptically: \u8220\'20\'1CBecause there\u8217\'20\'19s always going to be a sheep that strays away from the herd.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220725ei7p00335\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
