\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  under fire over new documents revealed by \uc2 John Barilaro\uc2  New York trade role inquiry\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael McGowan \par \uc2 951 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 July 2022\par 07:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Files released by parliament show premier was sent brief about prior candidate\u8217\'20\'19s appointment following \u8216\'20\'18full recruitment process\u8217\'20\'19Get our free news app, morning email briefing and daily news podcast\par \par \uc2 The New South Wales premier, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/new-south-wales"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dominic Perrottet}}}\uc2 , was sent a brief noting that former senior public servant and businesswoman Jenny West was the \u8220\'20\'1Csuccessful candidate\u8221\'20\'1D for the New York trade job now at the centre of a major controversy.\par \par \uc2 Contained in a tranche of documents released to the parliament on Tuesday, the brief is identical to the one investment minister \uc2 Stuart Ayres\uc2  signed in August last year, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jul/07/liberal-minister-signed-off-on-alternative-candidate-to-ny-trade-job-later-given-to-john-barilaro-documents-reveal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed by Guardian Australia earlier this month}}}\uc2 , as well as that sent to then premier \uc2 Gladys Berejiklian\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Their release has seen Labor ramp up its attacks over former deputy premier \uc2 John Barilaro\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s appointment to the $500,000-a-year trade position, with the shadow treasurer, Daniel Mookhey, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is a strong case now for Mr Ayres and Mr Perrottet to answer for why they didn\u8217\'20\'19t mislead the parliament.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The new documents \u8211\'20\'13 released on Tuesday after Labor successfully pushed to have the parliament recalled from its winter break on Friday \u8211\'20\'13 also include a brief sent to Barilaro.\par \par \uc2 The briefs to Perrottet, Ayres and Barilaro note that after a \u8220\'20\'1Cfull recruitment process\u8221\'20\'1D, West had been identified as the successful candidate for the lucrative role.\par \par \uc2 The documents state the recruitment panel, headed by the Investment NSW chief executive, Amy Brown, had recommended her for the job.\par \par \uc2 While the brief to Perrottet is unsigned, emails released to the parliament show that on 13 August a department liaison officer inside Perrottet\u8217\'20\'19s office wrote to Investment NSW saying the brief was being returned as \u8220\'20\'1Cnoted\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The brief to Barilaro is also unsigned.\par \par \uc2 The briefs place further pressure on both Perrottet and Ayres, the deputy Liberal party leader, after both men previously told parliament that no suitable candidate for the New York trade job had been selected following the first round of recruitment.\par \par \uc2 During a press conference in South Korea, where he is currently on a trade trip, the premier reiterated previous comments that his parliamentary statement was based on information from the department.\par \par \uc2 He said neither he nor his chief of staff recalled receiving the briefing.\par \par \uc2 Perrottet also defended Ayres \u8211\'20\'13 who is set to join the premier on the next leg of his trade mission in India \u8211\'20\'13 saying he was \u8220\'20\'1Ca very strong minister in the NSW government and has been for a long period of time\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 When asked whether he still had confidence the hiring process was done at arm\u8217\'20\'19s length from government, Perottet said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know, and that\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19ve asked for an independent review into this getting this information.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a statement responding to Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s release, Ayres said the document \u8220\'20\'1Cnotes information provided by Investment NSW. It is not a brief which seeks a decision from me\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would also like to make clear that this brief does not represent the end of the recruitment process,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat could only be determined by the CEO of Investment NSW as this is public service appointment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is consistent with testimony provided by the Investment NSW CEO and general-counsel to the Public Accountability Committee and the information I provided to the Legislative Assembly during question time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, Labor\u8217\'20\'19s Mookhey said the documents were evidence Perrottet and Ayres were \u8220\'20\'1Cboth told Jenny West was the best person for the job\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a strong case now for Mr Ayres and Mr Perrottet to answer for why they didn\u8217\'20\'19t mislead parliament,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 While Mookhey stopped short of committing Labor to move a censure motion against the ministers, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CMr Ayres and \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  have made statements to the Legislative Assembly which are inaccurate, and I think you can expect the opposition will respond.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Guardian Australia first reported in June that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/21/john-barilaro-got-trade-job-after-senior-public-servant-had-already-been-offered-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York City trade role had been offered to West}}}\uc2  in August 2021. The parliamentary inquiry has been told the first round of recruitment was discontinued after a cabinet decision to make the position a ministerial appointment. However, that decision was later reversed and it returned to being a public service appointment, with the position being readvertised in December after Barilaro left politics, and his appointment announced in June.\par \par \uc2 Despite the release of some documents on Tuesday, Labor said it would push ahead with recalling parliament from its winter break on Friday because more than 100 documents subject to a parliamentary order were kept secret.\par \par \uc2 More than 130 pages of documents given to the upper house \u8211\'20\'13 including applicant CVs and selection panel reports \u8211\'20\'13 were marked \u8220\'20\'1Cprivileged\u8221\'20\'1D, meaning they can only be seen by MPs in the legislative council who cannot talk about them publicly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is public money,\u8221\'20\'1D Labor\u8217\'20\'19s deputy leader in the upper house, John Graham, said on Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CThe public deserves to know and it\u8217\'20\'19s in the public interest that these documents are removed from behind closed doors.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last week, Barilaro\u8217\'20\'19s former senior adviser Mark Connell provided an explosive submission to the inquiry, claiming his then boss told him he would get the state\u8217\'20\'19s California trade office moved across the country because {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jul/20/john-barilaro-inquiry-former-chief-of-staff-explosive-submission-new-york-trade-job"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he wanted the New York job \u8220\'20\'1Cwhen I get the fuck out of this place\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Barilaro described Connell\u8217\'20\'19s submission as \u8220\'20\'1Cfictitious\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The former deputy premier quit the trade role late last month, saying it was \u8220\'20\'1Cnow not tenable with the amount of media attention this appointment has gained\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said he \u8220\'20\'1Cmaintained that I followed the process and look forward to the results of the review\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220726ei7q0005m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
