\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We want to be able to survive\u8217\'20\'19: Atlantic City casino workers to strike over wages\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 921 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 June 2022\par 14:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Demand for a new union contract that raises wages to cover rising cost of living and to attract workers in understaffed departments\par \par \uc2 Like all casino towns, Atlantic City in New Jersey trades on a public image of get-rich-quick success where a little slice of luck can deliver the good life. But for thousands of workers who toil in the city\u8217\'20\'19s casinos, hotels, restaurants and shops, that image is in stark contrast to reality.\par \par \uc2 Iris Sanchez, a housekeeper at Caesars Hotel and Casino in Atlantic City since 1998, has been struggling with increases in rent, gas and food, which has made it even more difficult to care for her daughter with diabetes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s expensive. I barely make it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanchez. \u8220\'20\'1CI have to think about which bill to pay at the end of the month because I have to have the money either for the rent or for the bills and then I\u8217\'20\'19ll pay the other with the next check.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She makes $16.25 an hour and is pushing for a wage increase to account for the rising cost of living and to attract workers, as her department has been severely understaffed, which has contributed to increased workloads and a lot of overtime. Her hotel has eliminated daily room cleaning, so she is cleaning dirtier rooms, while rushing to keep up with checkout rooms as well.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are working six days a week and we\u8217\'20\'19re working overtime at least four of those days,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanchez. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to be compensated for being loyal to the company, and we deserve a raise and a better quality of life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/thousands-atlantic-city-casino-workers-002223095.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than 6,000 workers }}}\uc2  at five major casinos in Atlantic City are set to strike in demand of a new union contract that significantly raises wages for workers, who say they\u8217\'20\'19ve sacrificed pay in previous contracts and are struggling as the cost of living and inflation has significantly increased.\par \par \uc2 On 15 June, workers represented by \uc2 Unite Here\uc2  Local 54 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uniteherelocal54.org/atlantic-city-casino-workers-vote-96-yes-to-strike/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  voted }}}\uc2  96% in favor of authorizing a strike if a new union contract isn\u8217\'20\'19t reached by 1 July at Caesars, Harrah\u8217\'20\'19s, Tropicana, and the Borgata, and 3 July for Hard Rock, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/covid-health-9516ab9b07ee5fabecbf3509d30f50fe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former Trump Taj Mahal casino}}}\uc2 , after their previous contracts expired on 31 May without a new deal in place.\par \par \uc2 The unions are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UHLocal54/status/1540100813112197120?t=7x6o9jHL-BBaCbWo4acO7w&s=19"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 preparing}}}\uc2  for a strike as the casinos have yet to raise wages and negotiations continue. The city council of Atlantic City unanimously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pressofatlanticcity.com/news/local/atlantic-city-council-pushes-for-higher-wages-for-casino-workers-to-avert-strike/article_893e3722-f230-11ec-8087-7fc65efdc6e4.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed }}}\uc2  a resolution in support of workers and their campaign for higher wages and called on the casinos to negotiate a contract in good faith to avert a strike.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/business/atlantic-city-casinos-losses-potential-union-strike-20220625.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to the union}}}\uc2 , the Borgata could lose an estimated $1.6m a day if workers strike, and Caesars, Tropicana, and Harrah\u8217\'20\'19s could lose an additional $1m a day combined from a strike, hitting the casinos ahead of the Fourth of July weekend, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/business/atlantic-city-casinos-losses-potential-union-strike-20220625.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  historically}}}\uc2  one of the busiest times of the year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe really need to get some significant wages across the board. We sacrificed wages for a lot of years to secure our healthcare and pension,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jeff Payne, who has worked as a server in the Laurel Lounge at Caesars for 33 years. \u8220\'20\'1CCasinos are doing very well. They\u8217\'20\'19re making billions of dollars in profits, and they don\u8217\'20\'19t want to invest in the workers. It\u8217\'20\'19s a struggle at this point and everyone is having a really hard time with everything going up, and the company is unwilling to put any wages on the table.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uniteherelocal54.org/wp-content/uploads/L54-AC-Economics-Report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 union survey }}}\uc2  conducted earlier this year of 1,934 casino workers in Atlantic City found 61% of respondents reported struggling to pay rent or their mortgage at least once in the past year, 32% said they\u8217\'20\'19ve struggled to afford food, 37% for utilities, and 27% for transportation.\par \par \uc2 As of March 2022, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uniteherelocal54.org/wp-content/uploads/L54-AC-Economics-Report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 average wage}}}\uc2  for non-tipped casino workers was $15.81 an hour and $8.80 an hour for tipped workers, while the living wage for one adult with no children in Atlantic county is $18.83 an hour, according to the MIT living wage calculator.\par \par \uc2 Workers have claimed the low wages have contributed to staffing shortages in casinos, which has increased workloads for staff, while profits at their casinos in Atlantic City have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/covid-health-sports-earnings-12bac08165adfe1e5a212a8b6df5486d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surpassed}}}\uc2  pre-pandemic levels.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re making a lot of money and we just want to be able to live, to survive,\u8221\'20\'1D said Al Kare, a banquet server at Caesars for 20 years. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re working for two people because they won\u8217\'20\'19t staff because they\u8217\'20\'19re not hiring at decent wages. We are the backbone of the casinos. Without us, our smiles, our hard work, our sweat, these casinos don\u8217\'20\'19t survive.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re also pushing for casinos to get subcontracting under control, so casinos don\u8217\'20\'19t outsource more work in response to the wage increases workers are demanding.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are some job classifications where we have very few workers and as a result, you have to pick up that slack because that body is missing, or there\u8217\'20\'19s a call out because they\u8217\'20\'19re on overtime and being forced to be mandatory,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ruth Ann Joyce, a banquet bartender at Harrah\u8217\'20\'19s. \u8220\'20\'1CIt all comes back to economics. If we pay correctly, pay the way we should be paying, the workers will come.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The casinos did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220629ei6t001bc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
