\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Senior public servants thought \uc2 John Barilaro\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s New York trade job would need cabinet approval\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael McGowan \par \uc2 723 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2022\par 03:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 An inquiry into former NSW deputy premier \uc2 John Barilaro\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s appointment to a $500,000-a-year trade role in New York begins on WednesdayFollow our Australia news live blog for the latest updatesGet our free news app, morning email briefing and daily news podcast\par \par \uc2 Public servants inside Investment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/new-south-wales"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New South Wales}}}\uc2  believed that the New York City trade commissioner job to which former deputy premier \uc2 John Barilaro\uc2  was appointed needed to be approved by cabinet.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of today\u8217\'20\'19s public inquiry into Barilaro\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/25/john-barilaros-bite-of-the-big-apple-the-plum-new-york-posting-that-set-off-a-firestorm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appointment to the $500,000-a-year job}}}\uc2  that he created before leaving parliament last year, emails reveal that senior officials inside the department responsible for filling the position expected it to need cabinet signoff.\par \par \uc2 On 24 June last year, the agency\u8217\'20\'19s senior HR officer wrote in an email that \u8220\'20\'1Call\u8221\'20\'1D of the six trade commissioner jobs created by the government would need cabinet approval.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was agreed when the global expansion strategy was first approved I believe,\u8221\'20\'1D the official wrote.\par \par \uc2 Contained in a tranche of documents obtained under parliamentary order, the missive is significant because the government has insisted that Barilaro\u8217\'20\'19s appointment did not require cabinet approval.\par \par \uc2 While the premier, \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2 , has previously conceded two of the six postings \u8211\'20\'13 to London and Tokyo \u8211\'20\'13 went to cabinet for approval, he has insisted that was an \u8220\'20\'1Cerror\u8221\'20\'1D and that the postings were decided by the public service.\par \par \uc2 But senior government ministers have expressed frustration at not being informed of Barilaro\u8217\'20\'19s appointment before it was announced earlier this month, pointing out that much more junior government postings generally require cabinet signoff.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf in doubt, send it to cabinet,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/25/john-barilaros-bite-of-the-big-apple-the-plum-new-york-posting-that-set-off-a-firestorm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one minister previously told the Guardian}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Separate emails show that Barilaro had questioned whether the posts needed cabinet signoff. In August the chief executive of Investment NSW, Amy Brown, wrote in an email that the \u8220\'20\'1CDP\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 deputy premier \u8211\'20\'13 had asked for \u8220\'20\'1Cclarification\u8221\'20\'1D on the process.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a fair question, because Treasury initially set up an erroneous process where they had to go to Cabinet, which is completely inappropriate,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote.\par \par \uc2 The confusion surrounding the appointment will be central to a parliamentary inquiry due to begin on Wednesday. Brown, who premier \uc2 Dominic Perrottet\uc2  has insisted was the \u8220\'20\'1Cfinal decision maker\u8221\'20\'1D on the appointment, is slated to give evidence.\par \par \uc2 Aside from the lack of cabinet approval, the committee\u8217\'20\'19s questioning will focus on the fact the agency was requested to consider making the positions subject to ministerial approval.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has previously reported that Brown told the recruitment company hired to find candidates for the New York position to stop the search because the job would be handled \u8220\'20\'1Cas an internal matter\u8221\'20\'1D as a \u8220\'20\'1Cministerial appointment\u8221\'20\'1D. The decision was, Brown said at the time, \u8220\'20\'1Coutside of our control\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 While the position was eventually not filled via a ministerial appointment, the trail of documents show Investment NSW\u8217\'20\'19s general counsel did seek advice about legislation to allow the positions to be filled by the minister.\par \par \uc2 That advice, according to one email, came after the department had been \u8220\'20\'1Casked to consider \u8230\'20\'26 whether there is an option for ministerial appointments\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/guardian-australia-morning-mail/2014/jun/24/-sp-guardian-australias-morning-mail-subscribe-by-email?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up to receive an email with the top stories from Guardian Australia every morning}}}\par \par \uc2 The email was sent in September, and it\u8217\'20\'19s understood the cabinet meeting in which businessman Stephen Cartwright was appointed to an identical job in London also took place in September. Nine News has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/9NewsSyd/status/1540249977024380929"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously reported}}}\uc2  that Barilaro, while not opposing Cartwright\u8217\'20\'19s appointment, allegedly said during that cabinet meeting that the jobs \u8220\'20\'1Cshould be open to politicians\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  revealed on Monday that Barilaro also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/27/john-barilaro-approached-former-nsw-labor-leader-jodi-mckay-about-trade-role-in-india"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 personally approached former NSW Labor leader Jodi McKay}}}\uc2  about filling the trade commissioner role in India.\par \par \uc2 It comes after Perrottet said he had first been told that Barilaro was interested in the New York trade job in a \u8220\'20\'1Csocial setting\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday the premier confirmed for the first time that he was aware Barilaro had intended to apply for the job. While he said he could not recall when he found out, Perrottet said it was after Barilaro had quit parliament.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think in a social setting he may have said he was applying for a position, which was an independent process,\u8221\'20\'1D Perrottet said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220628ei6s002nk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
