\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18People are walking off the job\u8217\'20\'19: workers blame \uc2 American Red Cross\uc2  for US blood shortage\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 807 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 June 2022\par 09:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Employees say staff shortages and low pay are causing donors to leave before giving blood, amid delays over union contract\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American Red Cross\uc2 , which controls about 40% of the blood supply in the US, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.redcrossblood.org/donate-blood/how-to-donate/how-blood-donations-help/blood-needs-blood-supply.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared}}}\uc2  a national blood shortage in January, the worst shortage in over a decade.\par \par \uc2 The Red Cross emphasized decreasing blood donations as a driving factor for shortages, citing a 10% decline in the number of people donating blood during the pandemic. The shortage has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://doh.wa.gov/newsroom/eligible-donors-urged-give-blood-national-blood-shortage-continues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continued }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.centralwinews.com/tribunephonograph/2022/06/14/u-s-currently-in-critical-blood-shortage/?destination=star-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 across the US }}}\uc2  in recent months.\par \par \uc2 But workers at the organization say the shortage is being caused by widespread staffing issues. Low pay and understaffing are causing problems, and workers say they often have to turn away donors due to backed-up lines, and that management has not supported workers or donors enough to resolve these issues.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1gOeDXcO7QRHZ17Pog7upqpZALynxo_C2/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=104158420780404716651&rtpof=true&sd=true"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 document}}}\uc2  from a January meeting revealed that a Red Cross senior account manager, Joseph Shockley, told hospital representatives that labor and staffing issues have driven blood supply concerns, cautioning: \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t want to drive donors to places that are understaffed that turn donors away \u8211\'20\'13 that becomes frustrating to donors.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shockley did not respond to requests for comment and the Red Cross did not comment on the memo.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a blood shortage, it\u8217\'20\'19s a worker shortage,\u8221\'20\'1D said Darryl Ford, a collection technician at Red Cross in Warner Robins, Georgia for 23 years, and president of local union branch USW L254. \u8220\'20\'1CCovid proved a lot of things. People are not going to take anything any more and just because the Red Cross has that non-profit logo, people are not above it. More people are walking off the job than I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen in 20 years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said in his area in Georgia, he\u8217\'20\'19s seen several workers quit recently, including workers who have been with the group for years. Due to short staffing, he argued, many donors walk in to blood drives and leave because the line is backed up. Workers are often expected to drive long hours to blood drives, work those drives short-staffed, and drive long hours back.\par \par \uc2 About {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/red-cross-must-bargain-for-worker-union-pact-lawmakers-insist"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 3,000 workers}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afscme.org/blog/american-red-cross-workers-including-afscme-members-rally-for-fair-contract"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 represented}}}\uc2  by a coalition of labor unions at Red Cross have been pushing for a new union contract over the past several months to address issues with pay and staffing, and to protect their current healthcare plans.\par \par \uc2 The unions have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afscme.org/document/FDALetter41822.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  on the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to pressure the Red Cross to agree to a fair contract with the unions, citing high staff turnover rates around the US. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenonprofittimes.com/news/red-cross-union-workers-extend-acrimonious-contract-talks/#:~:text=%E2%80%9CFrontline%20%5BAmerican%20Red%20Cross%5D,making%20the%20staffing%20crisis%20worse.%E2%80%9D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Several unions}}}\uc2  have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afscme.org/blog/wisconsin-council-32-files-charge-against-american-red-cross"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused}}}\uc2  the organization of not negotiating in good faith amid long delays in scheduling bargaining sessions.\par \par \uc2 In May, 47 members of Congress {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.google.com/document/d/10AKW-SXH7Y3vjcTlvQV8dfUB1L-NuYv4FZA7Kd8gMcA/edit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed}}}\uc2  a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BernieSanders/status/1534650781567156227?s=20&t=YonGrZCKPzKP4xCI2GJEvg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  calling on the Red Cross to negotiate a fair contract with the unions.\par \par \uc2 Bobbie Terrell, a Red Cross collection specialist for 23 years in Illinois and president of AFSCME Local 2691, argued many current workers have stayed with the organization for healthcare. But Red Cross has proposed to cut healthcare plans for workers, which will worsen staffing issues, and that current workers are not receiving pay increases while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.simplyhired.com/search?q=american+red+cross"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sign-on bonuses}}}\uc2  are being offered to new employees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t have the staff or the donors to support the blood supply and we\u8217\'20\'19re really going to be short-staffed because there are going to be people leaving because of healthcare,\u8221\'20\'1D said Terrell. \u8220\'20\'1CThey need to pay people an appropriate amount for the work that they do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 American Red Cross\uc2  said the organization was continuing to bargain in good faith with the coalition of unions and cited that they came to an agreement with the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , which occurred shortly after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thenonprofittimes.com/news/teamsters-red-cross-reach-tentative-agreement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike threat}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile we experienced a national blood shortage just a couple of months ago, we currently have a sufficient supply of blood on the shelves to support patients in need. Additionally, we are proud to share that in the last quarter, our hiring rate has increased approximately 50% \u8211\'20\'13 allowing us to bring on more employees than ever before \u8211\'20\'13 stabilizing the workforce and ensuring we can meet the needs of patients,\u8221\'20\'1D said the spokesperson in an email.\par \par \uc2 Terrell, Ford and the union coalition claimed the Red Cross has not communicated an end to the blood shortage to their workforce and provided a photo of a flyer soliciting donors taken on 21 June outside a Red Cross site in Illinois, which cited the blood shortage.\par \par \uc2 Several Red Cross donation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/RepHanbidge/posts/pfbid02zmyC7xecywCauzvfeKTA4egtPpmr7LHTGHMPDUyvUv8jj1YE2xP1LE8eZt9Nr3uQl?__cft__[0]=AZWDA6qEXdXfqWO63hiRXoFpAvY67Fdah_lAZLnp29UAgqm4QCyW0wTOTlAsGHCiCMFCKHmTbZA4-zy9hdsCpode5qCkhFie0fGc8BPTHH-CTAI1jgxqLGaFNUseO5Rwysg&__tn__=%2CO%2CP-R"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 events }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/myvccu/posts/pfbid0GjJr8NgG5aNuxbCWJzNN2XfEw92G9MN7ECykL1YGMYJxy5rXksr25SASJpTCF6nBl?__cft__[0]=AZXcQxSvamLKTYGIhvJSoAuDsK-TFE5bI6vD5S40kr_suJ0W7n_1ITjMXZzJrbk0em9b-L3pc4DyZV_4PB5mbGj0RumdAowWYysgFTkoex2Z48jyKNBUi6Rkfsg7RbcBcgr6nBH4cl9n94cUCGpLJxbr&__tn__=%2CO%2CP-R"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 around the US}}}\uc2  in just {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/CamdenClarkMedicalCenter/photos/a.248532835240718/5231593360267949/?__cft__[0]=AZUfgHeTdhTmMGFqD4C57CGsvCXpbOCecAyWgHW0AV-eJMBvrZ7rhLSta9nkO_ter93KyCLOxgLid9XCAzaeyUfUy8MMckCqUvWCpTS9v135IEAFJZySyypEZSemSl4MeSjUvM3i9jHludvkiFCyx0iF&__tn__=%2CO%2CP-R"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent weeks }}}\uc2  also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/MedicalCityFortWorth/photos/a.211223598904127/6095134620512966/?__cft__[0]=AZX0VLsZIDupAQG8_ocCJqUoKCrkIItE1q8w0PilD4LbTmJXwzxzMSb8sga_vB6g_RbXaWR3XS_PjfNyDuc9mOrhap6oShZHeCIvlMPBSH6iTh1QJ3iWl7RRunJu1RwFkUh2pDi2k688Ns7DT8outI26&__tn__=%2CO%2CP-R"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cite }}}\uc2  a blood shortage.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the union coalition said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe issue is retention. Incumbent workers are still leaving for higher-paying jobs, and according to members, many new hires are also leaving over issues of staffing and inadequate training.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220627ei6r001e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
