\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Ex-\uc2 BP\uc2  executive lands $6.2m payout at US firm despite death of offshore worker\b0\par\par\uc2 Alex Lawson Energy correspondent \par \uc2 558 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 June 2022\par 16:56 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Andy Inglis\uc2  ran \uc2 BP\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s exploration and production division before leaving in wake of Deepwater Horizon disaster\par \par \uc2 The executive who oversaw \uc2 BP\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Deepwater Horizon disaster has landed a $6.2m (\u163\'00\'A35m) payout at his new employer despite the death of a worker on an offshore rig in the Gulf of Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Andy Inglis\uc2  ran \uc2 BP\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s exploration and production division before leaving in the wake of the spill in the Gulf of Mexico in 2010, one of the worst ever environmental disasters, in which 11 workers died.\par \par \uc2 Inglis has run oil and gas firm \uc2 Kosmos Energy\uc2 , which is listed in New York and London, since 2014. Shareholders this month approved Inglis\u8217\'20\'19s pay package, which includes a $1.5m bonus and $3.7m in stock awards.\par \par \uc2 Inglis has been handed the payout despite the death of a contractor on a drillship working for \uc2 Kosmos\uc2  in the Gulf of Mexico. An Allrig contractor died on the \uc2 Seadrill\uc2 -owned West Neptune ship in January 2021.\par \par \uc2 Kosmos\uc2  said the company had conducted an \u8220\'20\'1Cextensive investigation\u8221\'20\'1D after the fatality and held sessions to study what could be done to prevent the recurrence of a similar incident.\par \par \uc2 Executives at multinational commodities companies can see their pay docked if workers die on the job. This year the FTSE firms {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/may/18/shell-boss-faces-investor-rebellion-over-pay-package"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shell}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/glencore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Glencore}}}\uc2  cut the bonuses of their chief executives after fatalities.\par \par \uc2 Inglis\u8217\'20\'19s bonus, and those of his colleagues, would have been larger, but the fatality meant health and safety targets were missed. Several operational and financial key performance indicators were also missed, trimming the payout.\par \par \uc2 However, Lord Sikka, professor of accounting at the \uc2 University of Sheffield\uc2 , said Inglis should not have received any bonus. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CI think the bonus is wrong and shows how insensitive corporations are to the death of workers. The company\u8217\'20\'19s sustainability report acknowledges the incidence, but provides no information about consequences for his family and what the company has done to mitigate the tragedy for them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe report comes across as a PR exercise rather than any reflections on corporate ethics and responsibility.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Inglis had been tipped to succeed \uc2 Tony Hayward\uc2  as chief executive of \uc2 BP\uc2  until the tragic oil spill. He was ousted from \uc2 BP\uc2  in a boardroom overhaul designed to improve the company\u8217\'20\'19s image in America after the rig blowout.\par \par \uc2 Lord Browne, the former chief executive of \uc2 BP\uc2  who preceded \uc2 Tony Hayward\uc2 , last month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2022/may/28/lord-browne-the-man-who-went-from-bp-and-the-north-sea-to-net-zero]"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Observer}}}\uc2  that Deepwater Horizon had presented \u8220\'20\'1Can existential threat\u8221\'20\'1D to the future of \uc2 BP\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Inglis joined \uc2 Kosmos\uc2  in 2014 as chairman and chief executive from Petrofac, the oil services firm, and he has also sat on the board of the defence company \uc2 BAE Systems\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kosmos\uc2  is a $3.7bn oil and gas explorer headquartered in Dallas, Texas with operations off the coast of the US and west Africa.\par \par \uc2 In a letter to shareholders commenting on the last year, Inglis said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe rebuilt operational momentum across the portfolio with a return to drilling in Ghana, Equatorial Guinea and the Gulf of Mexico.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kosmos\uc2  has emerged from the last two years of the pandemic with a stronger business and an important role to play in supporting the energy transition and strengthening energy security.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kosmos\uc2  declined to comment on Inglis\u8217\'20\'19 bonus.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220617ei6h002h0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
