\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Feel the benefit: union workers receive far better pay and rights, Congress finds\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 528 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 June 2022\par 12:00 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Study shows unionized workers earn 10.2% more than non-union peers, amid wave of organizing at some of largest US employers\par \par \uc2 Workers represented by labor unions earn 10.2% higher wages than their non-union peers, have better benefits and collectively raise wages industry-wide, according to a report released by the House and Senate committees on Friday and first shared with the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden has pledged to be the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/02/joe-biden-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most pro-union president}}}\uc2  in generations, and the report outlining the economic benefits of union membership was released as his administration pushes for legislative and executive-action efforts to support workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights to organize.\par \par \uc2 According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jec.senate.gov/public/index.cfm/democrats/issue-briefs?ID=A608604E-AAF6-4867-A080-648B29198E24"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report, }}}\uc2  by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jec.senate.gov/public/index.cfm/about"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joint economic committee}}}\uc2  of Congress and the House education and labor committee, unionized workers are also 18.3% more likely to receive employer-sponsored health insurance, and employers pay 77.4% more per hour worked toward the cost of health insurance for unionized workers compared with non-unionized workers.\par \par \uc2 Labor unions have also contributed to narrowing racial and gender pay disparities; unionization correlates to pay premiums of 17.3% for Black workers, 23.1% for Latino workers and 14.7% for Asian workers, compared with 10.1% for white workers. Overall, female union workers receive 4.7% higher hourly wages than their non-union peers and in female dominated service industries, union workers are paid 52.1% more than non-union workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnions are the foundation of America\u8217\'20\'19s middle class,\u8221\'20\'1D said congressman \uc2 Don Beyer\uc2 , chair of the Joint Economic Committee. \u8220\'20\'1CFor too long, the wealthy have captured an increasing share of the economic pie. As this report makes clear, unions help address economic inequality and ensure workers actually see the benefits when the economy grows.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s drive to increase union membership comes amid a wave of organizing among workers at some of America\u8217\'20\'19s largest employers, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/apr/09/amazon-union-organization-staten-island"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/aug/28/starbucks-workers-buffalo-ny-organizing-union-first-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starbucks.}}}\par \par \uc2 But despite the recent uptick in organizing, union membership has declined markedly in recent decades, from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2014/02/20/for-american-unions-membership-trails-far-behind-public-support/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 34.8% }}}\uc2  of all US wage and salary workers in 1954 to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/pdf/union2.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10.3%}}}\uc2  in 2021. According to several studies the decline has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/unequalpower/publications/private-sector-unions-corporate-legal-erosion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contributed }}}\uc2  significantly to increasing wage inequality and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://insight.kellogg.northwestern.edu/article/wage-stagnation-in-america#:~:text=U.S.%20workers%20have%20grappled%20with,compared%20to%20overall%20economic%20productivity."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stagnation}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Corporate practices and legal changes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/unequalpower/publications/private-sector-unions-corporate-legal-erosion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  have also eroded}}}\uc2  workers\u8217\'20\'19 bargaining power, particularly from the 1970s, as employers increasingly attempted to break union organizing efforts and were issued only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/civil-monetary-penalties-for-labor-violations-are-woefully-insufficient-to-protect-workers/#:~:text=While%20the%20civil%20monetary%20penalties,Labor%20Relations%20Act%20(NLRA)."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weak penalties}}}\uc2  for violating labor laws.\par \par \uc2 The report cites the recent resurgence of the US labor movement, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/354455/approval-labor-unions-highest-point-1965.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strong public support}}}\uc2  for labor unions, as a call to action to improve wages and working conditions and support worker organizing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs chair of the education and labor committee, I am committed to addressing the decades of anti-worker attacks that have eroded workers\u8217\'20\'19 collective bargaining rights,\u8221\'20\'1D said education and labor committee chair congressman Bobby Scott.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith the release of this report, I once again call on the Senate to pass the Protecting the Right to Organize Act, which would take historic steps to strengthen workers\u8217\'20\'19 right to organize, rebuild our middle class, and improve the lives of workers and their families.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220610ei6a001p7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
