\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Morning mail: threatened species plans scrapped, Depp v Heard verdict, \uc2 Sheryl Sandberg\uc2  quits\b0\par\par\uc2 Tamara Howie \par \uc2 1,520 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 June 2022\par 21:32 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Thursday : Coalition scrapped recovery plans for 176 threatened animals, plants and habitat. Plus: jury finds in favour of Johnny Depp in defamation caseWant to get the morning mail to your email inbox every weekday? Sign up here !\par \par \uc2 Good morning. The fallout from the federal election continues, as the Liberal party mulls what went wrong and who\u8217\'20\'19s to blame, and the environment takes a final hit from the former environment minister.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn what sort of planet does the commonwealth think they don\u8217\'20\'19t need a recovery plan for a Tasmanian devil?\u8221\'20\'1D That\u8217\'20\'19s the question being asked by the \uc2 Wilderness Society\uc2  after the Coalition\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Sussan Ley{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/jun/02/coalition-scrapped-recovery-plans-for-176-threatened-species-and-habitats-in-one-of-its-final-acts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scrapped recovery plans }}}\uc2  designed to prevent the extinction of almost 180 threatened species and habitats as one of her final acts as environment minister. Last year, the Morrison government proposed removing the requirement for a legislated plan for 185 plants, animals and habitats, including several plans that were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2020/oct/19/australian-threatened-species-at-risk-due-to-government-inaction-over-backlog-of-recovery-plans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 years overdue}}}\uc2 . In March, Ley signed off on decisions to remove that requirement for 176 of the species and habitats. Ley made the decisions despite a government call for feedback receiving 6,701 responses, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/mar/17/most-of-australias-threatened-species-not-monitored-by-government-audit-finds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all disagreeing}}}\uc2  with the proposal.\par \par \uc2 After preselection chaos, the NSW Liberal party is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/02/disgruntled-nsw-liberals-lay-blame-in-wake-of-federal-election-loss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 looking to lay blame}}}\uc2  for the federal election loss. Party members are pointing fingers at the unwieldy, faction-riven state executive, at the former prime minister Scott Morrison and his \u8220\'20\'1Ccaptain\u8217\'20\'19s picks\u8221\'20\'1D, and at his delegate on the state executive, \uc2 Alex Hawke\uc2 , who had been widely blamed for holding up preselections by failing to make himself available for months to vet candidates. Some are also blaming Covid lockdowns, which interfered with the party\u8217\'20\'19s ability to hold branch plebiscites. Meanwhile, the new Labor government continues the changes, creating a climate super-department in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/01/anthony-albanese-to-create-climate-super-department-in-bureaucratic-shake-up"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bureaucratic shake-up}}}\uc2 . The Australian federal police will also be removed from the home affairs department.\par \par \uc2 The jury in the Johnny Depp-Amber Heard defamation trial has ruled in favor of Johnny Depp, finding that a \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  editorial which she wrote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/jun/01/johnny-depp-amber-heard-verdict-trial-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defamed her former husband}}}\uc2 . Heard won on one count of her countersuit, in which she demanded $100m and argued she was defamed by a Depp press agent who called her allegations \u8220\'20\'1Can abuse hoax\u8221\'20\'1D. Heard was awarded $2m, while Depp was awarded $15m. The verdict follows a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/jun/01/johnny-depp-v-amber-heard-trial-quotes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week trial}}}\uc2  that heard from dozens of witnesses and attracted enormous attention. Now, attention will turn to the aftermath, including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2022/jun/01/johnny-depp-amber-heard-court-verdict-career-prospects"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 possible repercussions for their careers}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , said Ukraine had given \u8220\'20\'1Cassurances\u8221\'20\'1D that it wuld not use long-range weapons systems {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/01/us-to-send-advanced-rocket-systems-to-ukraine-as-russia-tightens-grip-on-sievierodonetsk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provided by Washington }}}\uc2  against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/jun/01/russia-ukraine-war-biden-approves-medium-range-rocket-systems-to-bolster-ukraine-defences-live?page=with:block-629783328f08c28a9854a89e#block-629783328f08c28a9854a89e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 targets on Russian territory}}}\uc2 . Russia\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister, Sergei Lavrov, said the supply of the rocket systems to Ukraine increased the risk of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/jun/01/russia-ukraine-war-biden-approves-medium-range-rocket-systems-to-bolster-ukraine-defences-live?page=with:block-62977e638f084d9060b72c77#block-62977e638f084d9060b72c77"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cthird country\u8221\'20\'1D being dragged into the conflict.}}}\uc2  Meanwhile, Kyiv\u8217\'20\'19s forces are suffering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/jun/01/russia-ukraine-war-biden-approves-medium-range-rocket-systems-to-bolster-ukraine-defences-live?page=with:block-629785ab8f08c28a9854a8b5#block-629785ab8f08c28a9854a8b5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 up to 100 fatalities }}}\uc2  and 500 wounded every day.\par \par \uc2 Australia\par \par \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s energy market operator warned of potential gas supply shortages in southeastern states on Thursday due to a burst of cold weather. Australia\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/02/world-of-pain-warnings-of-gas-shortages-amid-soaring-power-prices-add-to-australias-energy-woes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 energy woes are mounting}}}\uc2 , as one of the largest generators issues a profit warning and more retailers turn away customers as wholesale power prices soar.\par \par \uc2 The former prime minister \uc2 Julia Gillard\uc2  says a Covid-led shift to remote working could render some female employees \u8220\'20\'1Cinvisible behind the screen\u8221\'20\'1D and has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/02/julia-gillard-says-covid-led-shift-to-remote-working-could-render-some-female-employees-invisible"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged bosses}}}\uc2  to ensure female employees working from home aren\u8217\'20\'19t overlooked for promotion.\par \par \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s new minister for republic, \uc2 Matt Thistlethwaite\uc2 , says the \u8220\'20\'1Ctwilight\u8221\'20\'1D of the Queen\u8217\'20\'19s reign is a chance \u8220\'20\'1Cto discuss what comes next for Australia\u8221\'20\'1D. He said the work done over the next three years would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/01/minister-republic-twilight-queen-reign-good-opportunity-next-for-australia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ensure the country was \u8220\'20\'1Cready to go}}}\uc2  in a second term of an Albanese government\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A queer woman who allegedly experienced a \u8220\'20\'1Ccoordinated\u8221\'20\'1D sexual assault by two men claims police told her she \u8220\'20\'1Cwasn\u8217\'20\'19t the kind of woman who gets assaulted\u8221\'20\'1D when she reported the incident. The woman\u8217\'20\'19s story is one of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/02/wrong-type-of-woman-queensland-taskforce-hears-of-police-disbelief-of-abuse-allegations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 300 submissions }}}\uc2  to Queensland\u8217\'20\'19s women\u8217\'20\'19s safety and justice taskforce.\par \par \uc2 The world\par \par \uc2 Sheryl Sandberg\uc2 , the chief operating officer of \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and its parent company \uc2 Meta\uc2 , has announced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/jun/01/sheryl-sandberg-facebook-chief-operating-officer-resigns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she will step down from her role}}}\uc2 . In her 14 years in the job she became one of the most powerful figures in tech and oversaw a company weathering a meteoric rise and multiple controversies .\par \par \uc2 A door used by the gunman to access the Robb elementary school in Texas, did not automatically lock after being closed by a teacher,\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/01/texas-school-shooting-propped-open-door-closed-teacher"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas state investigators say}}}\uc2 , contradicting investigators\u8217\'20\'19 earlier account in which they said the teacher had propped open door.\par \par \uc2 Scientists have discovered a \u8220\'20\'1Ccatastrophic\u8221\'20\'1D change in blood cell composition, which may reveal why people can suddenly become frail after reaching their 70s, raising the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2022/jun/01/research-may-reveal-why-people-can-suddenly-become-frail-in-their-70s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prospect of new therapies }}}\uc2  to slow the ageing process.\par \par \uc2 A white man who shot and killed two Indigenous hunters on a country road in Canada has been found guilty of murder and manslaughter in a case that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/01/canada-anthony-bilodeau-guilty-murder-indigenous-hunters-metis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laid bare racial tensions}}}\uc2  in the region.\par \par \uc2 Recommended reads\par \par \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s freshly minted prime minister, Anthony Albanese, has made a habit of casually dropping song lyrics into his public appearances. On Tuesday he quoted a line from songwriter \u8211\'20\'13 and committed socialist \u8211\'20\'13 Billy Bragg when announcing his first ministry. \u8220\'20\'1CJust because you\u8217\'20\'19re going forwards doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean I\u8217\'20\'19m going backwards,\u8221\'20\'1D Albanese said. While not as image-obsessed as his predecessor Scott Morrison, there\u8217\'20\'19s no denying that \u8220\'20\'1CDJ Albo\u8221\'20\'1D is part of the Albanese brand. So, what does DJ Albo\u8217\'20\'19s music taste {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2022/jun/02/from-billy-bragg-to-dj-albo-what-anthony-albaneses-music-taste-says-about-him"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tell us about him}}}\uc2  ?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe internet is basically the sun to me. I need it to live, but I know that spending all day in its glow will eventually kill me,\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2022/jun/02/lewis-hobba-the-10-funniest-things-i-have-ever-seen-on-the-internet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says comedian and Triple J host Lewis Hobba}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI get nervous when showing people things on the internet \u8211\'20\'13 there\u8217\'20\'19s a real shame in showing people something they\u8217\'20\'19ve already seen. People roll their eyes at you like you\u8217\'20\'19re the second guy to invent the wheel.\u8221\'20\'1D Despite the nerves, Hobba has shared online bits and pieces that make him laugh, including very specific impressions, chaotic nightclub photos and a quiz about a dragon.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of a career-spanning exhibition, Indigenous Australian artist Daniel Boyd tells us about his family story, \uc2 Black Lives Matter\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2022/jun/02/a-pirate-captain-cook-and-his-own-head-in-a-jar-the-subversive-satire-of-daniel-boyd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 why he is inspired }}}\uc2  by an Aboriginal warrior who took on the invading Britons. Boyd\u8217\'20\'19s work has a satirical streak that dates back to his university days, when he first saw a portrait of Captain James Cook, by the British artist John Webber, in the National Portrait Gallery. Boyd wanted to \u8220\'20\'1Cmake sense of the power this painting has on the Australian public\u8221\'20\'1D and, through his art, began to undermine the hero myth of British explorers.\par \par \uc2 Listen\par \par \uc2 In their first few days of leadership, opposition leader \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2  and deputy \uc2 David Littleproud\uc2  have begun to lay out a roadmap for the future of their parties, and what they will stand for as leaders. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/audio/2022/jun/02/how-will-peter-dutton-and-david-littleproud-reshape-the-coalition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 today\u8217\'20\'19s Full Story}}}\uc2 , rural and regional editor Gabrielle Chan and political editor Katharine Murphy discuss the careers of the new leaders, and how their decisions will shape the next parliament.\par \par \uc2 Full Story is Guardian Australia\u8217\'20\'19s daily news podcast. Subscribe for free on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://podcasts.apple.com/au/podcast/full-story/id1482061243"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Apple Podcasts}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://open.spotify.com/show/7GJod4EyoLywB1AW6zrSHh?si=mbMJnUPiSO2snfF0jNw7jw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Spotify}}}\uc2  or any other podcasting app.\par \par \uc2 Sport\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s men\u8217\'20\'19s football team have just played, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2022/jun/01/scotland-ukraine-world-cup-2022-semi-final-playoff-match-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and won}}}\uc2 , their first game since the invasion of their country by \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 . This World Cup {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2022/jun/01/scotland-v-ukraine-world-cup-2022-qualifying-playoff-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 qualifying play-off semi-final}}}\uc2  against Scotland was due to be played in March, but the conflict led to its postponement.\par \par \uc2 Eddie Jones has been handed a major triple injury boost before England\u8217\'20\'19s rugby union summer tour of Australia with the Exeter trio of Jack Nowell, Luke Cowan-Dickie and Jonny Hill all {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/jun/01/england-boost-for-australia-tour-with-nowell-and-cowan-dickie-available"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected to be available }}}\uc2  for selection.\par \par \uc2 Media roundup\par \par \uc2 The SMH {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.smh.com.au/world/asia/we-didn-t-know-there-was-an-election-sri-lankan-men-reveal-desperate-boat-journey-20220531-p5apyr.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 talks to 12 Sri Lankan men}}}\uc2  who were on a boat intercepted by border force, revealed on election day. They say they are not people smugglers and had no idea there was an Australian election. The Herald Sun reports offices in Melbourne\u8217\'20\'19s CBD remain {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heraldsun.com.au/news/victoria/melbourne-office-occupancy-still-less-than-half-of-its-precovid-baseline/news-story/3b3a870ff11ba3a1fdde2506d6d59b11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less than half full}}}\uc2 , despite Covid restrictions lifting months ago. And the \uc2 Origin Energy\uc2  CEO has called for action to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afr.com/companies/energy/get-coal-power-plants-working-again-origin-ceo-20220601-p5aqbg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 get troubled coal-powered generators working agin}}}\uc2 , according to the AFR.\par \par \uc2 And if you\u8217\'20\'19ve read this far \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Have you been following #Swedengate? A Reddit post said Swedes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2022/jun/01/its-a-scandi-scandal-why-has-social-media-turned-on-sweden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 don\u8217\'20\'19t feed their children\u8217\'20\'19s playmates}}}\uc2  when they visit. But why \u8211\'20\'13 and why has it caused an uproar?\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 If you would like to receive the Guardian Australia morning mail to your email inbox every weekday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/guardian-australia-morning-mail/2014/jun/24/-sp-guardian-australias-morning-mail-subscribe-by-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sign up here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Discover Australian Weekend\par \par \uc2 Every Saturday at 6am, enjoy early access to the best journalism planned for the weekend in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/ng-interactive/2021/mar/17/make-sense-of-the-week-with-australia-weekend"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one elegant app}}}\uc2 , plus a curated selection of the week\u8217\'20\'19s news and analysis from Australia and the world.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220601ei61003ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
