\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 If everyone\u8217\'20\'19s working from home, why is commercial office space booming?\b0\par\par\uc2 Gene Marks \par \uc2 890 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 May 2022\par 09:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Not everyone is going to be working from home in the months to come. They\u8217\'20\'19re coming back to the office\par \par \uc2 Many people loved working from home during the pandemic. They got to spend more time with their families, adopted more pets, enjoyed the magic of delivery services, binged \uc2 Netflix\uc2 , swapped their suits for sweats and even started an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/nov/21/startups-2020-record-year-for-new-businesses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unprecedented number}}}\uc2  of businesses. All these reasons \u8211\'20\'13 and plenty of others \u8211\'20\'13 are behind why so many workers want to continue doing the same, even as we try to put Covid in the rearview mirror.\par \par \uc2 For those employees, here\u8217\'20\'19s a warning: prepare for reality. Employers are planning to have you back in the office.\par \par \uc2 Why else would \uc2 Facebook\uc2  lease another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-04-12/facebook-adding-manhattan-office-space-in-latest-nyc-expansion?c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 300,000 sq feet}}}\uc2  of office space in New York City to add to its already 3m sq feet occupied? Why would \uc2 Google\uc2  be spending {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/21/nyregion/google-buys-building-hudson-square.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $2.1bn}}}\uc2  on a Manhattan office building and expand its \u8220\'20\'1Csprawling campus\u8221\'20\'1D in the city to house its more than 12,000 employees? These are tech companies with businesses built on the cloud \u8230\'20\'26 so why expand offices?\par \par \uc2 And why would Manhattan\u8217\'20\'19s commercial real estate market be \u8220\'20\'1Crebounding\u8221\'20\'1D with CRBE, which tracks these sorts of things, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2022/04/10/manhattan-commercial-leasing-activity-rises-100-in-q1-from-last-year/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reporting}}}\uc2  that leasing activity rose 100% year over year as of 31 March? \u8220\'20\'1CWe just hit 95% occupancy, which is the highest occupancy number in the history of the building,\u8221\'20\'1D gushed one {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/newyork/news/experts-are-optimistic-commercial-real-estate-in-new-york-city-is-rebounding/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York City landlord}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This is not just a New York City thing, either.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.greenvillebusinessmag.com/2022/04/11/397128/charleston-s-bustling-commercial-real-estate-market-being-driven-by-post-pandemic-habits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Charleston, South Carolina}}}\uc2 , commercial vacancy rates are below 2% and almost 10m sq feet of industrial space is under construction. In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jaxdailyrecord.com/article/commercial-real-estate-demand-growth-should-help-keep-occupancy-and-rents-growing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jacksonville, Florida}}}\uc2 , 2021 was a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat year\u8221\'20\'1D for commercial real estate investors, with all product types posting increases in market rent, occupancy and interest from buyers. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/local/nw-arkansas/2022/04/06/skyline-report-commercial-real-estate-tight-but-strong"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Northwest Arkansas}}}\uc2  commercial real estate has its lowest vacancy rate since 2005. In Philadelphia, Baltimore, Santa Clara and Chicago, there\u8217\'20\'19s a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wealthmanagement.com/development/post-pandemic-boom-mixed-use-mega-projects-underway"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post-pandemic \u8220\'20\'1Cboom\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  in mixed-use commercial and residential properties under development. Developers in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kwqc.com/2022/04/24/booming-commercial-real-estate-market-quad-cities/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Iowa}}}\uc2  say that industrial spaces \u8220\'20\'1Ccannot be built fast enough\u8221\'20\'1D. Office vacancy rates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://journal.firsttuesday.us/socal-commercial-real-estate-results-are-in/83097/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continue to decline}}}\uc2  in San Diego, Los Angeles and Orange county, California.\par \par \uc2 If everyone\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cworking from home\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 as we hear again and again in the media \u8211\'20\'13 why is the commercial office space market booming? Yes, there\u8217\'20\'19s more demand for warehousing thanks to all those \uc2 Amazon\uc2  orders. But it\u8217\'20\'19s also because of something else: everyone is not going to be working from home in the months to come. They\u8217\'20\'19re coming back to the office.\par \par \uc2 Sure, the big companies are still slow to bring their employees back. Larger organizations from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hubblehq.com/blog/famous-companies-workplace-strategies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Goldman Sachs to KPMG}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 worried about bad PR and potential lawsuits \u8211\'20\'13 are tentatively allowing employees to determine their own arrangements. But this is quickly changing. More than half of corporate leaders want their people back in the office five days a week, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2022/03/18/50percent-of-companies-want-workers-back-in-office-5-days-a-week.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new study}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2022/04/12/70percent-of-interns-view-remote-work-negatively-study-finds.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Even GenZ-ers}}}\uc2  view remote working negatively!\par \par \uc2 So will these workers return? They\u8217\'20\'19re not going to have a choice.\par \par \uc2 We know that many employees are reluctant to come back to the office. Just this past week, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fortune.com/2022/05/02/apple-workers-unhappy-return-to-the-office-hybrid-work-pandemic/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study found}}}\uc2  that more than half of \uc2 Apple\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s workforce would like to quit their jobs because they prefer working from home. Other studies \u8211\'20\'13 like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tech.co/news/remote-workers-optimistic-in-office-employees"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this one}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/jobs/remote-working-new-normal-82-employees-prefer-working-from-home-study/articleshow/89201519.cms?from=mdr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this one}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 have shown that workers overwhelmingly prefer to keep working from their homes in lieu of commuting. Who can blame them?\par \par \uc2 But as much as employees want to work from home all the time, that\u8217\'20\'19s just not going to happen. The reality is that workers at the nation\u8217\'20\'19s small businesses \u8211\'20\'13 who employ about half of our workforce \u8211\'20\'13 have been back to the office for a while now. When I visit my clients \u8211\'20\'13 who are almost all small to midsized firms \u8211\'20\'13 their employees are at their desks. If you don\u8217\'20\'19t believe me, take a drive around your town\u8217\'20\'19s suburbs and look at the parking lots.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no question that work-from-home arrangements are now a core benefit that businesses must provide. My best clients are re-addressing their work cultures and doing their best to offer as much flexibility for their employees as they can allow. But there will be a limit. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know any who are going fully virtual and very, very few that are allowing their employees to work remotely for more than two days a week.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s because employers know that real work gets done when teams can be together, face-to-face, and collaborate, innovate and yes, even socialize. They also know that working from home can be difficult for some, cause loneliness and depression in others and also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2020/nov/19/small-business-startups-corporate-employees-pandemic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provide opportunities}}}\uc2  to avoid the work they\u8217\'20\'19re actually being paid for in lieu of running their side-gigs.\par \par \uc2 Working from home is here to stay. But \u8211\'20\'13 judging from what we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing in commercial real estate \u8211\'20\'13 companies are expanding, not abandoning, their offices. Many employers are doing their best to help transition their employees back. But in the end, this is business. And business gets done in a workplace, which means coming into the office \u8211\'20\'13 at least most of the time \u8211\'20\'13 is a reality that workers are going to have to face.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220508ei58000m9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
