\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Airport workers ramp up pressure for a living wage and union rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 756 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2022\par 09:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 From baggage handlers to wheelchair attendants, jobs \u8211\'20\'13 often outsourced \u8211\'20\'13 offer low pay, few benefits and vary wildly by city\par \par \uc2 Larry Allen has worked in various jobs at Dallas Fort Worth international airport for over 40 years.\par \par \uc2 Before the pandemic, Allen worked as a baggage handler, making just over $2 an hour and relying on tips to get by. When Covid-19 hit the US, Allen was told not to come back into work and wasn\u8217\'20\'19t recalled until one year later, when he took a position as a wheelchair agent.\par \par \uc2 He now makes only $8 an hour, plus tips, but those tips aren\u8217\'20\'19t guaranteed and can vary widely and he relies on social security benefits and Medicare. In his late 60s, Allen walks a few miles every day at work, and at his age worries about the physical toll working in the airport has taken on his body and his ability to eventually retire comfortably.\par \par \uc2 He is pushing to organize a union among his co-workers at the airport to improve wages, benefits and working conditions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need more money and more respect for the work we do. Eight dollars an hour is just not enough,\u8221\'20\'1D said Allen. \u8220\'20\'1CA union is an advantage, to get proper wage and insurance so if you get sick, you\u8217\'20\'19ll have some medical coverage, and if something happens, you\u8217\'20\'19ll have somebody to represent you and back you up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Allen is one of many airport workers around the US who took part in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://action.airportworkersunited.org/a/march30"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protest actions}}}\uc2  last month to pressure government officials at local, state and federal levels, and the CEOs of large airlines, including United, Delta and \uc2 American Airlines\uc2 , to sign on to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://act.seiu.org/a/goodairports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Good Airports pledge}}}\uc2 , committing to ensuring airport workers are paid living wages, provided affordable healthcare and have the right to organize a union.\par \par \uc2 The actions were part of a campaign led by the \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2  (\uc2 SEIU\uc2 ) for airport workers to bargain through a union for improved pay, working conditions, healthcare and sick leave.\par \par \uc2 Contracted workers, including baggage handlers, cabin cleaners, security guards, wheelchair attendants and janitorial staff participated in actions at \uc2 United Airlines\uc2  and \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  headquarters and airports in Atlanta, Boston, Philadelphia, New York City, Miami, Houston, San Francisco, Los Angeles, Seattle, Minneapolis, Orlando, Tampa, Fort Lauderdale, Washington DC, Portland, Newark, Chicago. and Denver. New union organizing efforts {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seiu.org/2022/03/airport-workers-in-20-cities-take-demands-to-top-us-airline-ceos-hold-national-day-of-action"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  were launched}}}\uc2  in Phoenix, Dallas and Charlotte.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m only paid $12 an hour. I work a lot of hours and some days I work so late that I just sleep over at the airport. I can\u8217\'20\'19t afford a car, rent and to send money home to my family in Sudan,\u8221\'20\'1D said Omer Hussein, a wheelchair attendant servicing \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  at Dallas Fort Worth international airport, in a press release on the actions. \u8220\'20\'1CI like working with passengers, but I\u8217\'20\'19m so tired all the time. That won\u8217\'20\'19t fly any longer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Airline contractors have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marketplace.org/2021/07/14/as-air-travel-soars-airline-contract-jobs-struggle-to-be-filled/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  difficulties in staffing positions as air travel demand has continued to improve toward pre-pandemic levels. Airline corporations have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cwa-union.org/AirlineOutsourcing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasingly outsourced }}}\uc2  work to contractors in recent decades, which often pay workers low wages with few or no benefits.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 SEIU\uc2  cited {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seiu.org/2022/03/airport-workers-in-20-cities-take-demands-to-top-us-airline-ceos-hold-national-day-of-action"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  data}}}\uc2  on the demographics of contracted airport workers in the US, revealing that 64% are people of color and are paid 42% less on average than their white peers in the air transportation industry.\par \par \uc2 Mary Kay Henry\uc2 , president of the \uc2 SEIU\uc2 , said workers were speaking up to hold airlines accountable because they are paid from the profits of these companies through contractors. She characterized the actions as part of a historic uprising of workers around the US demanding a voice on the job through a union and to be respected, protected and paid what they are worth.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re speaking up to say they\u8217\'20\'19re fed up with business as usual, because why should a worker in Chicago who drops a passenger off in a wheelchair get paid $18 an hour while the worker in Dallas who picks them up upon arrival gets paid only $8 an hour? Where your firm or the job you do are should not determine whether you support your family and can take care of yourself when you\u8217\'20\'19re sick or have a voice on the job,\u8221\'20\'1D said Henry. \u8220\'20\'1CThe major airlines can change the system of these jobs that used to be middle-class jobs with benefits that people could raise their families on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220408ei480018j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
