\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Union chief vows to pressure \uc2 Amazon\uc2  after historic New York vote\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 999 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2022\par 12:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien says the e-commerce company has \u8216\'20\'18total disrespect\u8217\'20\'19 for its workers\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 new president has pledged his powerful union will step up the pressure on \uc2 Amazon\uc2  and mount its own efforts to unionize the company after workers in New York {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/apr/01/amazon-union-groups-see-hope-workers-vote-alabama-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to form the company\u8217\'20\'19s first US union}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an interview with the Guardian Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said it was vital to organize \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , asserting that the e-commerce company has \u8220\'20\'1Ctotal disrespect\u8221\'20\'1D for its workers and was putting downward pressure on standards for unionized warehouse workers and truck drivers across the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have an employer like \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2  taking a joyride into space, and he bangs on his workers to be able to fund his trip,\u8221\'20\'1D said O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, who was inaugurated as \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  president on 22 March. He asserted that \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers would benefit greatly from joining the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , saying that \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s drivers and warehouse workers are treated and paid considerably worse than their unionized counterparts at other companies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re awful, they\u8217\'20\'19re disrespectful the way they treat their employees,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said of \uc2 Amazon\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Friday, a final vote count showed that \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers in Staten Island {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/apr/01/amazon-union-groups-see-hope-workers-vote-alabama-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to unionize}}}\uc2 , 2,654 for a union, 2,131 against. Another vote to organize workers in Alabama hangs in the balance. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  beat off the union drive by 118 votes but the final tally is awaiting a review of 416 challenged ballots.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said he applauds any organization that seeks to take on \uc2 Amazon\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CI commend anybody who tries to take on a schoolyard bully like \uc2 Amazon\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Retail, Wholesale and Department Store Union is seeking to unionize an \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse in Bessemer, Alabama, while a new, independent union, the Amazon Labor Union, was behind the organizing at two \uc2 Amazon\uc2  facilities on Staten Island.\par \par \uc2 You have an employer like \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2  taking a joyride into space, and he bangs on his workers to be able to fund his trip\par \par \uc2 Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said that no union is better positioned than the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  to organize \uc2 Amazon\uc2  because his 1.3-million-member union has decades of experience in unionizing and winning good contracts for warehouse workers and truck drivers. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the only union that has the proven track record of organizing workers in these industries,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said.\par \par \uc2 He said the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  needed to organize \uc2 Amazon\uc2  as an obligation to \u8220\'20\'1Cour members\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cour largest employers\u8221\'20\'1D, most notably \uc2 United Parcel Service\uc2  and DHL. Concerned that \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lower pay is undercutting Teamster employers and Teamster contracts, O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said he didn\u8217\'20\'19t want \uc2 Amazon\uc2  to threaten the livelihood of \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  or \u8220\'20\'1Cdiminish the standards established by collective bargaining agreements\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to organize \uc2 Amazon\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to have a plan in place. We have to execute that plan and not be scared to change that plan if it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t work at times. Even a world champion team doesn\u8217\'20\'19t win all the time. Hopefully we will have a favorable win-to-loss ratio.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Before winning a five-year term as \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 president, O\u8217\'20\'19Brien headed a large \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  local in the Boston area for 15 years. He succeeded \uc2 James P Hoffa\uc2 , who stepped down after 23 years as \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have the best resources out there, not just financially\u8221\'20\'1D to unionize \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have the ability to utilize our members who work in the industry, who know the benefits of working under a collective bargaining agreement and having dignity and respect in the workplace.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a lot of work to do,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a plan to focus on the big metro cities,\u8221\'20\'1D where he said the likelihood of winning unionization elections would be greatest. He said that the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  would mount \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-traditional campaigns\u8221\'20\'1D that include up lining politicians\u8217\'20\'19 support and extensive community support behind unionization. He stressed the importance of worker-to-worker organizing: \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to utilize our best organizers: our worker members who work in these industries.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  officials say their company\u8217\'20\'19s pay levels are competitive \u8211\'20\'13 $18 for a full-time entry-level worker in Staten Island and nearly $16 in Alabama. The company notes that its benefits, including health coverage, begin for full-time workers the day they join the company.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  officials have repeatedly said they are committed to maintaining an environment where its employees can thrive and feel appreciated and respected.\par \par \uc2 News of the Staten Island victory comes as union activity is experiencing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/mar/16/us-union-victories-wave-labor-strategists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resurgence in the US}}}\uc2 . Joe Biden has positioned himself as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/02/joe-biden-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most pro-union president}}}\uc2  in generations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Biden administration has done a great job for unions right out of the gate,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said. \u8220\'20\'1CAn administration that\u8217\'20\'19s not afraid to endorse unions is great.\u8221\'20\'1D He praised, in particular, a 2021 law that Biden backed that helped secure the pensions of millions of union members and retirees, including many \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  whose pension plans were seriously underfunded.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  and other unions need to do a far better job explaining to Americans how unions lift workers and the nation as a whole. He said many Americans view the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  favorably despite the movie The Irishman about scandals inside the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  a half-century ago. \u8220\'20\'1CDuring the worst pandemic we\u8217\'20\'19ll ever face people saw that we delivered packages, did trash pick-ups, did food and grocery deliveries,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve proven our worth providing goods and services to keep this country moving.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He talked at length about the importance of holding politicians accountable, especially when they fail to back workers and unions. \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t remember people\u8217\'20\'19s birthdays. But I can remember the last person that screwed me. That\u8217\'20\'19s how we\u8217\'20\'19re going to deal with those politicians who vote against us. We\u8217\'20\'19ll run people against you. We\u8217\'20\'19ll campaign against you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220402ei420015q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
