\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US graduate students protest against low pay while universities profit from their work\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,217 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 March 2022\par 14:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Student workers often earn \u8216\'20\'18below the minimum living wage\u8217\'20\'19 for helping teach courses and assisting with research\par \par \uc2 Thousands of graduate student workers around the US at private and public universities have gone on strike over the past few years, from Ivy League institutions like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thecrimson.com/article/2021/10/27/hgsu-second-strike-explained/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harvard University}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/dec/09/columbia-university-student-worker-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Columbia University}}}\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/feb/28/university-of-california-student-strike-fired"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 public state universities in California}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Graduate workers at even more colleges have organized unions in spite of staunch opposition from their administrations. Among the most pressing unifying themes among graduate student workers organizing unions and holding protest actions and strikes is the low pay, an issue plaguing graduate student workers around the US.\par \par \uc2 In the US, graduate workers take on jobs such as helping teach courses, assisting with research projects and performing often vital clerical tasks that help run academic institutions.\par \par \uc2 In Indiana, graduate workers at \uc2 Indiana University Bloomington\uc2  are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.indianagradworkers.org/strike-faq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 currently considering a strike}}}\uc2  over their university\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.idsnews.com/article/2022/02/iu-graduate-workers-continue-fighting-for-unionization-despite-tough-legal-environment-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refusal to negotiate with their union}}}\uc2  over ending fees charged to graduate workers and paying them a living wage.\par \par \uc2 Zara Anwarzai, a PhD candidate in philosophy and cognitive science at \uc2 Indiana University Bloomington\uc2  for four years, receives about $20,000 a year in pay from the university, and barely makes ends meet without working a side job, even as she shares a tiny one-bedroom apartment with her partner, who is also a graduate worker.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s often the case that we pay our monthly bills late so that we can make it until the next check,\u8221\'20\'1D said Anwarzai.\par \par \uc2 She has struggled with chronic back pain and can\u8217\'20\'19t afford the physical therapy her doctor has recommended for it. She\u8217\'20\'19s often delayed filling prescription medications because she couldn\u8217\'20\'19t afford the copay for it. When taking on side jobs either within or outside the university, she\u8217\'20\'19s worked as much as nearly 18 hours with few breaks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to stop spreading the \u8216\'20\'18I get paid to study!\u8217\'20\'19 narrative of graduate school,\u8221\'20\'1D added Anwarzai. \u8220\'20\'1CAs you go through a program, you realize to what extent your work in your departments and the university have benefited them . They need your labor as a teacher and researcher, they need you as someone who takes on unpaid service roles, and they need your academic and professional reputation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For international students, they legally cannot work additional jobs while working as a graduate student worker. Simon Luo, a PhD candidate in political science at \uc2 Indiana University Bloomington\uc2  and international graduate worker, is paid just $19,000 a year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is thousands of dollars below the minimum living wage in Bloomington, Indiana. I\u8217\'20\'19m constantly unable to make ends meet,\u8221\'20\'1D said Luo. \u8220\'20\'1CNot being able to support myself financially means constantly confronting the financial anxiety brought by low income.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Salaries for graduate student workers vary widely around the US. In January 2022, \uc2 Princeton University\uc2  announced raises for graduate worker stipends of 25% to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nj.com/education/2022/01/princeton-announces-25-increase-in-graduate-student-stipends.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about $40,000 annually}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Brown University\uc2  recently raised base annual stipends to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brown.edu/about/administration/human-resources/sites/human-resources/files/Brown%20SUGSE%20Final%20Agreement_061520.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 over $42,000 annually}}}\uc2 , while many colleges and universities pay stipends of far {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.phdstipends.com/results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less than $20,000 annually}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Pay can often vary for graduate student workers depending on academic departments and alternative sources of funding and grants. This pay has remained low at universities and colleges around the US, despite university endowments {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bizjournals.com/bizjournals/news/2022/02/24/university-endowments-2021-returns.html#:~:text=University%20endowments%20soar%20in%20fiscal%202021%20with%2031%25%20average%20returns,-Email&text=College%20and%20university%20endowments%20generated,posted%20average%20returns%20of%201.8%25."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 soaring}}}\uc2  in 2021, with an average return of nearly 31%, the highest average returns since 1983. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.insidehighered.com/news/2022/02/18/college-endowments-boomed-fiscal-year-2021-study-shows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 About 19%}}}\uc2  of colleges and universities that reported endowment returns in 2021 had endowments worth more than $1bn each.\par \par \uc2 At the \uc2 University at Buffalo\uc2  in New York, pay for some graduate workers can be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ubspectrum.com/article/2022/02/graduate-student-union-petitions-president-tripathi-for-higher-minimum-stipend-fee-elimination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as low as $10,500 annually}}}\uc2 , noted Lawrence Mullen, a PhD student worker in the English department at the \uc2 University at Buffalo\uc2  and president of UB graduate student employees union. He cited an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1ZmB1VgQlNbZPbzpsNWkbhlUtl94vqvQsegzXnpRXxJ8/edit#responses"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  internal survey}}}\uc2  of graduate workers at UB conducted by the union, which found around 20% of graduate workers at the school were making less than $15,000 annually.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey are paying our graduate graduate workers less than a living wage and in some cases, a third of what is the living wage in Erie county, which, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/press/updated-family-budget-calculator-provides-data-on-the-cost-of-living-in-every-county-and-major-metropolitan-area/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Economic Policy Institute}}}\uc2 , is about $35,000,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mullen. \u8220\'20\'1CAt UB, we have a food bank, and last semester, fall 2021, 80% of the people who used that food bank were graduate students.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 Stony Brook University\uc2  in New York, graduate workers are currently organizing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://stonybrookgradschool.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a living wage campaign }}}\uc2  to demand pay increases for graduate workers, with current base stipends set at $22,500 annually. The union also reported survey findings of graduate student workers reporting issues in affording rent and the ongoing financial stress induced by low pay with the high cost of living in Suffolk county, New York.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe teachers and the instructors of these courses are having a difficult time just getting by. Racking up credit card debt, not being able to repair their car, selling blood plasma, picking up side jobs, doing sex work on the side, just for the purpose of supporting themselves,\u8221\'20\'1D said John Klecker, a graduate student worker in chemistry at Stony Brook.\par \par \uc2 Low pay is emerging as a more pressing issue for graduate workers who often live in cities with high costs of living, which are currently soaring with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/16/renters-rent-increases-us-lease#:~:text=According%20to%20an%20analysis%20conducted,in%20more%20than%20two%20years."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 soaring rents}}}\uc2  and spikes in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://time.com/nextadvisor/in-the-news/rising-inflation-rising-prices-how-to-plan/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  prices of basic necessities}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Preston Stone, a graduate worker in the English department at the \uc2 University of Miami\uc2 , makes about $24,000 a year. Despite working through summers, he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t receive any pay for three months between spring and fall semesters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany people, because of the increase in rent without increasing stipends, have decided to not continue graduate studies. They\u8217\'20\'19ve decided to go back home or transfer to a different university,\u8221\'20\'1D said Stone.\par \par \uc2 At the \uc2 University of Florida\uc2 , graduate workers\u8217\'20\'19 starting pay {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://psych.ufl.edu/behavioral-and-cognitive-neuroscience/graduate-information/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is about $19,000 annually}}}\uc2  for nine months out of the year, though individuals require an income of at least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reports.nlihc.org/oor/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $32,200 annually}}}\uc2  to afford a studio apartment in the area in 2021.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ufgau.org/blog/stipend-survey-results-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey}}}\uc2  conducted by \uc2 UF\uc2  Graduate Assistants United of more than 1,000 graduate workers at \uc2 UF\uc2  found significant proportions of graduate workers struggling to make ends meet, relying on local food banks, and unable to afford medical care on the pay from the university. The union is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ufgau.org/blog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 currently pushing }}}\uc2  for significant wage increases in new union contract negotiations with the \uc2 University of Florida\uc2 , as the school has an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uff.ufl.edu/your-impact/for-uf-another-year-of-record-breaking-generosity/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endowment}}}\uc2  of more than $2.2bn and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.ufl.edu/2021/08/research-awards-/#:~:text=Podcast-,University%20of%20Florida%20faculty%20earn%20%24861%20million%20in%20research%20awards,challenges%20presented%20by%20the%20pandemic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  received $861m}}}\uc2  in research awards in 2021, research in which graduate workers are heavily involved.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGraduate students\u8217\'20\'19 work is the pillar upon which research projects are built. These are the very same projects that brought almost $900m in funding and for which the \uc2 University of Florida\uc2  makes prideful statements on social media. Yet at the same time, the university publicly rejected the union\u8217\'20\'19s bargaining package, on the grounds of being unable to find the money to pay graduate students a living wage,\u8221\'20\'1D said Konstantina Sokratous an international graduate student worker in behavioral and cognitive neuroscience at the \uc2 University of Florida\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese universities make a lot of profit off of graduate students, while being apathetic about the fact that these human beings struggle to feed themselves every single day,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220330ei3u001ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
