\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Hundreds of \uc2 Chevron\uc2  workers at California refinery go on strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Dani Anguiano and agencies \par \uc2 920 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2022\par 10:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Chevron\uc2  says it will bring trained workers to the plant in Richmond and continue operations as normal\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of \uc2 Chevron\uc2  workers in California went on strike Monday after the company and the \uc2 United Steelworkers\uc2  union failed to reach a contract agreement.\par \par \uc2 More than 500 workers at a refinery producing gasoline, diesel and jet fuel and lubricating oils in the San Francisco Bay Area city of Richmond began striking at 12.01am, the union said in an email. Workers recently voted down a contract offer from \uc2 Chevron\uc2 , and the company refused to return to the bargaining table.\par \par \uc2 Refinery operations will continue as normal, \uc2 Chevron\uc2  said. But if the strike were to halt operations at the refinery, that could negatively affect fuel prices in California, which already has the highest gas prices in the US at $5.86 a gallon, according to the \uc2 American Automobile Association\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be coming at a very unfortunate time because we already have a shortage of refinery capacity in California right now, and so losing even one or two percent of the state\u8217\'20\'19s refinery capacity would probably result in a noticeable increase in gasoline prices,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Severin Borenstein\uc2 , a \uc2 UC Berkeley\uc2  professor, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ktvu.com/news/chevron-refinery-workers-to-go-on-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 KTVU}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Gas prices in the Golden State have continued to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mercurynews.com/2022/03/21/gas-prices-in-california-still-on-the-rise-despite-a-drop-in-the-national-average/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rise}}}\uc2 , even as they\u8217\'20\'19ve started to fall elsewhere in the US. Lawmakers are calling for a $400 rebate for every taxpayer to help alleviate the burden of high prices at the pumps.\par \par \uc2 Chevron\uc2 , which is based in San Ramon, California, has said it does not expect the strike to cause any supply chain issues and told KTVU it would bring in trained workers to replace those on strike.\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Sunday, \uc2 Chevron\uc2  said it has negotiated with the union for months, and believes the contract it offered was fair and addressed union concerns.\par \par \uc2 The union said it had negotiated a national agreement for oil workers on wages and working conditions, but about 200 individual bargaining units still had to negotiate local issues.\par \par \uc2 USW Local 5 representative B.K. White, a refinery operator who has worked for the company for 29 years, said \uc2 Chevron\uc2  failed to address worker fatigue and a lack of staffing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we had more people and could get a better pay rate, maybe our members wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t feel obligated to come in and work as many as 70 hours a week to make ends meet. We don\u8217\'20\'19t believe that is safe,\u8221\'20\'1D White said.\par \par \uc2 Chevron\uc2  said that in Richmond, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe union\u8217\'20\'19s demands exceeded what the company believes to be reasonable and moved beyond what was agreed to as part of the national pattern bargaining agreement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The old contract with \uc2 Chevron\uc2  in Richmond expired 1 February and workers had been reporting to their jobs on a rolling 24-hour extension, the union said.\par \par \uc2 The company offered a 2.5% pay increase, but the union had asked for 5% to keep up with inflation and cost of living in the Bay Area, White said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s rough for the blue-collar worker in the Bay Area, and we asked for a 5% bump to help us out a little bit with our medical at Kaiser, which went up 23% last year,\u8221\'20\'1D White said.\par \par \uc2 White said the company has already brought in about 100 replacement workers who are not trained to run the plants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is at the detriment of the city of Richmond and the environment,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The company said it brought in qualified replacements starting with Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s night shift.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe employees who are operating the refinery during the strike have satisfied the necessary requirements to perform their designated jobs (including receiving on-the-job training from experienced employees/operators) so that the refinery will be operated safely and in compliance with all applicable laws,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Chevron\uc2  spokesperson Tyler Kruzich said in an email.\par \par \uc2 If the strike were to shut down the refinery, that could negatively affect gasoline prices in California \u8211\'20\'13 which has the highest regular gas price in the nation at $5.86 per gallon, according to the \uc2 American Automobile Association\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, Ken Medlock, director of the Center for Energy Studies at \uc2 Rice University\u8217\'20\'19s Baker Institute\uc2 , said it is highly unlikely the strike would lead \uc2 Chevron\uc2  to shut down operations or raise prices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is more likely that the refinery will run with a skeleton crew\u8217\'20\'19 until the labor contract issues can be resolved,\u8221\'20\'1D Medlock said in an email.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia prices are already higher than other states due to the unique blend that must be sold in the state that limits arbitrage of imported gasoline from other regions, so there is ample incentive to keep the refinery running,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 The old contract with \uc2 Chevron\uc2  in Richmond expired Feb. 1, and workers had been reporting to their jobs on a rolling 24-hour extension, the union said.\par \par \uc2 The San Ramon, California-based \uc2 Chevron\uc2  said on its website that the refinery employs 1,300 workers. The union represents about 600 employees who include machinists, pipefitters, lab technicians and warehouse workers, White said.\par \par \uc2 The refinery is one of largest in the state and processes about 240,000 barrels of crude oil a day to make gasoline, diesel and jet fuel and lubricating oils, products that are sold mainly in California.\par \par \uc2 Chevron\uc2  said in a statement it is \u8220\'20\'1Cfully prepared to continue normal operations\u8221\'20\'1D despite the strike.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe anticipate no issues in maintaining a reliable supply of products to the market,\u8221\'20\'1D it said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220322ei3m001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
