\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Disney\uc2  staff stage walkouts over Florida\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18don\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8217\'20\'19 bill\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 437 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 March 2022\par 10:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Disney\uc2  and its CEO, \uc2 Bob Chapek\uc2 , spoke out against the bill in an internal staff email but refused to publicly condemn it\par \par \uc2 Disney\uc2  staff members this week and next are staging walkouts over Florida\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/08/dont-say-gay-bill-florida-senate-lgbtq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t Say Gay\u8221\'20\'1D bill}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Parental Rights in Education bill, which critics have dubbed as the \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t Say Gay\u8221\'20\'1D bill, was recently passed by Florida Republicans but has not yet been signed into law. The controversial bill bans all discussion of sexuality and gender identity in schools.\par \par \uc2 Disney\uc2  and its CEO, \uc2 Bob Chapek\uc2 , spoke out against the bill last week in an internal staff email but refused to publicly condemn the bill, prompting the staged walkouts from employees.\par \par \uc2 Chapek said \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s leadership \u8220\'20\'1Cunequivocally stand\u8221\'20\'1D with LGBTQ+ employees but said that corporate statements \u8220\'20\'1Cdo very little to change outcomes or minds\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cthey are often weaponized by one side or the other to further divide and inflame\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Chapek\u8217\'20\'19s statement sparked backlash within the company, which employs more than 75,000 staff members in Florida. Many condemned Chapek\u8217\'20\'19s silence, to which he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2022/03/11/media/disney-chapek-apology-florida-lgbtq/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 responded}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CSpeaking to you, reading your messages, and meeting with you have helped me better understand how painful our silence was.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou needed me to be a stronger ally in the fight for equal rights and I let you down. I am sorry,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that \uc2 Disney\uc2  will be \u8220\'20\'1Cpausing all political donations in the state of Florida\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Since then, \uc2 Disney\uc2  employees have been organizing 15-minute daily walkouts and \u8220\'20\'1Csickouts\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the \uc2 Twitter\uc2  page @DisneyWalkout launched in response to the bill. Staff members will stage a full-day walkout on 22 March.\par \par \uc2 In an open letter on the accompanying website, WhereIsChapek.com, \uc2 Disney\uc2  employees criticized \uc2 Disney\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s leadership, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whereischapek.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CAs a community, we have been forced into an impossible and unsustainable position. We must now take action to convince TWDC to protect employees and their families in the face of such open and unapologetic bigotry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Marvel Studios, which is owned by \uc2 Disney\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://denounced"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denounced}}}\uc2  the bill and said that it \u8220\'20\'1Cproudly\u8221\'20\'1D stands with the community and pledged to continue its support and allyship.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flsenate.gov/Session/Bill/2022/1557/?Tab=BillText"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The bill}}}\uc2  requires the implementation of \u8220\'20\'1Cprocedures to reinforce fundamental right of parents to make decisions regarding upbringing and control of their children\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In addition to allowing parents to launch legal actions against school boards if they believe policies overstep that \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamental right\u8221\'20\'1D, the bill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/changing-america/respect/equality/590838-house-committee-in-florida-passes-dont-say-gay-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bans}}}\uc2  teachers from discussing in classrooms LGBTQ+ topics \u8220\'20\'1Cnot age-appropriate or developmentally appropriate for students\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220317ei3h001ms\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
