\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US workers in new push for level playing field in unionization efforts\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,010 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 March 2022\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers are calling for the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  to ban captive audience meetings and make organizing easier\par \par \uc2 American workers attempting to form unions in their workplaces are pushing the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  to expand organizing rights \u8211\'20\'13 from reinstating the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/nlrb-legal-chief-plans-back-to-future-strategy-on-board-powers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joy Silk doctrine}}}\uc2  that makes unionization easier, to banning captive audience meetings held by employers to discourage organizing efforts.\par \par \uc2 Their efforts could transform how unions organize workers in the US, especially amid opposition from employers.\par \par \uc2 Max Capasso, who has worked as a barista at Great Lakes Coffee in Detroit for six months, is one of about 20 workers at the coffee chain currently on strike, demanding their employer recognize their union and collectively bargain with workers.\par \par \uc2 In January, Capasso said, nine baristas at the Midtown location in Detroit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/news/local/michigan/detroit/2022/02/16/great-lakes-coffee-strike-union-contract-detroit/6811803001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tested positive }}}\uc2  for Covid-19, and management insisted the remaining workers, despite having been exposed, still come into work. The company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mlive.com/public-interest/2022/03/detroit-baristas-file-unfair-labor-practice-charges-against-great-lakes-coffee.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denies}}}\uc2  that workers were asked to come into work sick.\par \par \uc2 Capasso and others had been communicating with each other about working conditions and low pay, but the Covid-19 issue prompted them to sign a joint letter requesting that management provide hazard pay and not demand workers return to work without being cleared of the virus.\par \par \uc2 In response, the store location was shut down indefinitely, which incited the union organizing effort with \uc2 Unite Here\uc2  Local 24. Twenty out of 24 workers have signed union authorization cards and have been on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://miaflcio.org/great-lakes-coffee-roasting-company-baristas-and-cooks-go-on-strike-for-union-recognition/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike}}}\uc2  since 16 February to demand recognition.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe clearly have a vast majority, we\u8217\'20\'19ve clearly proven that we are dedicated to this strike and we are dedicated to this union and getting a contract, and they have refused to acknowledge it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Capasso. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are seeking a higher authority to force their hand and come sit at the table with us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During the third week of the strike, workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/coffee_comrades/status/1498677682116214785"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed unfair labor practice charges}}}\uc2  against Great Lakes Coffee with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 , requesting the board reinstate the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://brandonmagner.substack.com/p/the-scandalous-story-of-how-joy-silk?s=r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joy Silk doctrine}}}\uc2 , a policy which stipulates an employer must recognize and bargain collectively with a union unless they have a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood faith doubt\u8221\'20\'1D of majority support for the union.\par \par \uc2 Great Lakes Coffee did not respond to multiple requests for comment on the filing.\par \par \uc2 This would make it easier for workers to form unions as they would not have to hold ballot elections to do so, and under Joy Silk, employers would be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fastcompany.com/90720656/the-joy-silk-doctrine-how-a-small-change-to-labor-law-that-could-have-huge-benefits-for-organizing-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 forced}}}\uc2  to bargain collectively with the union if found to have broken labor law during a union election process.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has repeatedly expressed support for expanding union organizing rights, most recently during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2022/03/01/remarks-of-president-joe-biden-state-of-the-union-address-as-delivered/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 State of the Union address}}}\uc2 . During the speech, Biden said that \u8220\'20\'1Cwhen a majority of workers want to form a union they shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be stopped,\u8221\'20\'1D which was reaffirming support for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/117th-congress/house-bill/842/all-actions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Protecting the Right to Organize Act}}}\uc2 , which passed the House last year but has yet to receive a Senate vote.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s new appointees to the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 , including the general counsel, \uc2 Jennifer Abruzzo\uc2 , have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/news-outreach/news-story/general-counsel-jennifer-abruzzo-releases-memorandum-presenting-issue"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  for several types of cases for regional offices to bring to the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  general counsel office, outlining the office\u8217\'20\'19s priorities, including consideration of requesting the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  reinstate Joy Silk, which was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nlrbgc/status/1441399054798364676"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 abandoned }}}\uc2  by the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  around 1970.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGiven the many years that we have had since Joy Silk was abandoned, we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen over those years, decade upon decade, employers abuse their power at the workplace where they intimidate employees\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to unionize,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Risa Lieberwitz\uc2 , a professor of law and employment law at \uc2 Cornell University\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CBringing Joy Silk back would be a doctrine that more fully respects workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights to unionize.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lieberwitz said banning captive audience meetings will probably be more difficult, given employer opposition in citing first amendment rights. But there could be other ways for the board to address the coercive nature of captive audience meetings, such as granting unions equal access and time with workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C Now is a chance with a new board and this very creative general counsel to really take actions to engage in review and rethinking about how to make the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  work the way it was supposed to,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lieberwitz.\par \par \uc2 Workers trying to unionize at Amazon in New York and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-03-01/starbucks-accused-of-worker-coercion-in-new-union-complaints"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starbucks workers}}}\uc2  in Alabama have filed unfair labor practice charges with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.law360.com/employment-authority/articles/1468923/labor-pushes-to-ban-forced-anti-union-meetings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 push}}}\uc2  for the board to ban captive audience meetings held by employers to discourage unionization efforts, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/pro-act-problem-solution-chart/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 policy}}}\uc2  that is also included in the Pro Act.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re definitely inherently coercive and we feel absolutely disgusted by Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s union-busting tactics,\u8221\'20\'1D said Brett Daniels, an Amazon worker and organizer at JFK8 warehouse in Staten Island, New York. \u8220\'20\'1CThey need to end and should be banned.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Daniels said that workers are regularly forced to attend captive audience meetings held by Amazon throughout their work week.\par \par \uc2 Under the Trump administration, the \uc2 NLRB{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://labor411.org/411-blog/nlrb-moves-to-overturn-state-law-that-bans-mandatory-attendance-at-anti-union-meetings/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  fought to overturn}}}\uc2  state laws that prohibited or limited employers\u8217\'20\'19 use of captive audience meetings during union campaigns, claiming bans limit the free speech of employers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are no first amendment rights there, people are forced to go there. The unions have no way to respond to it and they lie to them,\u8221\'20\'1D said Seth Goldstein, a pro bono attorney for the Amazon Labor Union. \u8220\'20\'1CCaptive audience meetings are inherently coercive and the board has to take action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amazon is publicly and aggressively opposing unionization in their warehouses, with a rerun election currently being held in Alabama after the initial results in 2021 were overturned due to Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s conduct during the election. Amazon is pushing workers to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unpackjfk8.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vote no}}}\uc2  in the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  elections that the board ordered after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nysfocus.com/2021/12/22/after-initial-setback-amazon-workers-on-staten-island-refile-for-union-election/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a majority of workers}}}\uc2  expressed interest in unionization through union authorization cards.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/pamdanziger/2022/03/03/first-starbucks-now-rei-next-amazon-and-apple-the-movement-to-unionize-retail-workers-picks-up/?sh=e5e888c10ad3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/30/business/starbucks-coffee-buffalo-union.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starbucks}}}\uc2  have rejected criticisms of captive audience meetings, dubbing them \u8220\'20\'1Cregular informational meetings\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Clistening sessions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Oregon has a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/employers-forced-worker-meetings-face-legislative-challenge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban }}}\uc2  on captive audience meetings and Connecticut is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courant.com/politics/hc-pol-captive-audience-connecticut-20220305-xjvu2c7gafbmfcn5hxa3b2fkbm-story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 currently debating}}}\uc2  legislation that would grant employees the right to leave these meetings, which business groups strongly oppose.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220311ei3b001e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
