\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Strike on children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital \u8216\'20\'18ultimate evidence that genocide is happening\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Samantha Lock (now); Maanvi Singh, Gloria Oladipo, L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong , Miranda Bryant and Royce Kurmelovs (earlier) \par \uc2 23,435 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 March 2022\par 04:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president calls bombing in Mariupol \u8216\'20\'18beyond atrocity\u8217\'20\'19 and urges world to \u8216\'20\'18stand united in condemning Russia for this crime\u8217\'20\'19Russia-Ukraine war: what we know on day 15 of the Russian invasionChildren under rubble after Russian airstrike on hospital, says ZelenskiyBritain and US fear Russia may be setting stage to use chemical weaponsPutin will lead Russia to strategic defeat in Ukraine, says BlinkenChernobyl power supply cut but \uc2 IAEA\uc2  says no imminent safety threat\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 Thank you for joining today\u8217\'20\'19s live coverage of the war in Ukraine. We have moved our live feed to a new blog which you can view below.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/10/ukraine-news-russia-war-kyiv-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-russian-invasion-hospital-bombing-latest-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia-Ukraine war latest news: US house passes $13bn Ukrainian aid bill; outrage at bombing of Mariupol hospital }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war on Ukraine has entered its third week. Hundreds have been reported to be dead or wounded while more than two million Ukrainian refugees have so far fled their homeland, according to \uc2 UN\uc2  estimates.\par \par \uc2 It is 6.45am in Ukraine and here is where the crisis currently stands:\par \par \uc2 * A children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital and maternity ward in Mariupol was destroyed by a Russian airstrike on Wednesday afternoon, Ukrainian officials said.\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  called the attack \u8220\'20\'1Cthe ultimate evidence of genocide\u8221\'20\'1D adding that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/ukraine-mariupol-civilians-russia-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 children are buried under rubble}}}\uc2  while the regional governor said 17 people have been wounded. \u8220\'20\'1CA children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital, a maternity ward. How did they threaten the Russian Federation?\u8221\'20\'1D Zelenskiy added. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  was unable to fully verify Ukrainian officials\u8217\'20\'19 accounts, but video published by the Associated Press showed multiple injured people at the site of the hospital attack.\par \par \uc2 * Western officials warned of their \u8220\'20\'1Cserious concern\u8221\'20\'1D that \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  could use chemical weapons on Kyiv. In an assessment, they said an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228e5bd8f08527b36853ed3#block-6228e5bd8f08527b36853ed3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cutterly horrific\u8221\'20\'1D attack on the Ukrainian capital could be unleashed}}}\uc2  as Russian forces attempt to overcome the logistical issues that have apparently plagued troops headed towards Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2  approved $13.6 billion in US aid to Ukraine and its European allies.\par \par \uc2 * Britain is planning to supply Starstreak anti-aircraft weapons and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/uk-plans-to-send-anti-aircraft-weapons-to-ukraine-says-ben-wallace"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Ca small consignment\u8221\'20\'1D of Javelin anti-tank missiles}}}\uc2  to Ukraine as Russian forces close in on Kyiv, the British defence secretary said.\par \par \uc2 * Canada will also provide {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  with an additional $50m in lethal and non-lethal military aid.\par \par \uc2 * The United States has seen indications that Russia is dropping \u8220\'20\'1Cdumb bombs\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 unguided munitions with no precise target \u8211\'20\'13 on Ukraine, a senior US defence official said.\par \par \uc2 * Russian foreign minister \uc2 Sergei Lavrov\uc2  has landed in Turkey for the face-to-face talks on Thursday with his Ukrainian counterpart \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2 , the highest-level meeting between the two countries since Russia invaded. Kuleba warned in a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  video his expectations were \u8220\'20\'1Climited\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine has accused Russian forces of \u8220\'20\'1Cholding 400,000 people hostage\u8221\'20\'1D in Mariupol. The Ukrainian foreign minister, \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2 , said the city, where conditions are described as \u8220\'20\'1Capocalyptic\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/ukraine-mariupol-civilians-russia-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was still being shelled by Russian troops}}}\uc2  despite an agreement to establish a safe evacuation corridor for civilians.\par \par \uc2 * Overnight strikes in the north-eastern city of Okhtyrka, Sumy region, reportedly killed a 13-year-old boy and two women, according to regional officials.\par \par \uc2 * Ukrainian authorities have said the power supply has been cut to the defunct Chernobyl power plant. The \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s atomic watchdog said the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/chernobyl-power-supply-cut-completely-after-russian-seizure-warns-ukaine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent nuclear fuel stored there had cooled down sufficiently}}}\uc2  for it not to be an imminent concern. Still, the news is raising concerns that a lack of external power to the site could compromise nuclear safety.\par \par \uc2 * More than 40,000 civilians were evacuated from across Ukraine on Wednesday but authorities struggled to get people away from conflict zones around the cities of Kyiv, Kharkiv and Mariupol, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228f6028f0806dde1f8b4eb#block-6228f6028f0806dde1f8b4eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Ukrainian negotiator said.}}}\uc2  Ukrainian authorities said earlier that the corridors should allow residents of the heavily bombarded cities of Mariupol, Enerhodar, Sumy, Izyum and Volnovakha, as well as towns around Kyiv including Bucha, Irpin and Hostomel, to leave, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/ukraine-mariupol-civilians-russia-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling on Russian forces }}}\uc2  to respect an \u8220\'20\'1Cofficial public commitment\u8221\'20\'1D to cease fire.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  has approved $1.4 billion in emergency financing for Ukraine to help meet urgent spending needs and mitigate the economic impact of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s military invasion.\par \par \uc2 * Mining giant \uc2 Rio Tinto\uc2  has become the latest corporation to cut ties with Moscow saying it was ending all commercial relations with Russian businesses.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Another video shared by Ukrainian media outlet {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nexta_tv/status/1501653510915596310"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NEXTA TV}}}\uc2 , purports to show a 61-year-old Scottish man bearing arms in Kyiv in the fight against the Russian invasion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy name is Rob. I am a 61-year-old grandfather from Scotland,\u8221\'20\'1D the man says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI travelled from Edinburgh to Kyiv to help in the fight against the Russians. I will do anything in my power to stop Russia from capturing Kyiv.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrMeet Rob, a \u8220\'20\'1C61yr old grandfather\u8221\'20\'1D from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Edinburgh?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Edinburgh}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Scotland?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Scotland}}}\uc2 , who\u8217\'20\'19s traveled to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Ukraine?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Ukraine}}}\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cdo anything in my power to stop {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Russia?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Russia}}}\uc2  from capturing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Kyiv?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Kyiv}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YYLJs31KdB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YYLJs31KdB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Charles Lister (@Charles_Lister) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Charles_Lister/status/1500948164903383046?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 7, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 The terrifying moment two Ukrainian explosive disposal specialists defuse a Russian bomb with just their hands a bottle of water has gone viral after the footage was shared by Ukrainian media outlet {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nexta_tv/status/1501653510915596310"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NEXTA TV. }}}\par \par \uc2 The 31-second clip, which has since been viewed more than 1.4m times, was captioned \u8220\'20\'1Cbomb defusing process\u8221\'20\'1D and shows two men kneeling beside the weapon while carefully unscrewing the seal using just a small water bottle and gloves.\par \par \uc2 Charles Lister, senior fellow and the director of the Syria and countering terrorism and extremism programs at the Middle East Institute, shared the video, describing the moment as an act of \u8220\'20\'1Cmind boggling bravery\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis Russia-dropped bomb would flatten a building \u8212\'20\'14 and yet these Ukraine EODs defuse it with 2 hands and a bottle of water, while shells audibly land nearby,\u8221\'20\'1D Lister said. \u8220\'20\'1CMind boggling bravery.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBomb defusing process {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AZeMaesE6K"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AZeMaesE6K}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NEXTA (@nexta_tv) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nexta_tv/status/1501653510915596310?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Russia?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Russia}}}\uc2  -dropped bomb would flatten a building \u8212\'20\'14 and yet these {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Ukraine?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Ukraine}}}\uc2  EODs defuse it with 2 hands and a bottle of water, while shells audibly land nearby.\par \par \uc2 Mind boggling bravery. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KvCZeOxRyz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KvCZeOxRyz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Charles Lister (@Charles_Lister) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Charles_Lister/status/1501654584992968712?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 US House approves $13.6bn worth of aid for Ukraine\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2  has approved a massive spending bill that would rush $13.6 billion in US aid to battered Ukraine and its European allies, the Associated Press is reporting.\par \par \uc2 After approval in the House on Wednesday night, Senate approval is expected by week\u8217\'20\'19s end or perhaps slightly longer.\par \par \uc2 House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  told reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got a war going on in Ukraine. We have important work that we\u8217\'20\'19re doing here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said with her party in the 50-50 Senate needing at least 10 GOP votes to pass legislation, Democrats \u8220\'20\'1Care going to have to know there has to be compromise.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The House approved the overall bill in two separate votes. The measure\u8217\'20\'19s security programs were overwhelmingly approved by 361-69, the rest by 260-171, with most Republicans opposed.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, the House will proudly pass our government funding legislation, which includes $13.6 billion in assistance for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 We will also pass our strong, bipartisan bill to ban Russian oil and energy products and taking further actions to diminish Russia\u8217\'20\'19s economy.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (@SpeakerPelosi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerPelosi/status/1501747789612605443?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The Ukraine aid included $6.5 billion for the US costs of sending troops and weapons to eastern Europe and equipping allied forces there in response to Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s invasion and repeated, bellicose threats.\par \par \uc2 There was another $6.8 billion to care for refugees and provide economic aid to allies, and more to help federal agencies enforce economic sanctions against Russia and protect against cyber threats at home. Biden had requested $10 billion for the package.\par \par \uc2 Pelosi said she talked to Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  for 45 minutes Wednesday. She said they discussed the weapons and other assistance his country needs and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe crimes against humanity that Putin is committing,\u8221\'20\'1D including a Russian airstrike that destroyed a maternity hospital. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the beast that Putin is,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelosi said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 Overnight strikes in the north-eastern city of Okhtyrka, Sumy region, reportedly killed a 13-year-old boy and two women, according to regional officials.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEnemy aviation hit residential houses. 5 people were rescued from the falls, 2 of them children. Also partially destroyed police department,\u8221\'20\'1D Sumy regional state administration head Dmytro Zhyvytsky said, citing a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/Zhyvytskyy/posts/377764341018538"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from the Sumy regional military administration.\par \par \uc2 Zhyvytsky said that just after midnight local time on Thursday residential areas and a gas pipeline were hit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe enemy artillery fired at the former Electrobutprilad plant. The result of the shelling killed three villagers, including a minor boy,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGreat Pisar\u237\'00\'EDvka suffered a night bombing. Power lines are torn, lying on the ground. A 13-year-old boy and 2 women were killed as a result of an artillery shelling.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Zhyvytsky also says three humanitarian corridors to evacuate civilians are expected to open from 9am local time.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, about 5,000 people were evacuated from Sumy, the regional capital that has been under heavy Russian bombardment for days.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Carlsberg\uc2 , the world\u8217\'20\'19s third-largest brewer, has said it will stop selling its flagship beer brand, cease all advertising in Russia and will donate profits from its Russia business where the company has already halted investments.\par \par \uc2 The Carlsberg Group\u8217\'20\'19s Baltika Breweries, headquartered in St Petersburg, will be run as a separate business and continue operating its eight breweries in Russia, where it has around 8,400 employees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Baltika Breweries\uc2  will be run as a separate business, with the purpose of sustaining our employees and their families,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Carlsberg\uc2  said, as reported by \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Heineken NV\uc2  also stopped the production and sale of its own brand beer in Russia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHeineken will no longer accept any net financial benefit derived from our Russian operations,\u8221\'20\'1D the company said in a statement in Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Asian shares surged on Thursday, tracking Wall Street\u8217\'20\'19s gains as planned diplomatic talks between Russia and Ukraine buoyed sentiment, although analysts warned the rally could be susceptible to a sharp reversal as risks remain, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices also regained some footing, having fallen more than 12% on the previous session as United Arab Emirates pledged to support hiking oil output to ease mayhem in energy markets.\par \par \uc2 MSCI\u8217\'20\'19s broadest index of Asia-Pacific shares outside Japan gained 1.6% in early trade. Japan\u8217\'20\'19s Nikkei surged 3.4% while Australian shares were up 1%.\par \par \uc2 Chinese blue chips rose 1.96% while Hong Kong\u8217\'20\'19s Hang Seng index rallied 1.8%.\par \par \uc2 US crude ticked up 1.37% to $110.19 a barrel, while Brent crude rose 2% to $113.2 per barrel.\par \par \uc2 European Union\uc2  leaders will phase out buying Russian oil, gas and coal, a draft declaration showed on Thursday, as the bloc seeks to reduce its reliance on Russian sources of energy. The United States banned oil and gas imports from Russia on Tuesday, while Britain said it would phase out Russian oil imports by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 Data due later on Thursday is expected to show US consumer inflation racing at a 7.9% annualised clip, according to a Reuters poll.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom a central bank perspective, the war in Ukraine is likely to lead to further upward pressure on consumer price inflation that could result in a supply side shock,\u8221\'20\'1D said David Chao, Hong Kong-based global market strategist at Invesco.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUS equities could be in a holding pattern with higher levels of volatility as investors assess the impact of the Ukraine conflict on inflation and possible Fed actions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 US stocks surged overnight, led by financial and tech shares. The Nasdaq Composite added 3.59% while the Dow Jones Industrial Average rose 2%.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 The British newspapers have once again led with Zelenskiy\u8217\'20\'19s war effort against Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion.\par \par \uc2 enltrZelensky has made quite the impression on the British press. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tGCckGy4d5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tGCckGy4d5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kevin Rothrock (@KevinRothrock) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KevinRothrock/status/1501733464395165705?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTomorrow's front page: Twisted \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's war on Ukraine plunged sickening new depths when he bombed women and children at a maternity hospital {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qp04Fo41i3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/qp04Fo41i3}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NQI5OOpOhz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NQI5OOpOhz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Sun (@TheSun) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheSun/status/1501686882064863232?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrGuardian front page, Thursday 10 March 2022: 'An atrocity': Russia bombs Ukraine children's hospital {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IJSpw13Ctl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IJSpw13Ctl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Guardian (@guardian) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/guardian/status/1501680124315545605?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrThursday's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DailyMailUK?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DailyMailUK}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/MailFrontPages?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #MailFrontPages}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xMOvLIEL0A"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xMOvLIEL0A}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Daily Mail U.K. (@DailyMailUK) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DailyMailUK/status/1501688007807709192?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 The United States is rapidly processing requests from Americans to export firearms and ammunition to Ukraine, the \uc2 US Commerce Department\uc2  said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Americans are collecting weapons for Ukraine after President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  called on his citizens to defend the country from invading Russian forces and promised to arm them.\par \par \uc2 The Commerce Department said it had imposed export controls on Russia to \u8220\'20\'1Cdegrade its ability to sustain military aggression\u8221\'20\'1D and Americans should check agency regulations to see if a license was needed to ship specific firearms to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe department has been processing requests rapidly for the export of firearms and ammunition to Ukraine under its existing processes and authorities,\u8221\'20\'1D a department spokesperson said, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Americans are donating thousands of sets of body armour and millions of rounds of ammunition in response to Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s pleas for military support.\par \par \uc2 Equipment donors and US volunteers for Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s armed forces must navigate US export license requirements for items like military-grade bullet proof vests.\par \par \uc2 Controls at airports on volunteers carrying such body-armour appear to have eased, a US volunteer in Poland said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom the latest wave of people carrying plates this week, not a single person has been stopped,\u8221\'20\'1D said the volunteer, who asked not to be named, referring to the ceramic plates that make vests bullet-proof.\par \par \uc2 Two Americans shipping military supplies to Ukraine, who asked to remain anonymous, said they had seen rapid export license approvals.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 At least 35,000 civilians were evacuated from besieged Ukrainian cities on Wednesday, President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  said, adding that three humanitarian corridors had allowed residents to leave the cities of Sumy, Enerhodar and areas around Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 Evacuations will hopefully continue on Thursday with three more routes set to open out of the cities of Mariupol, Volnovakha in the southeast and Izium in eastern Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN refugee agency\uc2 UNHCR\uc2  has estimated the total number of refugees at 2.1 to 2.2 million.\par \par \uc2 A serviceman helping carry a woman\u8217\'20\'19s child during an evacuation in Irpin, Ukraine. Photograph: Mykhaylo Palinchak/SOPA Images/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\uc2  A mother and her baby seen during an evacuation on Wednesday. Photograph: Mykhaylo Palinchak/SOPA Images/REX/Shutterstock Servicemen carry a baby to safety as the \uc2 UN refugee agency\uc2 UNHCR\uc2  estimates the total number of Ukrainian refugees at 2.1 to 2.2 million. Photograph: Mykhaylo Palinchak/SOPA Images/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 Mining giant \uc2 Rio Tinto\uc2  has become the latest corporation to cut ties with Moscow saying it was ending all commercial relations with Russian businesses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Rio Tinto\uc2  is in the process of terminating all commercial relationships it has with any Russian business,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesman said in a message sent to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The announcement from the Anglo-Australian firm comes after a top executive said the company was looking for alternative fuel sources for its Mongolian copper operations at \uc2 Oyu Tolgoi\uc2  but did not believe it can stop buying from Russia altogether.\par \par \uc2 The company did not immediately respond to questions on whether it would continue to buy Russian fuel and other products through non-Russian third parties.\par \par \uc2 Leading US companies like \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , \uc2 PepsiCo\uc2 , \uc2 Coca-Cola\uc2  and \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stopped trading with Russia this week.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 Canada will provide Ukraine with an additional $50m in lethal and non-lethal military aid, including Canadian-made cameras used in military drones and other specialised equipment, according to defence minister Anita Anand.\par \par \uc2 Prime minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  earlier announced another shipment of highly-specialised military equipment to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 enltrAs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JustinTrudeau?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JustinTrudeau}}}\uc2  announced today, Canada will provide Ukraine with an additional $50 million in lethal & non-lethal military aid, including Canadian-made cameras used in military drones and other specialized equipment.\par \par \uc2 We stand with Ukrainians fighting to defend their country. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iSdYNze7z9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/iSdYNze7z9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Anita Anand (@AnitaAnandMP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AnitaAnandMP/status/1501725316351414274?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 10, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.57am GMT\par \par \uc2 US secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  and Ukrainian foreign minister \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2 , in a phone call on Wednesday, discussed additional security and humanitarian support for Ukraine after Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion, the state department said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Blinken and Kuleba also discussed Russia\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cunconscionable attacks harming population centres,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement said.\par \par \uc2 US defence secretary Lloyd Austin also spoke with Ukrainian defence minister \uc2 Oleksii Reznikov\uc2  about the continued provision of defensive security assistance to Ukraines military, the Pentagon said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 enltrCall with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecBlinken?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SecBlinken}}}\uc2  on further steps to strengthen Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s defense capabilities. Grateful to the U.S. for the new package of tough sanctions on Russia. Pressure must be elevating until Russia stops its brutal aggression and barbaric war crimes against Ukrainians.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2  (@DmytroKuleba) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DmytroKuleba/status/1501619690161983493?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 Britain may escalate its military aid to Ukraine by sending state-of-the-art anti-aircraft missile systems.\par \par \uc2 UK defence secretary Ben Wallace said that \u8220\'20\'1Cin response to a Ukrainian request\u8221\'20\'1D the government was exploring the donation of Starstreak high-velocity man-portable anti-air missiles, according to PA Media.\par \par \uc2 Starstreak, the portable missile which works by a laser being pointed at a target to shoot down helicopters and fighter jets, would help Ukraine to \u8220\'20\'1Cbetter defend their skies\u8221\'20\'1D, Wallace said.\par \par \uc2 The weapons were in response to a change in Russian tactics, \u8220\'20\'1Cso the Ukrainians need to, too\u8221\'20\'1D, the defence secretary said.\par \par \uc2 He also confirmed that 3,615 Nlaw anti-tank weapons had been supplied - up from the previously-announced figure of 2,000 - and \u8220\'20\'1Csmall consignments\u8221\'20\'1D of the Javelin system would also be sent to Ukraine, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thetimes.co.uk/article/britain-may-send-starstreak-anti-aircraft-weapons-to-ukraine-9kndz9pqf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Times }}}\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 In answer to questions from MPs about how long the supply decision would take, Wallace said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are in principle going to do it.\u8221\'20\'1D He acknowledged that Ukrainian soldiers would need to be trained to use the missiles. \u8220\'20\'1CHow we are doing it [training] is sensitive,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The government has already supplied Ukraine with 3,615 anti-tank weapons and soon would be sending a \u8220\'20\'1Csmall consignment\u8221\'20\'1D of Javelin anti-tank missiles, Wallace told MPs.\par \par \uc2 A Starstreak HVM (High Velocity Missile) surface-to-air missile system on display in an undated handout photo issued by the UK ministry of defence. Photograph: UK MOD Crown copyright/PA\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 Index provider Morningstar will remove Russia securities from its fixed income indexes beginning 31 March and immediately move the country from emerging markets to unclassified, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  - which runs the most widely used emerging market bond indexes - also said Russia will be excluded from all its fixed income indexes on 31 March.\par \par \uc2 Index providers FTSE Russell and MSCI said last week they were taking similar steps as deepening sanctions and public pressure isolate Russia\u8217\'20\'19s economy from western investment and trading partners.\par \par \uc2 Morningstar said its indexes will remove cash and accrued interest from all Russian issuers regardless of payment status, from 9 March for all indexes except the Morningstar Infrastructure Bond Indexes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  said he believes Putin will eventually cease hostilities and enter negotiations after seeing invading Russian forces encounter fierce resistance from Ukrainians, according to an interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/xgdm37/volodymyr-zelenskyy-interview-ukraine-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 VICE}}}\uc2  News.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think he will. I think he sees that we are strong,\u8221\'20\'1D Zelenskiy told the publication. \u8220\'20\'1CHe will. We need some time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Zelenskiy suggested that he believes Putin will be forced to recalculate and end the conflict through negotiations, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CHow to stop this war? Only dialogue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president said his message to Putin right now would be: \u8220\'20\'1CStop the war. Begin to speak. That\u8217\'20\'19s it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCan you trust Putin?\u8221\'20\'1D Zelenskiy was asked. \u8220\'20\'1CTrust [Putin]? Oh, no. I trust only my family,\u8221\'20\'1D he replied.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 In case you missed this earlier, US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/vladimir-putin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vladimir Putin}}}\uc2  will fail in his effort to subjugate Ukraine, and will instead lead Russia into a \u8216\'20\'18strategic defeat\u8217\'20\'19 that is already unfolding. The secretary of state said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m absolutely convinced that Putin will fail, and Russia will suffer a strategic defeat no matter what short-term tactical gains it may make in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 You can win a battle, but that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean you win the war. On the contrary, you can take a city but you can\u8217\'20\'19t take the hearts and minds of its people and Ukrainians are demonstrating that every single day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Watch the video from his earlier press conference below.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US warns Russia may use biological weapons in Ukraine\par \par \uc2 The United States has warned that Russia could soon use biological weapons in Ukraine, rejecting Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s claims that the US supports a bioweapons program.\par \par \uc2 US state department spokesman \uc2 Ned Price\uc2  said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.state.gov/the-kremlins-allegations-of-chemical-and-biological-weapons-laboratories-in-ukraine/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin is intentionally spreading outright lies that the United States and Ukraine are conducting chemical and biological weapons activities in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 We have also seen PRC officials echo these conspiracy theories. This Russian disinformation is total nonsense and not the first time Russia has invented such false claims against another country. Also, these claims have been debunked conclusively and repeatedly over many years.\par \par \uc2 As we have said all along, Russia is inventing false pretexts in an attempt to justify its own horrific actions in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Russia has a track record of accusing the West of the very crimes that Russia itself is perpetrating. These tactics are an obvious ploy by Russia to try to justify further premeditated, unprovoked, and unjustified attacks on Ukraine. We fully expect Russia to continue to double down on these sorts of claims with further unfounded allegations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrFalse claims from Kremlin officials about alleged U.S. chemical and biological weapons labs in Ukraine are total nonsense. It is exactly the kind of disinformation we've seen Russia use repeatedly to attempt to justify its horrific actions in Ukraine. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UBBX26mhaO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/UBBX26mhaO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ned Price\uc2  (@StateDeptSpox) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/StateDeptSpox/status/1501701919571693578?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said the claims were \u8220\'20\'1Cpreposterous\u8221\'20\'1D and noted that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19ve also seen Chinese officials echo these conspiracy theories.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Taking to \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , she said:\par \par \uc2 This is preposterous. It\u8217\'20\'19s the kind of disinformation operation we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen repeatedly from the Russians over the years in Ukraine and in other countries, which have been debunked, and an example of the types of false pretexts we have been warning the Russians would invent.\par \par \uc2 Now that Russia has made these false claims... we should all be on the lookout for Russia to possibly use chemical or biological weapons in Ukraine, or to create a false flag operation using them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On 6 March, Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry tweeted that Russian forces found evidence that Kyiv was erasing traces of the military-biological program in Ukraine, allegedly financed by the United States.\par \par \uc2 The United States said Tuesday however it was working with Ukraine to prevent invading Russian forces from seizing biological research material in the country.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe took note of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s false claims about alleged U.S. biological weapons labs and chemical weapons development in Ukraine. We\u8217\'20\'19ve also seen Chinese officials echo these conspiracy theories.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  (@PressSec) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PressSec/status/1501676230617321480?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/britain-fears-russia-could-be-setting-stage-to-use-chemical-weapons"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Britain and US fear Russia could be setting stage to use chemical weapons}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  has approved $1.4 billion in emergency financing for Ukraine to help meet urgent spending needs and mitigate the economic impact of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s military invasion.\par \par \uc2 The global lender said Ukrainian authorities had cancelled an existing stand-by lending arrangement with the IMF, but would work with the fund to design an appropriate economic program focused on rehabilitation and growth when conditions permit, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Russian military invasion of Ukraine has been responsible for a massive humanitarian and economic crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D IMF Managing Director Kristalina Georgieva said in a statement after the meeting, predicting a deep recession in Ukraine this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFinancing needs are large, urgent, and could rise significantly as the war continues,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. Once the war was over, Ukraine was likely to need additional \u8220\'20\'1Clarge support.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The seal for the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (IMF) in Washington, DC. USA Photograph: Olivier Douliery/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Catch up\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  called the Russian strike on a maternity hospital \u8220\'20\'1Cthe ultimate evidence of genocide\u8221\'20\'1D. The children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital and maternity ward in the southern Ukrainian city of Mariupol was been destroyed by a Russian airstrike this afternoon, Ukrainian officials said. Zelenskiy said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228c7c68f08ec6557dfa681#block-6228c7c68f08ec6557dfa681"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 children are buried under rubble}}}\uc2  and the regional governor said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228d9708f0806dde1f8b3c0#block-6228d9708f0806dde1f8b3c0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 17 people have been wounded.}}}\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry\uc2  has confirmed the use of the TOS-1A weapon system in Ukraine, Britain said. The \uc2 UK\u8217\'20\'19s ministry of defence\uc2  said the system {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228f08d8f08ec6557dfa7f8#block-6228f08d8f08ec6557dfa7f8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 uses thermobaric rockets, creating incendiary and blast effects.}}}\par \par \uc2 * The United States has seen indications that Russia is dropping \u8220\'20\'1Cdumb bombs\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 unguided munitions with no precise target \u8211\'20\'13 on Ukraine, a senior US defence official said. They added that the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228ef308f087f6d099f4535#block-6228ef308f087f6d099f4535"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was observing \u8220\'20\'1Cincreasing damage to civilian infrastructure and civilian casualties\u8221\'20\'1D.}}}\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine has accused Russian forces of \u8220\'20\'1Cholding 400,000 people hostage\u8221\'20\'1D in Mariupol. The Ukrainian foreign minister, \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2 , said the city, where conditions are described as \u8220\'20\'1Capocalyptic\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/ukraine-mariupol-civilians-russia-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was still being shelled by Russian troops}}}\uc2  despite an agreement to establish a safe evacuation corridor for civilians.\par \par \uc2 * Ukrainian authorities have said the power supply has been cut to the defunct Chernobyl power plant. The \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s atomic watchdog said the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/chernobyl-power-supply-cut-completely-after-russian-seizure-warns-ukaine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent nuclear fuel stored there had cooled down sufficiently}}}\uc2  for it not to be an imminent concern. Still, the news is raising concerns that a lack of external power to the site could compromise nuclear safety.\par \par \uc2 * More than 40,000 civilians were evacuated from all over Ukraine today but authorities struggled to get people away from conflict zones around the cities of Kyiv, Kharkiv and Mariupol, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228f6028f0806dde1f8b4eb#block-6228f6028f0806dde1f8b4eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Ukrainian negotiator said.}}}\uc2  Ukrainian authorities said earlier that the corridors should allow residents of the heavily bombarded cities of Mariupol, Enerhodar, Sumy, Izyum and Volnovakha, as well as towns around Kyiv including Bucha, Irpin and Hostomel, to leave, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/ukraine-mariupol-civilians-russia-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling on Russian forces }}}\uc2  to respect an \u8220\'20\'1Cofficial public commitment\u8221\'20\'1D to cease fire.\par \par \uc2 * Western officials warned of their \u8220\'20\'1Cserious concern\u8221\'20\'1D that \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  could use chemical weapons on Kyiv. In an assessment, they said an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228e5bd8f08527b36853ed3#block-6228e5bd8f08527b36853ed3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cutterly horrific\u8221\'20\'1D attack on the Ukrainian capital could be unleashed}}}\uc2  as Russian forces attempt to overcome the logistical issues that have apparently plagued troops headed towards Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 \u8211\'20\'13 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong, Gloria Oladipo, Maanvi Singh\par \par \uc2 Children and mothers rush to board trains heading to Poland from Lviv, Ukraine Photograph: RMV pictures/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Analysis: Russia\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18warning\u8217\'20\'19 of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s biological weapons sounds just like Syria\par \par \uc2 When a Russian spokesperson took to a podium in Moscow on Wednesday and warned of a \u8220\'20\'1Cbiological weapons programme\u8221\'20\'1D in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2 , fighters on another battlefield \u8211\'20\'13 Syria \u8211\'20\'13 understood what she meant.\par \par \uc2 The anti-Assad opposition groups that still held northern Syria had heard it all before. From 2015, when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  took a prominent stake in the conflict, and throughout the gruesome years that followed, claims that they, instead of the Assad regime, had used chemical weapons were a ready-made slur that put them on notice of an imminent assault. The allegations were made by Moscow, whenever ground forces it was supporting wanted to clear a town or city. Brutal, indiscriminate bombardment followed. So did impunity.\par \par \uc2 Even in its infancy, the Russian war in Ukraine has many parallels with the conflict in Syria: barely restrained savagery, the mass flight of terrified civilians, and wanton destruction. Now the use of foreboding pretexts can be added to a growing list, which was born amid the ruins of Grozny, Crimea and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/feb/20/donbas-ukraine-evacuees-face-uncertain-future-in-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donbas}}}\uc2  and fine-tuned on the civilian population of Syria\u8217\'20\'19s beleaguered north.\par \par \uc2 The Pentagon and Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s leadership both disdainfully denied the Russian claim, which had been accompanied by a call for answers, and there seemed little likelihood of it cutting through an international discourse that has run heavily against the Kremlin and its disinformation programmes.\par \par \uc2 It was a very different story in Syria, where each claim of chemical weapons use by rebels was received with credulity in parts of the UK and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/europe-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Europe}}}\uc2  and there was little interest in exposing Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s lies. Winning the war of misinformation was a Russian success in Syria, in a theatre that wasn\u8217\'20\'19t short of wins for a military with no one apart from outgunned rebels and jihadists willing to stand in its way.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUkraine today is part of a much longer continuum than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/syria"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Syria}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D a former senior Nato officer told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CIt goes back further than Chechnya \u8211\'20\'13 politically, in terms of foreign policy, in terms of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s internal dynamics and in terms of the tactics of the Russian war machine. The only surprise over the past fortnight is quite how useless the Russian armed forces have been \u8211\'20\'13 thankfully. They have been utterly dire in every respect, which is very good news all round.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/russias-warning-of-ukraines-biological-weapons-sounds-just-like-syria"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18warning\u8217\'20\'19 of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s biological weapons sounds just like Syria}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Children under rubble after Russian airstrike on maternity hospital, says Zelenskiy\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lukeharding"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Luke Harding}}}\uc2  in Lviv, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/julianborger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Julian Borger}}}\uc2  in Washington, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/jonhenley"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jon Henley}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Russian bombs have \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely destroyed\u8221\'20\'1D a children\u8217\'20\'19s and maternity hospital in Mariupol, Ukrainian authorities have said, as shelling again halted mass evacuations from several cities, including the devastated southern port where conditions are described as \u8220\'20\'1Capocalyptic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister, Dmitryo Kuleba, accused Russia of \u8220\'20\'1Cholding 400,000 people hostage\u8221\'20\'1D in Mariupol, much of whose population has been without power, heat, water or phone signal for over a week, the president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , denounced an atrocity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMariupol. Direct strike of Russian troops at the maternity hospital,\u8221\'20\'1D Zelenskiy tweeted. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople, children are under the wreckage. Atrocity! How much longer will the world be an accomplice ignoring terror? Stop the killings! You have the power but you seem to be losing humanity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amid western warnings that Moscow\u8217\'20\'19s invasion was about to become even more brutal as the Russian leader, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , seeks to regain stalled momentum, local authorities described the damage to the hospital \u8211\'20\'13 a combined 600-bed complex with children\u8217\'20\'19s and maternity wards \u8211\'20\'13 as \u8220\'20\'1Ccolossal\u8221\'20\'1D and said at least 17 people had been wounded, including women in labour.\par \par \uc2 The deputy mayor, Sergei Orlov, said the city was being shelled continuously and 1,170 residents had died, 47 of whom were buried in a mass grave on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s medieval,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s pure genocide. The attack isn\u8217\'20\'19t simply treacherous. It\u8217\'20\'19s a war crime. They are attacking us with aviation, shells, multiple rocket launchers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  was unable to fully verify the Ukrainian officials\u8217\'20\'19 accounts, but video published by the Associated Press showed multiple injured people at the site of the hospital attack.\par \par \uc2 A pregnant woman is carried on a stretcher bed as she is evacuated from a children hospital in Mariupol, southeastern Ukraine, following Russia army bombardment. Photograph: EyePress News/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/ukraine-mariupol-civilians-russia-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Children under rubble after Russian airstrike on maternity hospital, says Zelenskiy}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  committed to tightening sanctions \u8220\'20\'1Cin order to impose the maximum economic cost on Russia\u8221\'20\'1D, in a call with Zelenskiy.\par \par \uc2 Per a statement from Downing Street, the two discussed the strike on a maternity hospital in Mariupol\par \par \uc2 Both leaders condemned the horrifying attack on a maternity hospital in Mariupol and the failure by Russian forces to respect ceasefire agreements in humanitarian corridors. The Prime Minister noted that this was yet further evidence that Putin was acting with careless disregard for International Humanitarian Law.\par \par \uc2 Johnson also \u8220\'20\'1Coutlined the work the UK is doing to provide the military equipment Ukraine needed to defend itself,\u8221\'20\'1D according to the statement.\par \par \uc2 In his latest address, Zelenskiy thanked Johnson for his support and urged western nations to help Ukraine \u8220\'20\'1Cto finally secure our sky\u8221\'20\'1D. NATO has rejected Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s calls for a no-fly zone.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEither close the Ukrainian sky from Russian bombs, or give us fighter jets so that we did it ourselves. The pause of indecision has become murderous,\u8221\'20\'1D Zelenskiy said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Russian strike on maternity hospital is 'ultimate evidence of genocide' \u8211\'20\'13 Zelenskiy\par \par \uc2 Speaking in Russian, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  decried the bombing of a children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital and maternity ward in Mariupol.\par \par \uc2 In an apparent appeal to Russians, Zelenskiy said:\par \par \uc2 A children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital, a maternity ward. How did they threaten the Russian Federation? What is this country, the Russian Federation, that is afraid of hospitals, maternity wards and is destroying them? Were there little Banderovites? Were pregnant women going to shoot on Rostov? Did anyone in the maternity ward humiliate Russian speakers? Or was it de-Nazification of a hospital?\par \par \uc2 Switching back to Ukrainian, Zelenskiy called the bombing \u8220\'20\'1Cbeyond atrocity\u8221\'20\'1D, in an address posted on Telegram.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEuropeans, Ukrainians, Mariupol residents, we have to stand united in condemning Russia for this crime that reflects all evil that the invaders have brought on us, on all destroyed cities: Volnovakha, Izyum, Kharkiv, Chernihiv, Okhtyrka, Borodyanka, Hostomel, Zhytomyr and tens of our Ukrainian cities that never posed any threat to Russia,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8216\'20\'18Hospitals and schools are destroyed. Churches and ordinary buildings are destroyed. People are killed. Children are killed. Air bombing on a children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital is the ultimate evidence that genocide of Ukrainians is happening.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Nations Population Fund{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Atayeshe/status/1501652238883770377"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 condemned}}}\uc2  the strike on the hospital. Footage of the attack shared online by Zelenskiy shows the hospital\u8217\'20\'19s windows being blown out, and parts of the structure collapsing.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukraine confirmed that the Chornobyl Nuclear Power Plant has been disconnected from the electricity grid, raising concerns that a lack of external power to the site could compromise nuclear safety.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2  (\uc2 IAEA\uc2 ) issued a statement:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IAEA\uc2  agreed with the Ukrainian regulator that its disconnection from the grid would not have a critical impact on essential safety functions at the site, where various radioactive waste management facilities are located. Specifically, regarding the site\u8217\'20\'19s spent fuel storage facility, the volume of cooling water in the pool is sufficient to maintain effective heat removal from the spent fuel without a supply of electricity. The site also has reserve emergency power supplies with diesel generators and batteries.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, the lack of power is likely to lead to a further deterioration of operational radiation safety at the site and create additional stress for around 210 technical experts and guards who have not been able to rotate for the past two weeks, in effect living there around the clock.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom day to day, we are seeing a worsening situation at the Chornobyl NPP, especially for radiation safety, and for the staff managing the facility under extremely difficult and challenging circumstances,\u8221\'20\'1D Director General \uc2 Rafael Mariano Grossi\uc2  said. \u8220\'20\'1CI repeat my urgent appeal to the forces in effective control of the plant to respect internal radiation protection procedures, to facilitate the safe rotation of staff and to take other important steps to ensure safety.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 IAEA\uc2  said it had also lost remote data transmission from its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iaea.org/topics/safeguards-and-verification"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 safeguards}}}\uc2  systems at the Chornobyl and Zaporizhzhya, another Ukrainian nuclear power plant overtaken Russia\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More than 1 million children have left Ukraine and fled to neighboring countries in the less than two weeks since Russia began its war on Ukraine, reported Reuters:\par \par \uc2 More than 1 million children have fled Ukraine to neighboring countries in the less than two weeks since Russia started its invasion of Ukraine, the head of the \uc2 United Nations Children\u8217\'20\'19s Fund (UNICEF\uc2 ) said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 At least 37 children had been killed and 50 injured, Executive Director Catherine Russell said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Russell said that she was \u8220\'20\'1Chorrified\u8221\'20\'1D by the reported attack on a children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital in the Ukrainian city of Mariupol, where officials said a Russian air strike buried patients under rubble despite an agreed ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis attack, if confirmed, underscores the horrific toll this war is exacting on Ukraine*s children and families,\u8221\'20\'1D Russell said.\par \par \uc2 The bombing, which Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  called an \u8220\'20\'1Catrocity,\u8221\'20\'1D took place despite an agreed ceasefire to enable thousands of civilians trapped in the city to escape.\par \par \uc2 Mariupol city council said the hospital had been hit several times by an air strike, causing \u8220\'20\'1Ccolossal\u8221\'20\'1D destruction. Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov said: \u8220\'20\'1CRussian forces do not fire on civilian targets.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More than 2 million people have fled Ukraine since Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  ordered the invasion on Feb. 24. Moscow calls its action a \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial military operation\u8221\'20\'1D to disarm its neighbor and dislodge leaders it calls \u8220\'20\'1Cneo-Nazis.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Most of those who fled are women and children, as able-bodied men have been ordered by the Kyiv government to stay home to fight.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian explosive ordnance disposal specialists (EODs) reportedly defuse a Russian bomb with their two hands a bottle of water.\par \par \uc2 From Charles Lister, senior fellow and the Director of the Syria and Countering Terrorism & Extremism programs at the Middle East Institute:\par \par \uc2 enltrThis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Russia?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Russia}}}\uc2  -dropped bomb would flatten a building \u8212\'20\'14 and yet these {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Ukraine?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Ukraine}}}\uc2  EODs defuse it with 2 hands and a bottle of water, while shells audibly land nearby.\par \par \uc2 Mind boggling bravery. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KvCZeOxRyz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KvCZeOxRyz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Charles Lister (@Charles_Lister) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Charles_Lister/status/1501654584992968712?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More photos coming out of civilians on the ground in Ukraine as Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion continues:\par \par \uc2 An injured pregnant woman walks downstairs in the damaged by shelling maternity hospital in Mariupol, Ukraine. A Russian attack has severely damaged a maternity hospital in the besieged port city of Mariupol. Photograph: Evgeniy Maloletka/AP Emergency employees work at the site of the damaged maternity hospital in Mariupol. Photograph: Evgeniy Maloletka/AP People fleeing advancing Russian forces file across wooden planks crossing Irpin River below a destroyed bridge as Russia\u8217\'20\'19s attack on Ukraine continues in Irpin. Photograph: Thomas Peter/Reuters People attempt to board a train leaving the Kyiv station, Ukraine. Photograph: Felipe Dana/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Industrial conglomerate 3M announced that it is suspending its business in Russia, the latest Western company to do so following Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 From Reuters:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter re-assessing our business in Russia, we have decided to suspend all business operations there,\u8221\'20\'1D the company told Reuters in an email, adding that its focus continues to be on the safety of its employees and their families.\par \par \uc2 Rival industrial conglomerate \uc2 Honeywell International Inc\uc2  had also announced the suspension of its business in Russia, as the West continues to pressure Kremlin with severe economic sanctions.\par \par \uc2 Today, \uc2 Nestle\uc2  as well as tobacco brands Philip Morris and \uc2 Imperial Brands\uc2  temporarily stopped business in Russia, with \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , \uc2 Coca-Cola\uc2 , and \uc2 PepsiCo\uc2  making similar announcements yesterday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Russian\u8217\'20\'19s delegation at peace talks with Ukraine \u8220\'20\'1Cwill not concede a single negotiating point,\u8221\'20\'1D reported a RIA news agency today.\par \par \uc2 From Reuters:\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s delegation at peace talks with Ukraine \u8220\'20\'1Cwill not concede a single negotiating point,\u8221\'20\'1D RIA news agency cited negotiator Leonid Slutsky as telling a television station on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The two sides have carried out three rounds of talks since the start of the Russian invasion. Russian Foreign Minister \uc2 Sergei Lavrov\uc2  is scheduled to have talks in Turkey on Thursday with his Ukrainian counterpart \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 John Kirby, the Pentagon spokesman, has been talking about the plan to deliver Polish MiG-29 fighter jets to Ukraine. In short, the plan is off.\par \par \uc2 He said the US defence secretary, Lloyd Austin had being talking to his Polish counterpart, and had \u8220\'20\'1Cstressed that we do not support the transfer of additional fighter aircraft to the Ukrainian Air Force at this time, and therefore had no desire to see them in our custody either.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kirby went through the reasons, the US was against the transfer of combat aircraft.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFirst, we believe the best way to support Ukrainian defense is by providing them the weapons and the systems that they need most to defeat Russian aggression, in particular, anti-armor and air-defense. We, along with other nations, continue to send them these weapons and we know that they\u8217\'20\'19re being used with great effect. The slow Russian advance in the north and the contested airspace over Ukraine is evidence alone of that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlthough Russian air capabilities are significant, their effectiveness has been limited due to Ukrainian strategic operational and tactical ground-based air-defense systems surface to air missiles, and Manpads [shoulder-launched anti-aircraft missiles]. Secondly, the Ukrainian Air Force currently has several squadrons of fully mission capable aircraft. We assess that adding aircraft to the Ukrainian inventory is not likely to significantly change the effectiveness of the Ukrainian Air Force relative to Russian capabilities. Therefore, we believe that the gain from transferring those MIG-29s is low.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFinally, the intelligence community has assessed the transfer of MiG-29s to Ukraine may be mistaken as escalatory and could result in a significant Russian reaction that might increase the prospects of a military escalation with Nato. Therefore, we also assess the transfer of the MiG 29 to Ukraine to be high risk. We also believe that there are alternative options that are much better suited to support the Ukrainian military in their fight against Russia. We will continue to pursue those options.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Systems of the \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2  (\uc2 IAEA\uc2 ) that were monitoring nuclear material at the Zaporizhzhia nuclear power plant in Ukraine have stopped transmitting data, said the agency today, reported Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, the same interruption of data was reported at the Chernobyl power plant amid an urgent request by Ukraine to the \uc2 IAEA\uc2 , the \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nuclear watchdog, about rotating the 210 technical personnel and guards working at the plant.\par \par \uc2 IAEA\uc2  chief \uc2 Rafael Grossi\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Csaid he was concerned about the sudden interruption of such data flows to the \uc2 IAEA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Vienna headquarters from the two sites, where large amounts of nuclear material are present in the form of spent or fresh nuclear fuel and other types of nuclear material,\u8221\'20\'1D said the \uc2 IAEA\uc2  in a statement.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The US is reportedly considering sanctions against Russian nuclear power supplier \uc2 Rosatom\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 From Bloomberg\u8217\'20\'19s Ari Natter:\par \par \uc2 SCOOP: The Biden administration is considering sanctioning Russian uranium supplier \uc2 Rosatom\uc2 . Huge implications for domestic uranium mining and nuclear power operators. No decision has been made yet.\par \par \uc2 enltrSCOOP: The Biden administration is considering sanctioning Russian uranium supplier \uc2 Rosatom\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Huge implications for domestic uranium mining and nuclear power operators.\par \par \uc2 No decision has been made yet.\par \par \uc2 Story on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheTerminal?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @TheTerminal}}}\uc2  w {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NickWadhams?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Nickwadhams}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nwadhams?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @nwadhams}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SalehaMohsin?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SalehaMohsin}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/willwwade?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @willwwade}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ari Natter (@AriNatter)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AriNatter/status/1501655345416052737?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukraine is preparing to potentially move its sensitive data and servers to another country if Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion continues deeper into the country, said a senior cybersecurity official to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Victor Zhora, the deputy chief of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s State Service of Special Communications and Information Protection, emphasized his department was planning for a contingency, but that it is being considered at all suggests Ukrainians want to be ready for any Russian threat to seize sensitive government documents.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are preparing the ground,\u8221\'20\'1D Zhora said. Plan A was to protect IT infrastructure within Ukraine. Removing it to a another country would only be a \u8220\'20\'1CPlan B or C\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The move could only happen after regulatory changes approved by Ukrainian lawmakers, Zhora said.\par \par \uc2 Government officials have already been shipping equipment and backups to more secure areas of Ukraine beyond the reach of Russian forces, who invaded on Feb. 24 and are laying siege to several cities.\par \par \uc2 Last month Zhora told Politico there were plans to move critical data out of the capital Kyiv should it be threatened, but preparations for potentially moving data abroad go a step further.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine has received offers to host data from a variety of countries, Zhora said, declining to identify them. For reasons of proximity \u8220\'20\'1Ca European location will be preferred,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are a lot options,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CAll the proposals are highly welcome and worth considering.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Zhora gave few details of how such a move might be executed, but he said past efforts to keep government data out of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s grasp involved either the physical transport of servers and removable storage devices or the digital migration of data from one service or server to another.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Hilton Worldwide Holdings\uc2 , the multinational hospitality company, said today it would be stopping all new developmental activity in Russia.\par \par \uc2 Hilton\uc2  also said that it had closed all its Moscow offices, citing the ongoing war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Here is \uc2 Hilton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s full statement:\par \par \uc2 Hilton\uc2  joins those around the world in shock and disbelief at the tragic events unfolding in Ukraine. Our hotels have always been part of the fabric of our communities that we serve, and we take seriously our promise to positively impact the places where we live and work. In addition to the steps we have already taken to protect our Team Members and guests, we are taking the following further actions in response to the current crisis:\par \par \uc2 * We are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newsroom.hilton.com/corporate/news/hilton-american-express-to-provide-rooms-to-support-ukranian-refugees"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 donating}}}\uc2  up to 1 million room nights to support Ukrainian refugees and humanitarian relief efforts across Europe, in partnership with \uc2 American Express\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://hospitality-helps.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #HospitalityHelps}}}\uc2 , and our community of owners.\par \par \uc2 * We have closed our corporate office in Moscow and will ensure continued work and pay for any impacted Team Members.\par \par \uc2 * We are suspending all new development activity in Russia.\par \par \uc2 * We will donate any \uc2 Hilton\uc2  profits from business operations in Russia to the humanitarian relief efforts for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 * And as previously announced, the Hilton Effect Foundation has contributed $50,000 to \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  and Project Hope to further assist with humanitarian aid.\par \par \uc2 Hilton\uc2  continues to monitor the situation as it evolves. We are keeping our Team Members and all those impacted by these events in our thoughts and hope for a peaceful resolution to this crisis.\par \par \uc2 You can also read the statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newsroom.hilton.com/corporate/news/hilton-statement-on-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More images from an earlier Russian airstrike today that destroyed a maternity hospital in Mariupol, where pregnant women and medical staff were present.\par \par \uc2 From the Kyiv Independent:\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Russian?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Russian}}}\uc2  occupants launched an air strike against a maternity hospital in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Mariupol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Mariupol}}}\uc2 , where there were pregnant women and medical staff at that moment. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/RussianUkraineWar?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #RussianUkraineWar}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/RussiaInvasion?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #RussiaInvasion}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZzFpgPjKrA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZzFpgPjKrA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 KyivPost (@KyivPost)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KyivPost/status/1501644832858587149?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , has rejected every off-ramp offered by the US to de-escalate and has, instead, ramped up Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine, said the US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , reported Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve sought to provide possible off-ramps to President Putin. He\u8217\'20\'19s the only one who can decide whether or not to take them. So far, every time there\u8217\'20\'19s been an opportunity to do just that, he\u8217\'20\'19s pressed the accelerator and continued down this horrific road that he\u8217\'20\'19s been pursuing,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said at a joint news conference with his British counterpart, \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe has a clear plan right now to brutalize Ukraine but to what end?\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said, adding that Ukrainians have shown that they would not accept any \u8220\'20\'1Cpuppet regime\u8221\'20\'1D that Putin might try to install to replace the elected Ukrainian government.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf he tries to enforce such a puppet regime by keeping Russian forces in Ukraine, it will be a long, bloody, drawn-out mess,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said.\par \par \uc2 Senior US defence officials last month assessed that Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine was designed to \u8220\'20\'1Cdecapitate\u8221\'20\'1D Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s government.\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com./world/blinken-says-kremlin-proposals-create-humanitarian-corridors-into-russia-absurd-2022-03-09/?taid=6228fde318c5730001d58ca3&utm_campaign=trueAnthem:+Trending+Content&utm_medium=trueAnthem&utm_source=twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  (paywall).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nestle\uc2  as well as tobacco brands Philip Morris and \uc2 Imperial Brands\uc2  are the latest multinational corporations to pull out of Russia as pressure mounts for western companies to take a stand given Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine, reports Reuters:\par \par \uc2 The world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest packaged food group fell into line with rivals \uc2 Procter & Gamble{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/companies/PG.N"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 (PG.N)}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Unilever{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/companies/ULVR.L"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 (ULVR.L)}}}\uc2  in halting investment in Russia, while cigarette maker Philip Morris said it would scale down manufacturing and Imperial went further and suspended it.\par \par \uc2 These announcements follow similar ones from \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , \uc2 Coca-Cola\uc2  and \uc2 PepsiCo\uc2  yesterday that they would be suspending business in Russia.\par \par \uc2 Previously, \uc2 Est\u233\'00\'E9e Lauder\uc2  and Shell announced that they were pulling out of Russia amid the ongoing invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Read the full article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com./business/exodus-draws-russian-threat-nationalise-foreign-plants-2022-03-09/?taid=6228f80607024b000156cbb5&utm_campaign=trueAnthem:+Trending+Content&utm_medium=trueAnthem&utm_source=twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  (paywall).\par \par \uc2 Customers visit \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  in Moscow, Russia. \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  announced it would temporarily close all 847 of its restaurants in Russia. Photograph: Oleg Nikishin/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s stock market will not open on Thursday, but the foreign exchange market, money market and repo market will open at 10am Moscow time, said \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s central bank\uc2 , reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 enltr(Reuters) - Russia's stock market will not open on Thursday but the foreign exchange market, money market and repo market will operate starting at 10 am Moscow time, the central bank said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The exchange has closed several times since Russia's invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Phil Stewart (@phildstewart) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/phildstewart/status/1501632161354588169?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 An announcement on the exchange\u8217\'20\'19s opening hours on Friday will be made by 9am Moscow time on Friday. The exchange has closed several times since the start of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 It is 9pm in Ukraine. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where we stand right now:\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry\uc2  has confirmed the use of the TOS-1A weapon system in Ukraine, Britain said. The \uc2 UK\u8217\'20\'19s ministry of defence\uc2  said the system {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228f08d8f08ec6557dfa7f8#block-6228f08d8f08ec6557dfa7f8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 uses thermobaric rockets, creating incendiary and blast effects.}}}\par \par \uc2 * The United States has seen indications that Russia is dropping \u8220\'20\'1Cdumb bombs\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 unguided munitions with no precise target \u8211\'20\'13 on Ukraine, a senior US defence official said. They added that the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228ef308f087f6d099f4535#block-6228ef308f087f6d099f4535"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was observing \u8220\'20\'1Cincreasing damage to civilian infrastructure and civilian casualties\u8221\'20\'1D.}}}\par \par \uc2 * A children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital and maternity ward in the southern Ukrainian city of Mariupol has been destroyed by a Russian airstrike this afternoon, Ukrainian officials say. Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228c7c68f08ec6557dfa681#block-6228c7c68f08ec6557dfa681"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 children are buried under rubble}}}\uc2  and the regional governor said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228d9708f0806dde1f8b3c0#block-6228d9708f0806dde1f8b3c0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 17 people have been wounded.}}}\uc2 The Guardian\uc2  could not independently verify this.\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine has accused Russian forces of \u8220\'20\'1Cholding 400,000 people hostage\u8221\'20\'1D in Mariupol. The Ukrainian foreign minister, \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2 , said the city, where conditions are described as \u8220\'20\'1Capocalyptic\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/ukraine-mariupol-civilians-russia-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was still being shelled by Russian troops}}}\uc2  despite an agreement to establish a safe evacuation corridor for civilians.\par \par \uc2 * Ukrainian authorities have said the power supply has been cut to the defunct Chernobyl power plant. The \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s atomic watchdog said the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/chernobyl-power-supply-cut-completely-after-russian-seizure-warns-ukaine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent nuclear fuel stored there had cooled down sufficiently}}}\uc2  for it not to be an imminent safety concern.\par \par \uc2 * More than 40,000 civilians were evacuated from all over Ukraine today but authorities struggled to get people away from conflict zones around the cities of Kyiv, Kharkiv and Mariupol, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228f6028f0806dde1f8b4eb#block-6228f6028f0806dde1f8b4eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Ukrainian negotiator said.}}}\uc2  Ukrainian authorities said earlier that the corridors should allow residents of the heavily bombarded cities of Mariupol, Enerhodar, Sumy, Izyum and Volnovakha, as well as towns around Kyiv including Bucha, Irpin and Hostomel, to leave, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/ukraine-mariupol-civilians-russia-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling on Russian forces }}}\uc2  to respect an \u8220\'20\'1Cofficial public commitment\u8221\'20\'1D to cease fire.\par \par \uc2 * Western officials warned of their \u8220\'20\'1Cserious concern\u8221\'20\'1D that \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  could use chemical weapons on Kyiv. In an assessment, they said an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228e5bd8f08527b36853ed3#block-6228e5bd8f08527b36853ed3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cutterly horrific\u8221\'20\'1D attack on the Ukrainian capital could be unleashed}}}\uc2  as Russian forces attempt to overcome the logistical issues that have apparently plagued troops headed towards Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me, L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong, for today. My colleague Gloria Oladipo will continue to bring you all the developments on the unfolding crisis in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More than 40,000 civilians were evacuated from all over Ukraine today, but authorities struggled to get people away from conflict zones around the cities of Kyiv, Kharkiv and Mariupol, Ukrainian negotiator David Arakhamia said.\par \par \uc2 In a post on social media, Arakhamia said:\par \par \uc2 Over 40,000 women and children were evacuated from all over Ukraine in one day. Tried 100,000, but failed.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian servicemen carry a baby stroller after crossing the Irpin river on an improvised path under a bridge, that was destroyed by Ukrainian troops designed to slow any Russian military advance, while assisting people fleeing the town of Irpin, Ukraine. Photograph: Vadim Ghirda/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Thousands of dockworkers at ports along the US west coast are refusing to handle any Russian cargo in response to Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine, Dani Anguiano writes.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Longshore and Warehouse Union\uc2 , which represents about 20,000 workers at 29 ports from Bellingham, Washington, to San Diego, California, announced the policy last week, calling the invasion \u8220\'20\'1Can act of aggression that endangers a population of more than 40 million people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 With this action in solidarity with the people of Ukraine, we send a strong message that we unequivocally condemn the Russian invasion,\par \par \uc2 said Willie Adams, the ILWU International president.\par \par \uc2 West coast dockworkers are proud to do our part to join with those around the world who are bravely taking a stand and making sacrifices for the good of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Russia admits using thermobaric weapon system in Ukraine, UK says\par \par \uc2 The Russian ministry of defence has confirmed the use of the TOS-1A weapon system in Ukraine, which harnesses the power of thermobaric rockets, Britain said.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Russian MoD has confirmed the use of the TOS-1A weapon system in Ukraine. The TOS-1A uses thermobaric rockets, creating incendiary and blast effects.\par \par \uc2 Watch the video below for more information about this weapon and its devastating impact.\par \par \uc2 ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/StandWithUkraine?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #StandWithUkraine}}}\uc2  ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/d8PLQ0PhQD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/d8PLQ0PhQD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ministry of Defence ???? (@DefenceHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DefenceHQ/status/1501621370614173701?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The US has seen indications that Russia is dropping \u8220\'20\'1Cdumb bombs\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 unguided munitions with no precise target \u8211\'20\'13 on Ukraine, a senior US defence official said.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian officials are increasingly accusing Russia of intentionally targeting civilians. Russia has insisted it is using precision munitions and hitting military targets.\par \par \uc2 The official told reporters:\par \par \uc2 We do have indications that the Russians are in fact dropping some dumb munitions.\par \par \uc2 They added that the US was observing \u8220\'20\'1Cincreasing damage to civilian infrastructure and civilian casualties\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The comments came shortly after Ukraine accused Russia on Wednesday of bombing a children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital in the besieged port city of Mariupol.\par \par \uc2 The US official declined to comment on whether Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s hospital strike was a result of their use, saying:\par \par \uc2 We don\u8217\'20\'19t have visibility into their targeting process.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The UK foreign secretary, \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 , and the US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , were both asked today about the possibility of a no-fly zone over humanitarian corridors in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Truss pointed to the anti-tank weapons and anti-aircraft system that the UK announced today it would be supplying to Ukraine:\par \par \uc2 The reality is that setting up a no-fly zone would lead to a direct confrontation between Nato and Russia, and that is not what we are looking at.\par \par \uc2 What we are looking at is making sure that the Ukrainians are able to defend their own country with the best possible selection of anti-tank weapons and anti-[aircraft] systems.\par \par \uc2 Blinken said he agreed with everything Truss said, later adding:\par \par \uc2 If I were in president Zelenskiy\u8217\'20\'19s position, I\u8217\'20\'19m sure I would be asking for everything possible, in his mind, to help the Ukrainian people and, as the foreign secretary and I have laid out, both of our countries, and so many others, have done extraordinary things to make sure that the Ukrainians have in their hands the means to effectively defend themselves against this war of choice from Russia.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian emergency employees work at the side of the maternity hospital in Mariupol damaged by shelling. Photograph: Evgeniy Maloletka/AP A car burns at the side of the hospital. Photograph: Evgeniy Maloletka/AP A woman walks outside the hospital. Photograph: Evgeniy Maloletka/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 World Health Organization (WHO) \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  (WHO) has verified 18 attacks on healthcare facilities, health workers and ambulances in Ukraine, resulting in 10 deaths and 16 injuries, \uc2 WHO\uc2  chief \uc2 Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 WHO\uc2  chief told a press conference:\par \par \uc2 These attacks deprive whole communities of healthcare.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s health system was proving \u8220\'20\'1Cremarkably resilient\u8221\'20\'1D but the violence was creating a multi-pronged health crisis, the \uc2 WHO\uc2  emergencies director, \uc2 Michael Ryan\uc2 , said.\par \par \uc2 Some 1,000 health facilities, including hospitals and health clinics, are situated within 10km of the frontlines, he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 West has 'serious concern' Putin could use chemical weapons in Kyiv\par \par \uc2 Western officials have warned of their \u8220\'20\'1Cserious concern\u8221\'20\'1D that \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  could use chemical weapons on Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 In an assessment, they say an \u8220\'20\'1Cutterly horrific\u8221\'20\'1D attack on the Ukrainian capital could be unleashed as Russian forces attempt to overcome the logistical issues that have apparently plagued troops headed towards Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 One western official said:\par \par \uc2 I think we\u8217\'20\'19ve got good reason to be concerned about possible use of non-conventional weapons, partly because of what we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen has happened in other theatres.\par \par \uc2 As I\u8217\'20\'19ve mentioned before, for example, what we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen in Syria, partly because we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen a bit of setting the scene for that in the false flag claims that are coming out, and other indications as well.\par \par \uc2 So it\u8217\'20\'19s a serious concern for us.\par \par \uc2 enltrWestern officials warning they have "good reason to be concerned about the possible use of non conventional weapons" - ie chemical and biological - by Russia in Ukraine\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dan Sabbagh (@dansabbagh) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dansabbagh/status/1501587003913211910?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWorth noting there have been similar warnings by Western officials about other possible Russian weapon use in Ukraine (e.g. themobaric bombs) - they are designed to deter as much as are an assessment of intent\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dan Sabbagh (@dansabbagh) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dansabbagh/status/1501591252478959617?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 It is 7.30pm in Ukraine. Here\u8217\'20\'19s where we stand right now:\par \par \uc2 * A children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital and maternity ward in the southern Ukrainian city of Mariupol has been destroyed by a Russian airstrike this afternoon, Ukrainian officials say. Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228c7c68f08ec6557dfa681#block-6228c7c68f08ec6557dfa681"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 children are buried under rubble}}}\uc2  and the regional governor said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228d9708f0806dde1f8b3c0#block-6228d9708f0806dde1f8b3c0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 17 people have been wounded.}}}\uc2 The Guardian\uc2  could not independently verify this. Ukraine has accused Russian forces of \u8220\'20\'1Cholding 400,000 people hostage\u8221\'20\'1D in Mariupol. The Ukrainian foreign minister, \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2 , said the city, where conditions are described as \u8220\'20\'1Capocalyptic\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/ukraine-mariupol-civilians-russia-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was still being shelled by Russian troops}}}\uc2  despite an agreement to establish a safe evacuation corridor for civilians.\par \par \uc2 * Ukrainian authorities have said the power supply has been cut to the defunct Chernobyl power plant. The national power company Ukrenergo said it was impossible to restore the power lines because of fighting in the surrounding areas. The \uc2 UN\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s atomic watchdog said the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/chernobyl-power-supply-cut-completely-after-russian-seizure-warns-ukaine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent nuclear fuel stored there had cooled down sufficiently}}}\uc2  for it not to be an imminent safety concern.\par \par \uc2 * Ukrainian authorities said earlier that the corridors should allow residents of the heavily bombarded cities of Mariupol, Enerhodar, Sumy, Izyum and Volnovakha, as well as towns around Kyiv including Bucha, Irpin and Hostomel, to leave, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/ukraine-mariupol-civilians-russia-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling on Russian forces }}}\uc2  to respect an \u8220\'20\'1Cofficial public commitment\u8221\'20\'1D to cease fire. But \uc2 Ukrainian interior ministry\uc2  adviser Vadym Denysenko says Moscow has \u8220\'20\'1Clargely failed\u8221\'20\'1D to adhere to these agreements. Civilians have been unable to evacuate from Izyum because of continued Russian shelling in the eastern Kharkiv region, said the regional governor, Oleh Synyehubov, adding that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/ukraine-mariupol-civilians-russia-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 buses intended to evacuate them were still waiting at the entrance to the town.}}}\par \par \uc2 * Zelenskiy said the international community would be responsible for a mass \u8220\'20\'1Chumanitarian catastrophe\u8221\'20\'1D if it did not agree a no-fly zone and warned that the country was at maximum threat level. In his daily televised address, he said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-622878f98f08527b36853b35#block-622878f98f08527b36853b35"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukrainians had shown throughout the last two weeks}}}\uc2  that they would never give in.\par \par \uc2 * More than 3 million Ukrainians will need food assistance, the head of the \uc2 World Food Programme\uc2  said. David Beasley, executive director of the \uc2 UN\uc2  agency, met Poland\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister, Zbigniew Rau, to discuss {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228b6a48f08527b36853d1e#block-6228b6a48f08527b36853d1e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 helping refugees arriving in Poland}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , has been asked about the apparent fiasco surrounding the plan to deliver Polish MiG-29s to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 I think what we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing is that Poland\u8217\'20\'19s proposal shows that there are some complexities that the issue presents when it comes to providing security assistance. We have to make sure that we\u8217\'20\'19re doing it in the right way.\par \par \uc2 Blinken said at a joint press conference with UK foreign secretary, \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Departing from a US Nato base in Germany to fly into airspace contested with Russia over Ukraine raises some serious concerns for the entire Nato alliance. So we have to work through the specifics of these things going forward. It\u8217\'20\'19s simply not clear to us that there\u8217\'20\'19s a substantive rationale for doing it in the way that was put forward yesterday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A woman is assisted to cross the Irpin river on an improvised path under a bridge, that was destroyed by Ukrainian troops designed to slow any Russian military advance, while fleeing the town of Irpin, Ukraine. Photograph: Vadim Ghirda/AP A member of the Ukrainian security forces hands over a girl to a man as civilians wait to board a train in Odesa. Photograph: Alexandros Avramidis/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , has been comparing the bombardment of Ukrainian cities with the wartime Blitz that Britain endured, Julian Borger reports.\par \par \uc2 I believe one reason we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing such an outpouring of support from the British people is because they\u8217\'20\'19ve been through something similar, the harrowing Blitz during World War Two, which inflicted colossal suffering on the country\u8217\'20\'19s people killing more than 60,000 British civilians, wounding 86,000 more,\par \par \uc2 Blinken said, standing alongside UK foreign secretary, \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 , at the state department in Washington.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s impossible to see the images of people seeking refuge in the Kyiv Metro in 2022 and not think of those who sheltered in the \uc2 London Underground\uc2  in 1942.\par \par \uc2 He added:\par \par \uc2 The grit, the compassionate determination that Britain exhibited eight decades ago that inspired the world, is exactly what we see in the people of Ukraine today, and it\u8217\'20\'19s why we need to stand with them.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  has described the reported attack by Russia on a children\u8217\'20\'19s and maternity hospital in Mariupol as \u8220\'20\'1Cdepraved\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrThere are few things more depraved than targeting the vulnerable and defenceless.\par \par \uc2 The UK is exploring more support for Ukraine to defend against airstrikes and we will hold Putin to account for his terrible crimes. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/PutinMustFail?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #PutinMustFail}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JBuvB78HVC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/JBuvB78HVC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  (@BorisJohnson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BorisJohnson/status/1501598088850518019?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Some 17 people have been wounded after a Russian airstrike reportedly hit a children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital and maternity ward in the Ukrainian city of Mariupol this afternoon, the governor of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s Donetsk region said.\par \par \uc2 Some of those injured included women in labour, regional governor Pavlo Kyrylenko said.\par \par \uc2 He accused Russia of carrying out the strike during an agreed ceasefire period that was meant to allow the evacuation of civilians from the besieged southern city.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis one appears to show people being helped out of the hospital {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Mariupol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Mariupol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pL8D1wsAhb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/pL8D1wsAhb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Liz Cookman (@liz_cookman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/liz_cookman/status/1501586280664252418?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Russia has denied targeting civilians in what it calls a \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial operation\u8221\'20\'1D in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At least 516 civilians have been killed since Russia began its invasion on 24 February, the \uc2 UN human rights office\uc2  has said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Office of the UN High Commissioner for Human Rights\uc2  said it had verified 1,424 civilian casualties \u8211\'20\'13 516 killed and 908 injured since the Ukraine conflict began two weeks ago \u8211\'20\'13 up from 1,335 reported (474 killed and 861 injured) reported on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The real casualty figures from Ukraine are \u8220\'20\'1Cconsiderably higher\u8221\'20\'1D,\par \par \uc2 especially in government-controlled territory and especially in recent days, as the receipt of information from some locations where intense hostilities have been going on has been delayed and many reports are still pending corroboration.\par \par \uc2 Most civilian casualties were caused by explosive weapons including shelling and missile and airstrikes, it said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Britain is planning to supply Starstreak anti-aircraft weapons and \u8220\'20\'1Ca small consignment\u8221\'20\'1D of Javelin anti-tank missiles to Ukraine as Russian forces close in on Kyiv to the east, the UK\u8217\'20\'19s defence secretary has said.\par \par \uc2 The UK would also continue to supply NLAW short-range anti-tank weapons, Ben Wallace told the Commons, and had already given Ukraine 3,615 of the portable missile systems \u8211\'20\'13 nearly double the 2,000 figure previously disclosed.\par \par \uc2 Wallace said Ukraine had already received \u8220\'20\'1C900 man-portable anti-air missiles\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a reference to Stingers supplied by other Nato countries \u8211\'20\'13 but was desperately seeking more arms as Russian forces attempted to encircle Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe capability needs strengthening,\u8221\'20\'1D Wallace said.\par \par \uc2 So in response to Ukrainian requests, the government has taken a decision to explore the donation of Starstreak high-velocity man-portable anti-air missiles.\par \par \uc2 Later, in response to questions from MPs as to how long the supply decision would take, Wallace said:\par \par \uc2 We are in principle going to do it.\par \par \uc2 He acknowledged Ukrainian soldiers would need to be trained in how to use the missiles.\par \par \uc2 How we are doing it [training] is sensitive.\par \par \uc2 Starstreak is the British army\u8217\'20\'19s equivalent to the better known US-made Stinger air-to-ground missiles that have been supplied to Ukraine by the US, Germany and the Netherlands among others since the Russian invasion. They are laser-guided with a range of 7km, unlike Stingers, which rely on infrared, and are designed to be harder to jam.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/uk-plans-to-send-anti-aircraft-weapons-to-ukraine-says-ben-wallace"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UK plans to send anti-aircraft weapons to Ukraine, says Ben Wallace}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 An adviser to Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , says women in labour and children are under the wreckage after Russia reportedly carried out an airstrike that severely damaged a children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital in the southern port city of Mariupol.\par \par \uc2 From Ukrainian presidential adviser Mykhailo Podolyak:\par \par \uc2 enltrMariupol is being erased by RF shells on our eyes. A direct blow at the maternity center has happened. Women in labor and kids are under the wreckage. Instead of new lives - deaths. Won't it be enough to close the ???? sky from missiles? Isn't it an argument to stop the killing? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lwUNrg4AkV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lwUNrg4AkV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ??????? ??????? (@Podolyak_M) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Podolyak_M/status/1501588915303718918?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Note: events are moving fast and the above footage has not been independently verified by the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s defence ministry\uc2  has admitted some conscript soldiers are taking part in the Russian invasion of Ukraine \u8211\'20\'13 despite multiple denials by its president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ministry said some conscripts \u8211\'20\'13 soldiers compulsorily drafted into the army \u8211\'20\'13 had been taken prisoner by the Ukrainian army.\par \par \uc2 We have discovered several facts of the presence of conscripts in units taking part in the special military operation in Ukraine. Practically all such soldiers have been pulled out to Russia.\par \par \uc2 Just yesterday, Putin had said Russia would not use any conscript soldiers in Ukraine in a televised message to mark International Women\u8217\'20\'19s Day:\par \par \uc2 I emphasise that conscript soldiers are not participating in hostilities and will not participate in them.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2  says children buried in rubble after Russian airstrike reportedly hits Mariupol maternity hospital\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , says children are buried under rubble after a Russian airstrike hit a maternity hospital in Mariupol.\par \par \uc2 enltrMariupol. Direct strike of Russian troops at the maternity hospital. People, children are under the wreckage. Atrocity! How much longer will the world be an accomplice ignoring terror? Close the sky right now! Stop the killings! You have power but you seem to be losing humanity. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FoaNdbKH5k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/FoaNdbKH5k}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ????????? ?????????? (@ZelenskyyUa)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/1501579520633102349?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Mariupol city council earlier said in a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  post that a children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital had been destroyed by Russian forces on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The destruction is colossal. The building of the medical facility where the children were treated recently is completely destroyed.\par \par \uc2 Information on casualties is being clarified.\par \par \uc2 In a \uc2 Facebook\uc2  video, the head of the regional military administration, Pavlo Kyrylenko, said:\par \par \uc2 The maternity ward in the city centre, the children\u8217\'20\'19s ward and the therapy ward at the hospital - all destroyed in a Russian air raid on Mariupol.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has not been able to independently verify these reports yet.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A lion from an animal shelter in Kyiv is seen in a cage at Natuurhulpcentrum nature centre in Oudsbergen, Belgium after its planned transfer procedures were accelerated following Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine. Photograph: Clement Rossignol/Reuters\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Children's hospital in Mariupol destroyed by Russian air strike, city council says\par \par \uc2 A children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital in the Ukrainian city of Mariupol has reportedly been destroyed by Russian air strikes, according to the city council.\par \par \uc2 Mariupol council described the damage on the hospital as \u8220\'20\'1Ccolossal\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that it did not yet know any casualty figures. In an online post today, the city council said:\par \par \uc2 The Russian occupying forces have dropped several bombs on the children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital.\par \par \uc2 enltrA man stands at a place where one of the aviation bombs Russians dropped on Mariupol children's hospital today, hit the ground. Show this to Russian fuckers. Children's hospital is completely destroyed. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BhIJHLB6wl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BhIJHLB6wl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nika Melkozerova (@NikaMelkozerova) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NikaMelkozerova/status/1501573568026525703?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrMariupol authorities say that a Russian aerial bomb destroyed a children\u8217\'20\'19s hospital less than a hour ago {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Ukraine?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Ukraine}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uTQOm17ucq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uTQOm17ucq}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bojan Pancevski (@bopanc)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bopanc/status/1501576915555164163?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The report could not immediately be verified by Reuters. Russia has denied targeting civilians in its assault on Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2  says it sees 'no critical impact on safety' at Chernobyl\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2  has said it sees \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/chernobyl-power-supply-cut-completely-after-russian-seizure-warns-ukaine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no critical impact on safety}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D at Chernobyl after reports that Russian forces had disconnected the nuclear power plant from the grid.\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Ukraine?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Ukraine}}}\uc2  has informed \uc2 IAEA\uc2  of power loss at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Chornobyl?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Chornobyl}}}\uc2  Nuclear Power Plant, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rafaelmgrossi?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @rafaelmgrossi}}}\uc2  says development violates key safety pillar on ensuring uninterrupted power supply; in this case \uc2 IAEA\uc2  sees no critical impact on safety.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 IAEA - International Atomic Energy Agency (@iaeaorg)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/iaeaorg/status/1501545852715905029?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 It also reiterated a previous statement in which it said that sufficient time has passed since the 1986 Chernobyl disaster that it can \u8220\'20\'1Cmaintain effective heat removal without the need for electrical supply\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrIAEA says heat load of spent fuel storage pool and volume of cooling water at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Chornobyl?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Chornobyl}}}\uc2  Nuclear Power Plant sufficient for effective heat removal without need for electrical supply. \uc2 IAEA\uc2  update from March 3: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/x5IlduZQOn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/x5IlduZQOn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 IAEA - International Atomic Energy Agency (@iaeaorg) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/iaeaorg/status/1501545859468742664?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The 3 March statement reads:\par \par \uc2 Due to time elapsed since the 1986 Chornobyl accident, the heat load of the spent fuel storage pool and the volume of cooling water contained in the pool is sufficient to maintain effective heat removal without the need for electrical supply.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, James Acton, a nuclear expert at the \uc2 Carnegie Endowment for International Peace\uc2 , said that while the loss of power at the site was concerning, \u8220\'20\'1Cmitigations should be straightforward\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He tweeted:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe loss of power at Chernobyl is concerning but it is extremely unlikely that spent fuel pools there will empty because of evaporation (which could lead to fuel melting). This process is slow and mitigations should be straightforward. (1/n) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GUVcBkFcd7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/GUVcBkFcd7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 (((James Acton))) (@james_acton32) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/james_acton32/status/1501558180207370240?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 He also said the risks at Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s operational nuclear power plants were \u8220\'20\'1Cmuch higher than at Chernobyl\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrRussia's treatment of the staff at Chernobyl is deeply concerning, as is Ukraine's regulator inability to fulfill its responsibilities. Overall, however, the risks at Ukraine's operational nuclear power plants are much higher than at Chernobyl. (2/2)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 (((James Acton))) (@james_acton32) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/james_acton32/status/1501559067990441985?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/chernobyl-power-supply-cut-completely-after-russian-seizure-warns-ukaine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chernobyl power supply cut but IAEA says \u8216\'20\'18no critical impact on safety\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The US vice-president, Kamala Harris, is due to arrive in Poland later today to meet leaders in Warsaw about the Ukraine crisis before travelling on to Bucharest.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports that she will collaborate with Poland and Romania on next steps to respond to Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion and to reassure them of Washington\u8217\'20\'19s support.\par \par \uc2 But, as Joan E Greve reports on the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2022/mar/09/kamala-harris-poland-jets-joe-biden-us-politics-latest-updates-russia-ukraine?page=with:block-6228b4bf8f08d38fbc42ad3d#block-6228b4bf8f08d38fbc42ad3d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics blog}}}\uc2 , her trip comes as the US and Poland have publicly clashed over providing fighter jets to Ukrainian forces:\par \par \uc2 Poland\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/08/poland-mig-29-jets-us-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced Tuesday}}}\uc2  that the country was \u8220\'20\'1Cready to deploy \u8211\'20\'13 immediately and free of charge \u8211\'20\'13 all their Russian-made MiG-29 jets to the [US] Ramstein air base and place them at the disposal of the government of the United States of America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It was originally expected that the US would receive the planes and then donate them to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2 , but the Pentagon released a statement hours after Poland\u8217\'20\'19s announcement saying that was not a feasible plan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe prospect of fighter jets \u8216\'20\'18at the disposal of the \uc2 Government of the United States of America\uc2 Government of the United States\uc2  of America\u8217\'20\'19 departing from a US/NATO base in Germany to fly into airspace that is contested with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  over Ukraine raises serious concerns for the entire Nato alliance,\u8221\'20\'1D said John Kirby, the Pentagon press secretary.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will continue to consult with Poland and our other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/nato"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nato}}}\uc2  allies about this issue and the difficult logistical challenges it presents, but we do not believe Poland\u8217\'20\'19s proposal is a tenable one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A senior administration official said Tuesday night that the White House has been in consistent communication with the Polish government about how to best provide security assistance to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a dialogue that absolutely will continue up to and as part of the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s trip,\u8221\'20\'1D the official said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a key priority for us and for all of our Nato allies, and so we expect that we will continue talking about how to achieve this really important objective.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ramstein air base in south-western Germany is headquarters for the US air forces in Europe and Nato allied air command.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris arrives to board Air Force Two at Joint Base Andrews in Maryland today for a three-day trip to Poland and Romania for meetings about Ukraine. Photograph: Saul Loeb/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More than 3m Ukrainians will need food assistance, says \uc2 World Food Programme\par \par \uc2 The head of the \uc2 World Food Programme\uc2  has said it will need to help over three million people from Ukraine with food donations.\par \par \uc2 David Beasley, executive director of the \uc2 UN\uc2  agency, spoke in Warsaw where he met Poland\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister Zbigniew Rau to discuss helping refugees arriving in Poland, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 enltrJust finished a meeting with President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrzejDuda?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AndrzejDuda}}}\uc2 . I said THANK YOU to the Polish people for welcoming 1+ million Ukrainian refugees, and discussed critical efforts to establish the humanitarian supply chain to reach families inside & outside of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Ukraine?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Ukraine}}}\uc2 . Thank you, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Poland?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Poland}}}\uc2  ! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2xojdXwD5V"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2xojdXwD5V}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Beasley (@WFPChief) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WFPChief/status/1501561019629551617?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 BBC Kyiv correspondent, James Waterhouse, reports a \u8220\'20\'1Cmixed picture\u8221\'20\'1D on humanitarian corridors, saying some have made it from Irpin to Kyiv, but others are trapped in Bucha. Waterhouse also reports shelling blocking the Mariupol route.\par \par \uc2 enltrA mixed picture with humanitarian corridors.\par \par \uc2 We've seen people make it from Irpin to central Kyiv, but we're hearing many people are trapped in neighbouring Bucha.\par \par \uc2 More are managing to leave Sumy, but there are reports Russian shelling is still blocking the Mariupol route.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 James Waterhouse (@JamWaterhouse) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JamWaterhouse/status/1501563715250012164?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Guardian journalist Luke Harding reports on comments from the deputy mayor of Mariupol, Sergei Orlov, who has just been speaking:\par \par \uc2 enltrDeputy mayor of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Mariupol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Mariupol}}}\uc2  Sergiy Orlov has just been speaking. Says city under "continuous Russian shelling", genocide taking place, 1170 people killed, 47 buried today in a mass grave. No water, heat, power, gas, with residents drinking snow and burning firewood. "It's medieval"\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Luke Harding (@lukeharding1968) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lukeharding1968/status/1501556301461172232?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrOrlov: "Putin is intent on having Ukraine without Ukrainians. It's pure genocide. The attack being waged by Russia isn't simply treacherous. It's a war crime. They are attacking us with aviation, shells, multiple rocket launchers."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Luke Harding (@lukeharding1968) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lukeharding1968/status/1501556979604635653?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrOrlov says {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Russian?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Russian}}}\uc2  army has shelled evacuation corridor, mined the road and put in a check point. 200K people desperate to leave, only 2-3K able to get out daily on 21 municipal buses. The others destroyed. Russians deliberately shelling assembly points for those trying to exit\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Luke Harding (@lukeharding1968) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lukeharding1968/status/1501560511074344960?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Russian?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Russian}}}\uc2  soldiers also fire on private cars trying to escape the siege, Orlov says. Not at them but alongside so they are forced to return to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Mariupol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Mariupol}}}\uc2 . "They are shooting and bombing the humanitarian corridor. That's the situation," he says, calling for an immediate no-fly zone\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Luke Harding (@lukeharding1968) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lukeharding1968/status/1501562986456129542?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Civilians have been unable to evacuate from the Ukrainian town of Izyum because of Russian shelling in the eastern Kharkiv region, regional governor Oleh Synehubov said.\par \par \uc2 An evacuation of civilians was scheduled to take place today from Izyum to Lozova as one of the six \u8220\'20\'1Chumanitarian corridors\u8221\'20\'1D today, but Synehubov said buses were still waiting at the entrance to the town.\par \par \uc2 He added that negotiations with the Russians were under way with the support of the Red Cross.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Newly arrived refugees seek assistance from Polish army soldiers after crossing the border from Ukraine into Poland at the Medyka border crossing, eastern Poland. Photograph: Louisa Gouliamaki/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The loss of power at the Chernobyl nuclear power plant in Ukraine does not have any critical impact on safety, the \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2  (\uc2 IAEA\uc2 ) said.\par \par \uc2 In a statement this afternoon, the \uc2 IAEA\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 Heat load of spent fuel storage pool and volume of cooling water at Chernobyl Nuclear Power Plant sufficient for effective heat removal without need for electrical supply.\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Ukraine?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Ukraine}}}\uc2  has informed \uc2 IAEA\uc2  of power loss at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Chornobyl?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Chornobyl}}}\uc2  Nuclear Power Plant, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rafaelmgrossi?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @rafaelmgrossi}}}\uc2  says development violates key safety pillar on ensuring uninterrupted power supply; in this case \uc2 IAEA\uc2  sees no critical impact on safety.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 IAEA - International Atomic Energy Agency (@iaeaorg) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/iaeaorg/status/1501545852715905029?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 French government spokesperson Gabriel Attal said France is in contact with the \uc2 IAEA\uc2  to assess the situation at Chernobyl.\par \par \uc2 France has asked Russia to cooperate, he said:\par \par \uc2 We are trying to clarify these reports together with the \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 German environment ministry\uc2  spokesperson said Germany had no knowledge of radiation leaking from the Chernobyl plant.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A local Kyiv orchestra performed the Ukrainian national anthem as Russian forces advance on the capital city from several directions.\par \par \uc2 The Kyiv-Classic Symphony Orchestra played to a small crowd on Kyiv\u8217\'20\'19s central Maidan Square today, who applauded when the national anthem was finished and a woman cried out: \u8220\'20\'1CTo Ukraine!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The orchestra also played an excerpt from Beethoven\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1COde to Joy\u8221\'20\'1D, on which the \uc2 European Union\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s anthem is based.\par \par \uc2 enltrHappening now in Maidan Square, a concert by the Kyiv Classic Symphony Orchestra {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zV6O5649bJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zV6O5649bJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Oz Katerji (@OzKaterji) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/OzKaterji/status/1501522456141520900?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrKyiv: the band plays in Maidan. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wIQ7O8ftWv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wIQ7O8ftWv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 John Sweeney (@johnsweeneyroar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/johnsweeneyroar/status/1501537726809653248?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  has refused to drop visa requirements for Ukrainians fleeing the country as Russian forces continued to bombard Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s towns and cities.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2  has allowed visa-free travel for Ukrainians, but the UK prime minister insisted that the UK was right to require the paperwork to be completed.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in the Commons today, Johnson said:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve already got 1,000 people in under the existing scheme, that number will climb very sharply. No one has been turned away.\par \par \uc2 Johnson said security checks were vital to prevent Russian agents from entering the UK.\par \par \uc2 We know how unscrupulous Putin can be in his methods, it would not be right to expose this country to unnecessary security risk and we will not do it.\par \par \uc2 We are going to be as generous as we can possibly be, but we must have checks.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the defence secretary, Ben Wallace, promised extra military equipment for the Ukrainian forces, with fresh supplies of anti-tank missiles and the possibility of anti-aircraft systems.\par \par \uc2 For more live updates from the UK, head over to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2022/mar/09/grant-shapps-private-jet-boris-johnson-ukraine-russia-keir-starmer-pmqs-visas-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our politics blog with Andrew Sparrow.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2022/mar/09/grant-shapps-private-jet-boris-johnson-ukraine-russia-keir-starmer-pmqs-visas-live"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Defence secretary announces new shipments of weapons to Ukraine \u8211\'20\'13 UK politics live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Video released by Ukrainian ground forces shows destroyed Russian vehicles in Sumy region.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian service personnel are also seen inspecting captured boxes of ammunition in the footage, which was filmed on Tuesday after Russian bombing of the north-east city of Sumy killed at least 21 civilians, including two children.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More than 400,000 people are being \u8220\'20\'1Cheld hostage\u8221\'20\'1D in the besieged Ukrainian city of Mariupol by Russian forces who are blocking humanitarian aid and evacuation, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister, \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2 , said.\par \par \uc2 Conditions in the port of Mariupol have been described as \u8220\'20\'1Capocalyptic\u8221\'20\'1D. Hundreds of thousands of residents there have been sheltering from brutal Russian shelling and missile attacks for more than a week without water, power or heating. Phone signals are also down.\par \par \uc2 enltrA video posted to social media Tuesday and verified by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nytimes?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @nytimes}}}\uc2  shows flattened homes in Mariupol, a key port city in southern Ukraine that Russian forces have surrounded. Information coming out from the city has been limited. W/ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ckoettl?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ckoettl}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dim109?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @dim109}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dA06f2WyTI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/dA06f2WyTI}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eb9ebE9mnE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/eb9ebE9mnE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Muyi Xiao (@muyixiao) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/muyixiao/status/1501363027765080070?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Attempts on Tuesday to begin the process of bussing about half the besieged city\u8217\'20\'19s 400,000 desperate inhabitants out via a \u8220\'20\'1Chumanitarian corridor\u8221\'20\'1D were abandoned after the Ukrainian government accused Russian forces of shelling it.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine has appealed to Russian forces to observe their \u8220\'20\'1Cofficial public commitment\u8221\'20\'1D to hold their fire during a 12-hour window today, in order to evacuate civilians.\par \par \uc2 Kuleba accused Russia of holding 400,000 residents of Mariupol hostage by shelling the city despite efforts to establish a safe evacuation corridor.\par \par \uc2 Almost 3,000 newborn babies lack medicine and food.\par \par \uc2 Russia continues holding hostage over 400,000 people in Mariupol, blocks humanitarian aid and evacuation. Indiscriminate shelling continues.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Soldiers arrive to reinforce one of the final checkpoints before the frontlines where Ukrainian forces are battling invading Russian forces near Brovary, Ukraine. Photograph: Marcus Yam/LOS ANGELES TIMES/REX/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukraine calls for ceasefire to allow power supply to be restored to Chernobyl\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister has called for a ceasefire to allow repairs to be carried out to restore the electricity supply to Chernobyl nuclear power plant.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s state power operator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228833e8f08d64fa95e910b#block-6228833e8f08d64fa95e910b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier said}}}\uc2  Russian forces had disconnected the nuclear power plant from the grid, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 Energoatom, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s state-run nuclear company, warned the situation could lead to the release of radioactive substances from the plant.\par \par \uc2 It warned in a Telegram post:\par \par \uc2 The wind can transfer the radioactive cloud to other regions of Ukraine, Belarus, Russia and Europe.\par \par \uc2 If the situation continued, \u8220\'20\'1Call personnel there will receive a dangerous dose of radiation\u8221\'20\'1D, it continued.\par \par \uc2 Work to repair the connection and restore power to the plant, which has been occupied by Russian troops, had not been possible because fighting was under way, it said.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian foreign minister, \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2 , said reserve diesel generators at Chernobyl nuclear power plant had a 48-hour capacity.\par \par \uc2 After that, cooling systems of the storage facility for spent nuclear fuel will stop, making radiation leaks imminent.\par \par \uc2 ukltr????? ????? ????????????????? ???? ? ???? ?? ??????? ??\u8217\'20\'19?????, ??? ????????? ????????? ?????, ??????????. ???? ????????????. ? ???????? ??? ?????????? ?????????????? ??????? ???????? ??? ????? ????????? ?????? ? ???? ????????? ???????? ??????????? ????????? ????????????????? 1/2\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2  (@DmytroKuleba) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DmytroKuleba/status/1501531656204783620?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A convoy of civilians, consisting mainly of women, children and the elderly, have been evacuated from the Ukrainian city of Enerhodar through a \u8220\'20\'1Chumanitarian corridor\u8221\'20\'1D after a temporary ceasefire was agreed with Russian forces, its mayor said.\par \par \uc2 Enerhodar is the site of Europe\u8217\'20\'19s largest nuclear power station, which has been held by Russian troops since they captured the plant late last week.\par \par \uc2 Mayor Dmytro Orlov said \u8220\'20\'1Cmostly women and children, the elderly, left the city\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Orlov earlier welcomed the announcement of a humanitarian corridor to and from the town, and said insulin, some medicines and food would be delivered to the city.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More than 400 Ukrainians who protested against the occupation of Kherson by Russian forces have been detained by Russia\u8217\'20\'19s national guard, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s military high command said.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the Ukrainian military high command said hundreds had been arrested for protesting in the now Russian-occupied Kherson.\par \par \uc2 Due to the furious resistance of the residents of Kherson, the occupiers are attempting to introduce an administrative-police regime.\par \par \uc2 enltrDay 14. Good morning. Video: Kherson - the only regional capital that has fallen. Ukrainian crowd of protestors gets angry after Russian troop start beating up a protestor. Russians open fire (in the air) and that does not stop but mobilize protestors. Pure anger and no fear {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MQQJwyyVju"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MQQJwyyVju}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tymofiy Mylovanov (@Mylovanov) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Mylovanov/status/1501437172502642690?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 ukltr??????????, ?? \u8212\'20\'14 ????!\par \par \uc2 ?? ??????? ????? ?????????? ????????? ??????????? ???????? ? ???????, ?????????, ??????? ?? ?????? ?????????\par \par \uc2 ???? ???????? ?? ??????? ??????? ?? ????????? \u171\'00\'AB????? \u8211\'20\'13 ?**??\u187\'00\'BB {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NhrJOD7JpW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/NhrJOD7JpW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ?????????? ????? (@HromadskeRadio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HromadskeRadio/status/1501205865776521229?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Russia has repeated allegations that the United States supported a military biological programme in Ukraine involving deadly pathogens including plague and anthrax \u8211\'20\'13 claims that the Pentagon has described as \u8220\'20\'1Cabsurd\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s foreign ministry\uc2  spokesperson \uc2 Maria Zakharova\uc2  said evidence of the alleged programme had been uncovered in Russia during what it calls its \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial military operation\u8221\'20\'1D in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Zakharova said:\par \par \uc2 We can already conclude that in Ukrainian biological laboratories in direct proximity to the territory of our country, development of components of biological weapons was being carried out.\par \par \uc2 She went on to allege that Russia had documents showing that the \uc2 Ukrainian health ministry\uc2  had ordered the destruction of samples of plague, cholera, anthrax and other pathogens after 24 February.\par \par \uc2 Both the Pentagon and the Ukrainian government has strongly denied these allegations, and Reuters reports that it was not possible to independently confirm the authenticity of any such documents.\par \par \uc2 Zakharova said the alleged programme was financed by the Pentagon, and demanded transparency from Washington.\par \par \uc2 We are not talking here about peaceful uses or scientific goals... What were you up to there?\par \par \uc2 Russia \u8220\'20\'1Cdemands details\u8221\'20\'1D, she continued:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Defence Department\uc2  and the presidential administration of the United States are obliged to officially explain to the global community, officially, not through talking heads, about the programmes in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 In response to earlier Russian allegations about the purported military biological programme in Ukraine, a Pentagon spokesperson said on Tuesday:\par \par \uc2 This absurd Russian misinformation is patently false.\par \par \uc2 A Ukrainian presidential spokesperson said Ukraine \u8220\'20\'1Cstrictly denies any such allegation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Following Zakharova\u8217\'20\'19s remarks earlier today, Kremlin spokesperson Dmitry Peskov said Russia considers its claims that Ukraine conducted military biological programmes as an important issue for the whole world.\par \par \uc2 enltrA \uc2 Russian Foreign Ministry\uc2  spokeswoman is claiming the US has been carrying out biological programmes in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 She claims Russia has seen documents backing up their claim that the US are harbouring components of biological weapons close to the Ukraine-Russia border. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mShzuyzUhk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mShzuyzUhk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sky News (@SkyNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SkyNews/status/1501498868797788160?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Hello from London, I\u8217\'20\'19m L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong and I\u8217\'20\'19ll be bringing you all the latest developments on the unfolding crisis in Ukraine. Feel free to drop me a message if you have anything to flag, you can reach me {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/leonie_chaofong"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on Twitter}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:leonie.chao-fong@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 via email.}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 A person is carried in Romanivka, Ukraine. Photograph: Maksim Levin/Reuters A man and his dog walk past a fire caused by a Russian bombardment on a storage facility, sending a dark plume of smoke into the forested area on the edge of Kalynivka, Ukraine. Photograph: Marcus Yam/Los Angeles Times/Rex/\uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here's a summary of the latest developments...\par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Lumen Technologies\uc2 , one of the companies that comprises the backbone of the internet, said on Tuesday it was pulling the plug on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  because of an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-622888f48f087f6d099f4180#block-622888f48f087f6d099f4180"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cincreased security risk\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . Lumen attempted to downplay the impact of the decision, saying in a brief statement it provides \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely small and very limited\u8221\'20\'1D business services in Russia. But it is part of the network that allows data to flow through the infrastructure of the internet.\par \par \uc2 * The Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskiy\uc2 , has said that the international community would be responsible for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-622878f98f08527b36853b35#block-622878f98f08527b36853b35"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mass \u8220\'20\'1Chumanitarian catastrophe\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  if it did not agree a no-fly zone and warned that the country was at maximum threat level. In his daily televised address, he said Ukrainians had shown throughout the last two weeks that they would never give in.\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s state power operator says that Russian forces have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-6228833e8f08d64fa95e910b#block-6228833e8f08d64fa95e910b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disconnected the Chernobyl nuclear power plant}}}\uc2  from the grid, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 * Kyiv authorities hoped to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-622878e48f0806dde1f8b073#block-622878e48f0806dde1f8b073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 evacuate many more people }}}\uc2  from Irpin, Bucha and Hostomel, the Ukrainian capital\u8217\'20\'19s deputy mayor said today. He also said that heat, water, power supplies and phone connections were working normally in Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 * EU member states have agreed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-62287c5f8f087f6d099f412a#block-62287c5f8f087f6d099f412a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new sanctions}}}\uc2  against Russian leaders and oligarchs over the invasion of Ukraine, reports Reuters. The French presidency of the EU said members approved the sanctions at a meeting and that they would be formally adopted by the EU summit on Thursday and Friday in Versailles.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 Russian foreign ministry\uc2  has claimed that its goals in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  would be better {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-622879178f08527b36853b39#block-622879178f08527b36853b39"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 achieved through talks}}}\uc2  and that it does not plan to overthrow the country\u8217\'20\'19s government, reports Reuters. It said about 140,000 Ukrainians had fled to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russia}}}\uc2  and that its actions in Ukraine were strictly following its plan.\par \par \uc2 * Congressional leaders in the US reached a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-622872a98f087f6d099f40d0#block-622872a98f087f6d099f40d0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bipartisan deal}}}\uc2  early this morning to provide $13.6bn to help {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  and European allies. The president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , originally requested $10bn for military, humanitarian and economic aid, but the backing from both parties was so strong that the figure climbed to $12bn on Monday and $13.6bn yesterday.\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s government has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-62286f918f08ec6557dfa3a1#block-62286f918f08ec6557dfa3a1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banned exports}}}\uc2  of rye, barley, buckwheat, millet, sugar, salt, and meat until the end of this year, according to a cabinet resolution published on Wednesday. It will put food security across Europe into sharp focus, leading to shortages of grain and price rises of staples including bread.\par \par \uc2 * Civilians have started leaving Sumy in private cars after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-62286b818f08d38fbc42aaf4#block-62286b818f08d38fbc42aaf4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Chumanitarian corridor\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  was established for a second consecutive day. The mayor of the north-eastern city, Oleksandr Lysenko, made the announcement in televised comments.\par \par \uc2 * EU leaders gathering for a summit in Versailles on Thursday and Friday will say that Russia\u8217\'20\'19s aggression \u8220\'20\'1Cconstitutes a tectonic shift in European history\u8221\'20\'1D, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-62286adb8f0806dde1f8b01d#block-62286adb8f0806dde1f8b01d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 draft communique}}}\uc2  seen by the Guardian. They will decide, the draft statement says, to \u8220\'20\'1Ctake more responsibility for security and take further decisive steps towards building our European sovereignty\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * A Russian airstrike that reportedly killed 47 civilians as they queued for bread in Chernihiv on Thursday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-622867938f08527b36853ab8#block-622867938f08527b36853ab8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may constitute a war crime}}}\uc2 , an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/03/ukraine-russian-dumb-bomb-air-strike-kills-civilians-in-chernihiv-new-investigation-and-testimony/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation}}}\uc2  by Amnesty International has found. At around 12.15pm on 3 March a square was hit by multiple bombs, killing civilians and severely damaging buildings.\par \par \uc2 * The number of people who have fled {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  since the start of the Russian invasion has reached {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-622865438f0806dde1f8affc#block-622865438f0806dde1f8affc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2.1-2.2 million people}}}\uc2 , the UN refugee agency said today. The UN high commissioner for refugees, Filippo Grandi, said during a visit to Stockholm that rather than talking about which countries refugees will go to, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe time is now to try to help at the border\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 * Britain has announced a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-622862668f08527b36853a96#block-622862668f08527b36853a96"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 series of new aviation sanctions}}}\uc2 , giving the government power to detain any Russian aircraft in the UK.\par \par \uc2 * The Ukrainian deputy prime minister has said that Russian armed forces have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-62285d448f08527b36853a77#block-62285d448f08527b36853a77"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed to stop firing}}}\uc2  in areas of humanitarian corridors from 9am to 9pm local time (7am-7pm GMT) today. Iryna Vereshchuk said the evacuation corridors would be open on Wednesday in several areas including Mariupol, but warned Russian forces against shooting in those areas.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s it from me for now. Handing over to Leonie Chao-Fong. Thanks for reading.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 Lumen Technologies, part of the backbone of the internet, pulls out of Russia due to 'increased security risk'\par \par \uc2 Lumen Technologies, one of the companies that comprises the backbone of the internet, said on Tuesday it was pulling the plug on Russia because of an \u8220\'20\'1Cincreased security risk.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It follows a similar move by fellow US firm Cogent Communications which said on Friday that it cutting internet service to Russian clients, raising concerns that Russia will be cut off from news sites and social media platforms based in the west (although the Kremlin has made several moves of its own on that front).\par \par \uc2 Lumen attempted to downplay the impact of the decision, saying in a brief statement it provides \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely small and very limited\u8221\'20\'1D business services in Russia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe decided to disconnect the network due to increased security risk inside Russia,\u8221\'20\'1D the company said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have not yet experienced network disruptions but given the increasingly uncertain environment and the heightened risk of state action, we took this move to ensure the security of our and our customers\u8217\'20\'19 networks, as well as the ongoing integrity of the global Internet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lumen and Cogent are both part of the network that allows data to flow through the infrastructure of the internet. However, access to information sources has been blocked in Russia regardless of Lumen and Cogent\u8217\'20\'19s actions. Facebook and Twitter have been blocked by the Kremlin in the wake of those platforms blocking Russian state news services across Europe. Meanwhile, Twitter is launching a new service on Tor - which allows users to surf the net anonymously - that could help users circumvent the Russia ban. Twitter is launching an \u8220\'20\'1Conion\u8221\'20\'1D service which can be accessed over Tor.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Irish government has just slashed excise duty on fuel to soften the blow of price hikes in the wake of the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 enltrDeal done.\par \par \uc2 An incorporeal cabinet meeting has signed off on\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 ?? 15c cut in excise duty for diesel\par \par \uc2 ?? 20c cut in excise for petrol\par \par \uc2 ?? 2c cut in excise for green diesel\par \par \uc2 Measures to take effect from midnight - pending D\u225\'00\'E1il approval today - until end of August. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VirginMediaNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @VirginMediaNews}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Gavan Reilly (@gavreilly) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/gavreilly/status/1501503735058550800?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 Zelenskiy says threat level at maximum and warns of mass 'humanitarian catastrophe' without no-fly zone\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president, Volodymyr Zelenskiy, has said that the international community would be responsible for a mass \u8220\'20\'1Chumanitarian catastrophe\u8221\'20\'1D if it does not agree a no-fly zone and warned that the country is at maximum threat level.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRussia uses missiles, aircraft and helicopters against us, against civilians, against our cities, against our infrastructure. It is the humanitarian duty of the world to respond,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in his daily televised address, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 He said Ukrainians have shown throughout the last two weeks that they will never give in.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian president, Volodymyr Zelensky, addressing MPs in the British Parliament yesterday via videolink. Photograph: EyePress News/REX/Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 The new EU sanctions ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?page=with:block-62287c5f8f087f6d099f412a#block-62287c5f8f087f6d099f412a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier}}}\uc2  ) will include travel bans and asset freezes for around 100 Russians, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The EU\u8217\'20\'19s top diplomat, Josep Borrell, said a decision could be made later today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMember states are working on a package of sanctions, around 100 people responsible at different levels of government,\u8221\'20\'1D he told the European Parliament in Strasbourg. He said he hoped for agreement \u8220\'20\'1Cby the end of this session today\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 The UK defence minister, Ben Wallace, is to make a statement in parliament on Ukraine, the house of commons leader has announced, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukraine says Russia has disconnected Chernobyl from grid\par \par \uc2 More on Chernobyl, Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s state power operator says that Russian forces have disconnected the nuclear power plant from the grid, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Am image from a handout video by the Russian Defence Ministry purportedly showing a Russian servicemen guard in front of the Chernobyl nuclear power plant in Pripyat, Ukraine on Monday. Photograph: Russian Defence Ministry Press Service/HANDOUT HANDOUT/EPA\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to the UK, Vadym Prystaiko, also called for Britain\u8217\'20\'19s visa requirement to be lifted for refugees.\par \par \uc2 PA reports that he told the Commons home affairs committee:\par \par \uc2 I understand how sensitive it is for your society...how reasonable, how justified it is with your own system, that\u8217\'20\'19s frankly for you to decide. We will be happy if all the barriers are dropped for some period of time when we can get maximum (numbers) of people, then we will deal with that.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian authorities say they do not know what the radiation levels are at Chernobyl nuclear power plant and have no control of Zaporizhzhia since they were seized by Russian troops.\par \par \uc2 The energy minister, Herman Halushchenko, on Wednesday said that Ukraine has not heard about what is happening there since it was seized and that the country has no control over what is happening at the occupied Zaporizhzhia nuclear power plant, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian ambassador to the UK, Vadym Prystaiko, has suggested that fighter jets would be more useful to Ukraine than Britain sending a plane to collect refugees.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether he would like to see a plane travel to Poland or Romania to bring back refugees, PA reports that Vadym Prystaiko told the Commons home affairs committee: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you want to send planes, send F-16s.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said the UK could expect at least 100,000 people coming from Ukraine to the UK to reunite with relatives.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would expect 100,000 - at least - to come here to their relatives, some of them just members of families of your citizens who have no Ukrainian blood but for different reasons they have connections... which we are not aware of,\u8221\'20\'1D he told MPs.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kyiv authorities hope to evacuate many more people from Irpin, Bucha and Hostomel\par \par \uc2 Kyiv authorities hope to evacuate many more people from Irpin, Bucha and Hostomel, the Ukrainian capital\u8217\'20\'19s deputy mayor said today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have places to house (refugees), we have trains to send people west,\u8221\'20\'1D Mykola Povoroznyk, said on television, reports Reuters. But, he added, it was unclear how many people they would be able to help escape.\par \par \uc2 He also said that heat, water, power supplies and phone connections are working normally in Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s territorial defence force help evacuate an elderly woman from Irpin, near Kyiv, yesterday. Photograph: Heidi Levine/SIPA/REX/Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 EU member states agree new sanctions package against Russia and exclude 3 Belarus banks from Swift\par \par \uc2 EU member states have agreed new sanctions against Russian leaders and oligarchs over its invasion of Ukraine, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The French presidency of the EU said members approved the sanctions at a meeting and that they will be formally adopted by the EU Summit on Thursday and Friday in Versailles.\par \par \uc2 They said the new measures clarify questions over cryptocurrencies, exclude three Belarus banks from Swift and target the maritime sector.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 Russia claims would prefer to reach its goals in Ukraine through talks and does not plan to overthrow government\par \par \uc2 The Russian foreign ministry has claimed that its goals in Ukraine would be better achieved through talks and that it does not plan to overthrow the country\u8217\'20\'19s government, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 It said about 140,000 Ukrainians have fled to Russia and that its actions in Ukraine is strictly following its plan.\par \par \uc2 Maria Zakharova, a Russian foreign ministry spokesperson, said its goal is for Ukraine to have neutral status, which it would prefer to attain through talks, and that it hopes to make more significant progress in the next round.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 The UK transport secretary, Grant Shapps, has warned against British soldiers traveling to Ukraine to illegally fight, saying it is a \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous situation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He told ITV\u8217\'20\'19s Good Morning Britain:\par \par \uc2 You cannot go and fight if you\u8217\'20\'19re in the British Army, you cannot just get up and go and fight. Of course that\u8217\'20\'19s inappropriate behaviour and you would expect the army to have some very, very strict rules in place, as they do.\par \par \uc2 Asked what Russia might do if a British soldier was captured or killed, PA reports that Shapps said:\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a big difference between Britain sending its army in and some people who are breaking with our law and going to do it.\par \par \uc2 But, clearly, this is a dangerous situation. And clearly, we want to make sure that the assistance we\u8217\'20\'19re providing is done in an official way - like the anti-tank missiles that we provided prior to and during this conflict, and like the 22,000 Ukrainians that we\u8217\'20\'19ve trained.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 US congressional leaders reach bipartisan deal for $13.6bn in aid for Ukraine and European allies\par \par \uc2 Congressional leaders in the US reached a bipartisan deal early this morning to provide $13.6bn to help Ukraine and European allies, reports the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 President Joe Biden originally requested $10bn for military, humanitarian and economic aid, but the backing from both parties was so strong that the figure climbed to $12bn on Monday and $13.6bn yesterday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to support them against tyranny, oppression, violent acts of subjugation,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said at the White House.\par \par \uc2 Party leaders are hoping to get the 2,741-page measure through the House today and the Senate by the end of the week, but the timing of the latter remains unclear.\par \par \uc2 US president Joe Biden speaking yesterday in the White House as he announced a ban on US imports of Russian oil and gas. Photograph: Jim Watson/AFP/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 International students and Ukrainians were among those who managed to escape Sumy by train last night after two weeks trapped under fire in a basement with insufficient food.\par \par \uc2 Around 7,000 people were safely evacuated yesterday, the BBC\u8217\'20\'19s Sarah Rainsford reports.\par \par \uc2 enltrInternational students & Ukrainians crammed onto evacuation trains late last night after 2 weeks trapped under fire in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Sumy?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Sumy}}}\uc2 . Manisa described 'miserable' days in a basement:'we were starving' she said\par \par \uc2 c 7000 people were evacuated safely yesterday; a 2nd corridor's planned today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9rZEpZz43V"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9rZEpZz43V}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sarah Rainsford (@sarahrainsford) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sarahrainsford/status/1501486346648670208?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukraine bans exports of rye, barley, buckwheat, millet, sugar and meat until end of year\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s government has banned exports of rye, barley, buckwheat, millet, sugar, salt, and meat until the end of this year, according to a cabinet resolution published on Wednesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/ukraine-bans-exports-several-grains-sugar-salt-meat-2022-03-09/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters has reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It will put food security across Europe into sharp focus, leading to shortages of grain and price rices of staples including bread.\par \par \uc2 Russia and Ukraine combined are responsible for about 30% of the world\u8217\'20\'19s wheat and barley exports.\par \par \uc2 Ireland\u8217\'20\'19s agriculture minister Charlie McConalogue told RTE that farmers, many dairy and beef producers, should consider growing grain this year. He said the country imports 60% of its grain.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 Exiled Belarus opposition leader, Sviatlana Tsikhanouskaya, is in London today meeting with representatives of the UK government to discuss support for the Belarusian anti-war movement and free media, she says.\par \par \uc2 enltrStarting my visit to London this morning. With {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FCDOGovUK?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FCDOGovUK}}}\uc2  & {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UKParliament?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @UKParliament}}}\uc2  leadership, diplomats, I will discuss support for the Belarusian anti-war movement & our free media. It's also crucial to impose harsh sanctions against the regime involved in Russia's invasion of Ukraine. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uveYywMJPp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uveYywMJPp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sviatlana Tsikhanouskaya (@Tsihanouskaya) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Tsihanouskaya/status/1501483288334114824?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a recent interview with Tsikhanouskaya by the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s associate editor for Europe, Katherine Butler:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/06/belarus-has-effectively-ceded-control-to-kremlin-says-opposition-leader-sviatlana-tsikhanouskaya"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alexander Lukashenko has effectively ceded control to Kremlin, say opposition }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Poland is ready to supply MiG-29 fighter jets to Ukraine - but only within the framework of Nato, an adviser to the president has said.\par \par \uc2 It comes after the US rejected a proposal to provide Washington with Polish planes, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe USA does not want these planes to come to Ukraine from American bases,\u8221\'20\'1D Jakub Kumoch, an adviser to Andrzej Duda, told public broadcaster TVP Info. \u8220\'20\'1CPoland is ready to act, but only within the framework of the alliance, within the framework of NATO.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ukraine has asked western countries to provide fighter jets to respond to the Russian invasion. But yesterday, after Poland said it was ready to deploy all of its MIG-29 jets to Ramstein airbase in Germany for the US and urged other Nato members to do the same, the Pentagon dismissed the offer as not \u8220\'20\'1Ctenable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57am GMT\par \par \uc2 Civilians start leaving Sumy in cars\par \par \uc2 Civilians have started leaving Sumy in private cars after a \u8220\'20\'1Chumanitarian corridor\u8221\'20\'1D was established for a second consecutive day.\par \par \uc2 The mayor or the northeastern city, Oleksandr Lysenko, made the announcement in televised comments, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 EU leaders to say Russia's aggression marks 'tectonic shift' in European history\par \par \uc2 EU leaders gathering for a summit in Versailles on Thursday and Friday will say that Russia\u8217\'20\'19s aggression \u8220\'20\'1Cconstitutes a tectonic shift in European history\u8221\'20\'1D, according to a draft communique seen by The Guardian.\par \par \uc2 They will decide, the draft statement says, to \u8220\'20\'1Ctake more responsibility for security and take further decisive steps towards building our European sovereignty\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On defence, the leaders are expected to agree to \u8220\'20\'1Cresolutely bolster... investment in defence capabilities and innovative technologies\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cincrease substantially defence expenditures\u8221\'20\'1D. They will collaborate more and take steps to \u8220\'20\'1Cstrengthen and develop our defence industry\u8221\'20\'1D. There will be a commitment to continue to help Ukraine by purchasing lethal weapons for use in the war with Russia.\par \par \uc2 On energy, they will agree to phase out dependency on Russian gas, oil and coal imports\u8221\'20\'1D by accelerating transition from fossil fuels, diversifying energy supply through liquified natural gas shipments, biogas and hydrogen and improving energy efficiencies and storage supplies.\par \par \uc2 Not contained within the communique is any mention of the EU membership applications made in recent days by Ukraine, Moldova and Georgia. A separate intervention on this issue is expected with the EU member states divided on how best to answer the calls.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 Attack on Ukrainians as they queued for bread may constitute war crime - Amnesty International\par \par \uc2 A Russian air strike that reportedly killed 47 civilians as they queued for bread in Chernihiv on Thursday may constitute a war crime, an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/03/ukraine-russian-dumb-bomb-air-strike-kills-civilians-in-chernihiv-new-investigation-and-testimony/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigation}}}\uc2  by Amnesty International has found.\par \par \uc2 At around 12.15pm on 3 March a square was hit by multiple bombs, killing civilians and severely damaging buildings.\par \par \uc2 Analysis by the NGO\u8217\'20\'19s crisis response team has concluded that the attack was most likely a Russian air strike that used at least 8 unguided aerial bombs known as \u8220\'20\'1Cdumb bombs\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Alina, a 21-year-old student who lives nearby with her family told Amnesty International:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI heard a very, very loud buzzing, and I felt our building shaking. It was as if our flat was inflating\u8230\'20\'26 And then after two seconds, I heard the windows get blown out into the courtyard. Our building shook a lot; I thought there would be no walls left.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I heard the buzz, I called my grandma into the corridor with me. We laid on the ground and that\u8217\'20\'19s likely what saved us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said her parents, who also survived, had been in the line for bread but decided to leave because the queue was too long. \u8220\'20\'1CThe people who were in that line are no more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Oksana Pokalchuk, director at Amnesty Ukraine, today said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe attack should be investigated as a war crime.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr? New investigation from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/amnesty?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @amnesty}}}\uc2  confirms Russian attack on 3 March killed civilians in Chernihiv as they queued for bread.\par \par \uc2 The attack should be investigated as a war crime. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NeJukCmpv6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/NeJukCmpv6}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Oksana Pokalchuk (@OPokalchuk) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/OPokalchuk/status/1501477041174192130?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 The race to save Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s cultural heritage. Luke Harding in Lviv and Harriet Sherwood report:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we lose our culture we lose our identity,\u8221\'20\'1D said Onyschenko, the head of Lviv\u8217\'20\'19s city council heritage protection office. \u8220\'20\'1CLviv has always been multicultural. Poles, Germans, Jews, Armenians and Hungarians built it. It\u8217\'20\'19s Unesco listed.\u8221\'20\'1D She said she and her colleagues were working their way through a long list of objects that needed to be protected.\par \par \uc2 Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  has been an all-round disaster. Its army had shelled densely populated cities, killing hundreds. More than 2 million refugees have fled abroad in Europe\u8217\'20\'19s biggest exodus since the second world war. In besieged Mariupol, families have spent more than a week living in desperate conditions without heat, water or power.\par \par \uc2 Alongside this humanitarian catastrophe, cultural assets have been bombed and damaged. They include a museum in the city of Ivankiv, north-west of Kyiv, which housed dozens of works by the Ukrainian folk artist Maria Prymachenko, some now lost forever. Last week Russian forces shelled the assumption cathedral in Kharkiv, hurling debris into its nave.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/ukrainians-in-race-to-save-a-nations-cultural-heritage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukrainians in race to save cultural heritage}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Refugees fleeing Ukraine reaches 2.1-2.2m, says UN\par \par \uc2 The number of people who have fled Ukraine since the start of the Russian invasion has reached 2.1-2.2m people, the United Nation\u8217\'20\'19s refugee agency said today.\par \par \uc2 The UN high commissioner for refugees, Filippo Grandi, said during a visit to Stockholm that rather than talking about which countries refugees will go to, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe time is now to try to help at the border\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Grandi said Moldova, which is not in the EU, is especially vulnerable in the crisis.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian refugees in Palanca, Moldova, yesterday. Photograph: Ciro Fusco/ANSA/ZUMA Press/REX/Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 UK announces new aviation sanctions on Russia\par \par \uc2 Britain has announced a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.uk/government/news/uk-strengthens-ban-on-russia-aircraft-and-introduces-new-trade-sanctions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 series of new aviation sanctions}}}\uc2 , giving the government power to detain any Russian aircraft in the UK.\par \par \uc2 Making the announcement, the UK foreign secretary, Liz Truss said:\par \par \uc2 enltrBanning Russian flagged planes from the UK and making it a criminal offence to fly them will inflict more economic pain on Russia and those close to the Kremlin. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aSpZdHCAvX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/aSpZdHCAvX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Liz Truss (@trussliz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/trussliz/status/1501469575627558914?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 The sanctions will enable the UK to do the following:\par \par \uc2 * Detain Russian aircraft and remove aircraft belonging to designated individuals and entities from the UK register.\par \par \uc2 * Ban export of aviation and space-related goods and technology, including technical assistance.\par \par \uc2 * Further ban UK companies providing insurance and re-insurance services in relation to these goods and technology.\par \par \uc2 It comes after the UK transport secretary, Grant Shapps, last night said he had made it a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2022/mar/08/russian-planes-that-enter-uk-airspace-could-be-detained-by-government"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminal offence }}}\uc2  for any Russian aircraft to enter UK airspace, tweeting: \u8220\'20\'1CWe will suffocate Putin\u8217\'20\'19s cronies\u8217\'20\'19 ability to continue living as normal while thousands of innocent people die.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 China has accused Nato of pushing tensions between Russia and Ukraine to \u8220\'20\'1Cbreaking point\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 At a daily news briefing, Chinese foreign ministry spokesperson Zhao Lijian urged the US to take China\u8217\'20\'19s concerns seriously and avoid undermining its rights or interests in handling the situation in Ukraine and ties with Russia, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukraine says Russia has agreed to ceasefire on humanitarian corridors from 9am to 9pm\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian deputy prime minister has said that Russian armed forces have agreed to stop firing in areas of humanitarian corridors from 9am to 9pm local time (7am-7pm GMT) today, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Iryna Vereshchuk said the evacuation corridors will be open on Wednesday in several areas including Mariupol, but warned Russian forces against shooting in those areas.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the latest images from Ukraine and Poland, where most refugees have fled:\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian refugees sleep in a temporary shelter in an abandoned Tesco supermarket in Przemysl, Poland yesterday. Photograph: Omar Marques/Getty Images Soldiers arrive to reinforce one of the final checkpoints before the frontlines where Ukrainian forces were battling Russian forces near Brovary, Ukraine yesterday. Photograph: Marcus Yam/LOS ANGELES TIMES/REX/Shutterstock A child is carried by a member of the Ukrainian defence force as residents of Iripin attempted to flee the city yesterday. Photograph: Dia Images/Getty Images Ukrainian refugees sleeping at a train station in Prezmysl, Poland today. Photograph: Daniel Cole/AP\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 22 people - including three children - reportedly killed on Monday in Sumy\par \par \uc2 Twenty-two people - including three children - were reportedly killed on Monday in a Russian airstrike in Sumy.\par \par \uc2 Sumy\u8217\'20\'19s regional governor, Dmytro Zhyvytskyi, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/world-europe-60657155?ns_mchannel=social&ns_source=twitter&ns_campaign=bbc_live&ns_linkname=622852dbec502b53cd4814f8%2622%20people%20killed%20in%20Russian%20air%20strike%20in%20Sumy%262022-03-09T07%3A29%3A13.415Z&ns_fee=0&pinned_post_locator=urn:asset:75e45910-a906-4bb4-97c4-3095f741603b&pinned_post_asset_id=622852dbec502b53cd4814f8&pinned_post_type=share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the BBC}}}\uc2  that Russia bombed a residential area in the north-east of the city overnight, accusing them of \u8220\'20\'1Cmass murder\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He told BBC Ukrainian: \u8220\'20\'1CThree bombs in one evening... It was a terrible night.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nine people in a single house were reportedly killed, six houses completely destroyed and around 20 more partially so.\par \par \uc2 Around 5,000 people have been evacuated from the city after a pause in bombardment to open up a humanitarian corridor.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 Russia warns it is working on 'swift' response to western sanctions\par \par \uc2 Russia has warned that it is working on a broad response to western sanctions that it claimed would be \u8216\'20\'18swift\u8217\'20\'19 and felt in the most sensitive areas, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRussia\u8217\'20\'19s reaction will be swift, thoughtful and sensitive for those it addresses,\u8221\'20\'1D Dmitry Birichevsky, the director of the foreign ministry\u8217\'20\'19s department for economic cooperation, said, according to the RIA news agency.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 Scepticism as Russia claims it will provide humanitarian corridors\par \par \uc2 Russia has again claimed it will provide humanitarian corridors today for Ukrainians fleeing Kyiv, Chernihiv, Sumy, Kharkiv and Mariupol, saying forces would \u8220\'20\'1Cobserve a regime of silence\u8221\'20\'1D from 9am in Ukraine (7am GMT).\par \par \uc2 It comes as the biggest refugee crisis in Europe since world war two surpassed two million.\par \par \uc2 However, as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Julian Borger and Patrick Wintour report, authorities in Kyiv have previously accused Moscow of shelling a refugee corridor intended for residents trying to escape Mariupol. It was also unclear whether the proposed routes would pass through Russia or Belarus, conditions previously opposed by the Ukrainian government.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe enemy has launched an attack heading exactly at the humanitarian corridor,\u8221\'20\'1D the Ukrainian defence ministry said on Facebook on Tuesday, adding that the Russian army \u8220\'20\'1Cdid not let children, women and elderly people leave the city\u8221\'20\'1D. The International Committee of the Red Cross said many Mariupol residents face an \u8220\'20\'1Capocalyptic\u8221\'20\'1D situation, with no water, power or heating.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s deputy prime minister said 5,000 civilians were evacuated from the Sumy region yesterday, where 21 people were killed in airstrikes.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/08/poland-mig-29-jets-us-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US dismisses Polish plan to provide fighter jets to be sent to Ukraine}}}\par \par \uc2 Hi, I will be looking after the liveblog for the next few hours. Please get in touch with any tips or suggestions: miranda.bryant@guardian.co.uk\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Good morning to our readers who are just tuning in. We\u8217\'20\'19ve been tracking the latest from Ukraine overnight as the situation continues to unfold.\par \par \uc2 Here are the main developments from the past few hours:\par \par \uc2 * Ukrainians looking to escape shelling could have a chance to evacuate after Russian forces said they will still firing from 10am Moscow time to provide humanitarian corridors out of Kyiv and four other cities. Several previous ceasefire promises have not been kept, however.\par \par \uc2 * The UK Ministry of Defence says in its latest update that Russia is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-6228458e8f08ec6557dfa2bf#block-6228458e8f08ec6557dfa2bf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struggling to breakthrough to the north of Kyiv}}}\uc2  while Ukrainian defence forces continue to shoot down Russian aircraft.\par \par \uc2 * The International Atomic Energy Agency has lost contact with safeguard monitoring systems at Chernobyl and has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/09/ukraine-news-russia-war-ceasefire-broken-humanitarian-corridors-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-622830fd8f0806dde1f8aee2#block-622830fd8f0806dde1f8aee2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed concern about}}}\uc2  the welfare of over 200 workers and guards at the facility.\par \par \uc2 * The US government has dismissed as \u8220\'20\'1Cuntenable\u8221\'20\'1D a suggestion by Poland that it could make 29 of its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/08/poland-mig-29-jets-us-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Soviet-era MIG fighter jets available}}}\uc2  to the Americans to help defend Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 * But the US will be sending two Patriot anti-missile batteries stationed in Europe to Poland to bolster its defences against attack.\par \par \uc2 * Russia\u8217\'20\'19s military is solving some of its logistical problems and could launch an attack on Kyiv within days, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/08/russia-solving-logistics-problems-and-could-attack-kyiv-within-days-experts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to experts}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president Volodymyr Zelenskiyhas been described as a hero by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/we-will-fight-until-the-end-how-the-papers-covered-zelenskiys-commons-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 British press}}}\uc2  after he invoked the fight against Nazism {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/08/zelenskiy-invokes-churchill-calls-on-uk-do-more-help-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  in an impassioned video address }}}\uc2  to MPs to do more to help protect his country.\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine accused Russia of breaking a ceasefire agreemen t, by shelling a route intended to allow civilians {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/08/ukraine-war-civilians-sumy-irpin-refugees-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to escape the besieged city of Mariupol}}}\uc2 . Residents of the port city are living without heat, water, sanitary systems or phones.\par \par \uc2 * The US is banning imports of Russian oil \u8220\'20\'1Cto inflict further pain on Vladimir Putin\u8221\'20\'1D, Joe Biden has said. The EU has not joined the ban, but the British government promised to phase out Russian oil imports {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/08/ukraine-news-russia-war-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-latest-updates?page=with:block-622784718f08d64fa95e8a90#block-622784718f08d64fa95e8a90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by the end of the year}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine is being bolstered by $285m in daily oil payments from European countries, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/08/ukraine-news-russia-war-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-latest-updates?page=with:block-6227d6e58f08ec6557dfa077#block-6227d6e58f08ec6557dfa077"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  a thinktank has found}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Venezuelahas released at least two Americans from jail in an apparent goodwill gesture toward the Biden administration following a visit to Caracas by a high-level US delegation.\par \par \uc2 * Chinese president Xi Jinping called for \u8220\'20\'1Cmaximum restraint\u8221\'20\'1D in Ukraine overnight and said China is \u8220\'20\'1Cpained to see the flames of war reignited in Europe\u8221\'20\'1D in his strongest statement to date on the conflict.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 The British papers have lapped up Volodymyr Zelenskiy\u8217\'20\'19s speech to the House of Commons yesterday in which the Ukrainian president deliberately invoked the spirit of Winston Churchill to act as a rallying cry for more help for his embattled nation.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Martin Farrer has had a look at the front pages and has this story:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/we-will-fight-until-the-end-how-the-papers-covered-zelenskiys-commons-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We will fight until the end\u8217\'20\'19: how the papers covered Zelenskiy\u8217\'20\'19s Commons speech}}}\par \par \uc2 And if you want a bit of a reminder of what Zelenskiy said, here\u8217\'20\'19s a video of his address:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 Russians struggling to breakthrough north of Kyiv, says MoD\par \par \uc2 Russia forces have failed to make a significant breakthrough to the north of Kyiv, and Ukrainian forces appear to be succeeding in shooting down enemy planes, according to the latest battleground intelligence update from Britain\u8217\'20\'19s Ministry of Defence.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian soldiers near Brovary on the outskirts of Kyiv. Photograph: Marcus Yam/LOS ANGELES TIMES/REX/Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 It said on Twitter: \u8220\'20\'1CFighting north-west of Kyiv remains ongoing with Russian forces failing to make any significant breakthroughs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUkrainian air defences appear to have enjoyed considerable success against Russia\u8217\'20\'19s modern combat aircraft, probably preventing them achieving any degree of control of the air.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrLatest Defence Intelligence update on the situation in Ukraine - 09 March 2022\par \par \uc2 Find out more about the UK government's response: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DjAjI4vbCk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/DjAjI4vbCk}}}\par \par \uc2 ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/StandWithUkraine?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #StandWithUkraine}}}\uc2  ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/eAqudcHW05"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/eAqudcHW05}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ministry of Defence ???? (@DefenceHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DefenceHQ/status/1501438467103989762?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 However, it added that \u8220\'20\'1CKharkiv, Chernihiv, Sumy and Mariupol remain encircled by Russian forces and continue to suffer heavy Russian shelling\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 Russian foreign minister Sergei Lavrov will travel to Turkey on Wednesday for talks with his Ukrainian counterpart, Dmytro Kuleba, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The diplomats will meet at the resort city of Antalya after repeated offers by Turkey to host talks and mediate between the two sides.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 The New York Times will have no reporters on the ground in Russia for the first time in a century after the news organisation joined those pulling out of the country.\par \par \uc2 Russian authorities made reporting from the country impossible when it recently criminalised the act of describing Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine as a \u8220\'20\'1Cwar\u8221\'20\'1D with those who commit the offence facing up to 15 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 As a result Russian media outlets have been forced to close, while global news organisations have pulled out their teams owing to the risk of arrest.\par \par \uc2 Former NYT Moscow bureau chief, Neil MacFarquhar, said on social media Russia has always been considered a \u8220\'20\'1Cimportant country, an important story\u8221\'20\'1D but the recent turn. had \u8220\'20\'1Cjust killed off that long tradition\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve had reporters there continuously since 1921, with one or two short interruptions due to visa hiccoughs. Not Stalin, not the Cold War, nothing drove us out,\u8221\'20\'1D MacFarquhar said.\par \par \uc2 enltrVery sad day for the history of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nytimes?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @nytimes}}}\uc2  in Moscow. Pulling all its correspondents out of the country. We have had reporters there continuously since 1921, with one or two short interruptions due to visa hiccoughs. Not Stalin, not the Cold War, nothing drove us out. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LcSwFqeAeU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LcSwFqeAeU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Neil MacFarquhar (@NeilMacFarquhar)\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NeilMacFarquhar/status/1501234123297505281?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrIt criminalized calling Russia's invasion of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Ukraine?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Ukraine}}}\uc2  what it was, a war, mandating up to 15 years in prison. That made it impossible for real reporters to work. So after 100 years, the Times withdrew its staff.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Neil MacFarquhar (@NeilMacFarquhar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NeilMacFarquhar/status/1501237548932292612?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrVery sad day for the history of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nytimes?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @nytimes}}}\uc2  in Moscow. Pulling all its correspondents out of the country. We have had reporters there continuously since 1921, with one or two short interruptions due to visa hiccoughs. Not Stalin, not the Cold War, nothing drove us out. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LcSwFqeAeU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LcSwFqeAeU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Neil MacFarquhar (@NeilMacFarquhar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NeilMacFarquhar/status/1501234123297505281?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 8, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 Some images from the evacuation of Sumy:\par \par \uc2 Civilians flee Sumy the city after temporary ceasefire announced on 8 March Photograph: Anadolu Agency/Getty Images Civilians flee Sumy Photograph: Anadolu Agency/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 Regional governor Dmytro Zhyvytskyy said a humanitarian corridor out of the besieged Ukrainian city of Sumy will continue to function on Wednesday, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 About 5,000 people rode buses out of the northeastern city on Tuesday after Moscow and Kyiv agreed on the corridor.\par \par \uc2 Zhyvytskyy said about 1,000 cars were also able to leave, moving towards the city of Poltava.\par \par \uc2 The successful evacuation comes days after New York Times reporters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/03/06/world/europe/ukrainian-family-killed-war.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 witnessed}}}\uc2  a Russian mortar strike in the city of Irpin that killed four people, including a mother and her teenage son and eight-year-old daughter, as they attempted to flee to safety in Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian general staff says it continues to hold Kyiv despite attacks by Russian forces overnight while fighting continues across the country.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/100069073844828/posts/271970551782071/?d=n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest update}}}\uc2  says there is fighting in the north and north-west with \u8220\'20\'1Ccombat operations\u8221\'20\'1D taking place in Polisky and Volyn, along Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s border. It also says there is also fighting in the settlements of Nizhyn, Ivanytsia, Trostyanets and also in the city of Chernihiv.\par \par \uc2 Soldiers at a checkpoint near the frontlines where Ukrainian forces are battling invading Russian forces at Brovary. Photograph: Marcus Yam/LOS ANGELES TIMES/REX/Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 In the south it says operations are continuing to secure \u8220\'20\'1Cairports and critical infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D, while the Ukrainian airforce is targeting artillery shelling civilian ares while providing air cover.\par \par \uc2 The update also alleges a propaganda campaign is underway to \u8220\'20\'1Caimed at discrediting the military and political leadership of our state\u8221\'20\'1D and that Russian forces have taken up firing positions next to hospitals in Chernihiv.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 IAEA loses contact with safeguard monitoring systems at Chernobyl\par \par \uc2 The International Atomic Energy Agency says it has lost contact with Chernobyl nuclear data systems as the plant is no longer transmitting to the UN\u8217\'20\'19s atomic watchdog.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iaea.org/newscenter/pressreleases/update-15-iaea-director-general-statement-on-situation-in-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on Tuesday, IAEA director general Rafael Mariano Grossi said \u8220\'20\'1Cremote data transmission from safeguards monitoring systems installed at the Chernobyl NPP had been lost,\u8221\'20\'1D and that the agency was currently \u8220\'20\'1Clooking into the status of safeguards monitoring systems in other locations in Ukraine \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Grossi also raised concerns about the well-being of 210 technical personnel and guards at the plant when Russian forces seized control two weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 The agency could only reach the plant by email and the staff had not been rotated out, which is \u8220\'20\'1Ccrucial for nuclear safety\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m deeply concerned about the difficult and stressful situation facing staff at the Chornobyl nuclear power plant and the potential risks this entails for nuclear safety. I call on the forces in effective control of the site to urgently facilitate the safe rotation of personnel there,\u8221\'20\'1D Grossi said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 Investors are turning to clean energy stocks as Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine threatens to further raise oil prices and highlights Europe\u8217\'20\'19s dependence on Russian oil and gas.\par \par \uc2 US markets are closed right now but on the Australian exchange the price of the Global Clean Energy ETF offered by VanEck, which tracks the price of big renewable energy companies that are on an index maintained by S&P, is up more than 8% so far today.\par \par \uc2 The index itself was up 5.6% overnight.\par \par \uc2 The Russian market, which is heavy with oil and gas companies, has already been devastated by sanctions imposed by the US and European countries, although so far western powers have steered clear of doing anything that could stop customers paying for Russian oil and gas.\par \par \uc2 The Australian securities exchange in Sydney. Photograph: Lisa Maree Williams/Getty Images\par \par \uc2 Russia itself is also about to default on its sovereign debt due to the sanctions and the threat of more to come, ratings agency Fitch said.\par \par \uc2 VanEck senior associate Alice Shen said the US\u8217\'20\'19s decision to ban imports of Russian oil could further boost prices, adding to the attractiveness of renewables.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis trend towards clean energy stocks too will likely gain momentum as energy consumers seek substitutes for fossil fuels and the demand for renewable energy rises to meet climate change carbon emissions targets,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Russia-Ukraine war highlights the vulnerability of countries that rely on fossil fuels, arguably raising the importance of clean energy as an energy supply and it could be an important impetus for the acceleration to clean energy globally.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 Sumy mayor Dmytro Zhyvytskyi says one person has been killed, fourteen missing and others missing following shelling in Okhtyr overnight.\par \par \uc2 Posting photos of the damage to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/Zhyvytskyy/posts/377073484420957"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social media}}}\uc2 , he reported that civilian infrastructure had been targeted including a railway station, executive committee building, local department stores and shops.\par \par \uc2 Zhyvytskyi said the city is without power, water and has experienced disruption to its sewerage system.\par \par \uc2 Humanitarian corridors from Sumy were opened overnight to allow residents caught in the fighting to flee.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 It is a new morning in Kyiv but residents in the Ukrainian capital have been greeted with air raid sirens and explosions.\par \par \uc2 enltrLoud series of explosions heard from Kyiv and surrounding area right now. Kyiv city just put out another siren alert to seek shelter immediately. The explosions have been incessant for three minutes.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Christopher Miller (@ChristopherJM) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChristopherJM/status/1501408353242734596?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 March 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 Any strike against supply lines from Nato members supporting Ukraine with arms and ammunition will be considered an escalation of the conflict, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbc.ca/news/politics/ukraine-russia-putin-stoltenberg-nato-1.6377675"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBC News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nato\u8217\'20\'19s secretary general Jens Stoltenberg said on Tuesday that while supply lines inside Ukraine were vulnerable to attack, those leading up to the border fell under the protection of the alliance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAn attack on Nato territory, on Nato forces, Nato capabilities, that would be an attack on Nato,\u8221\'20\'1D Stoltenberg said.\par \par \uc2 There have been concern among some in US intelligence services that Russia may attempt to stem the flow of support to Ukraine with an airstrike or long-range artillery.\par \par \uc2 Article 5 of Nato\u8217\'20\'19s founding treaty states that an attack on one member state is an attack on all 30 members.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 Welcome\par \par \uc2 Hello \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19m Royce Kurmelovs and welcome to our rolling coverage of the Ukraine-Russia war.\par \par \uc2 Here are the main developments in the past few hours:\par \par \uc2 * The US government has dismissed as \u8220\'20\'1Cuntenable\u8221\'20\'1D a suggestion by Poland that it could make 29 of its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/08/poland-mig-29-jets-us-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Soviet-era MIG fighter jets available}}}\uc2  to the Americans to help defend Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 * But the US will be sending two Patriot anti-missile batteries stationed in Europe to Poland to bolster its defences against attack.\par \par \uc2 * Russian forces say they will stop firing starting 10 am Moscow time on Wednesday and are ready to provide human corridors so civilians can evacuate Kyiv and four other cities.\par \par \uc2 * Russia\u8217\'20\'19s military is solving some of its logistical problems and could launch an attack on Kyiv within days, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/08/russia-solving-logistics-problems-and-could-attack-kyiv-within-days-experts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to experts}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president Volodymyr Zelenskiyhas been described as a hero by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/09/we-will-fight-until-the-end-how-the-papers-covered-zelenskiys-commons-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  British press}}}\uc2  after he invoked the fight against Nazism {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/08/zelenskiy-invokes-churchill-calls-on-uk-do-more-help-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  in an impassioned video address }}}\uc2  to MPs to do more to help protect his country.\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine accused Russia of breaking a ceasefire agreemen t, by shelling a route intended to allow civilians {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/mar/08/ukraine-war-civilians-sumy-irpin-refugees-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to escape the besieged city of Mariupol}}}\uc2 . Residents of the port city are living without heat, water, sanitary systems or phones.\par \par \uc2 * The US is banning imports of Russian oil \u8220\'20\'1Cto inflict further pain on Vladimir Putin\u8221\'20\'1D, Joe Biden has said. The EU has not joined the ban, but the British government promised to phase out Russian oil imports {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/08/ukraine-news-russia-war-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-latest-updates?page=with:block-622784718f08d64fa95e8a90#block-622784718f08d64fa95e8a90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by the end of the year}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine is being bolstered by $285m in daily oil payments from European countries, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2022/mar/08/ukraine-news-russia-war-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-kyiv-russian-invasion-live-latest-updates?page=with:block-6227d6e58f08ec6557dfa077#block-6227d6e58f08ec6557dfa077"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  a thinktank has found}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * Venezuelahas released at least two Americans from jail in an apparent goodwill gesture toward the Biden administration following a visit to Caracas by a high-level US delegation.\par \par \uc2 * Chinese president Xi Jinping called for \u8220\'20\'1Cmaximum restraint\u8221\'20\'1D in Ukraine overnight and said China is \u8220\'20\'1Cpained to see the flames of war reignited in Europe\u8221\'20\'1D in his strongest statement to date on the conflict.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 2022-03-09T04:09:32Z 2022-03-10T04:57:33Z {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://media.guim.co.uk/9be01e731f3c0c68567f6c342164e97081a8340c/0_222_5000_3001/500.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://media.guim.co.uk/9be01e731f3c0c68567f6c342164e97081a8340c/0_222_5000_3001/500.jpg}}}\uc2  A serviceman helping carry a woman\u8217\'20\'19s child during an evacuation in Irpin, Ukraine. A mother and her baby seen during an evacuation on Wednesday. Servicemen carry a baby to safety as the UN refugee agency UNHCR estimates the total number of Ukrainian refugees at 2.1 to 2.2 million. A Starstreak HVM (High Velocity Missile) surface-to-air missile system on display in an undated handout photo issued by the UK ministry of defence. The seal for the International Monetary Fund (IMF) in Washington, DC. USA Children and mothers rush to board trains heading to Poland from Lviv, Ukraine A pregnant woman is carried on a stretcher bed as she is evacuated from a children hospital in Mariupol, southeastern Ukraine, following Russia army bombardment. An injured pregnant woman walks downstairs in the damaged by shelling maternity hospital in Mariupol, Ukraine. A Russian attack has severely damaged a maternity hospital in the besieged port city of Mariupol. Emergency employees work at the site of the damaged maternity hospital in Mariupol. People fleeing advancing Russian forces file across wooden planks crossing Irpin River below a destroyed bridge as Russia\u8217\'20\'19s attack on Ukraine continues in Irpin. People attempt to board a train leaving the Kyiv station, Ukraine. Customers visit McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s in Moscow, Russia. McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s announced it would temporarily close all 847 of its restaurants in Russia. Ukrainian servicemen carry a baby stroller after crossing the Irpin river on an improvised path under a bridge, that was destroyed by Ukrainian troops designed to slow any Russian military advance, while assisting people fleeing the town of Irpin, Ukraine. Ukrainian emergency employees work at the side of the maternity hospital in Mariupol damaged by shelling. A car burns at the side of the hospital. A woman walks outside the hospital. A woman is assisted to cross the Irpin river on an improvised path under a bridge, that was destroyed by Ukrainian troops designed to slow any Russian military advance, while fleeing the town of Irpin, Ukraine. A member of the Ukrainian security forces hands over a girl to a man as civilians wait to board a train in Odesa. A lion from an animal shelter in Kyiv is seen in a cage at Natuurhulpcentrum nature centre in Oudsbergen, Belgium after its planned transfer procedures were accelerated following Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine. Kamala Harris arrives to board Air Force Two at Joint Base Andrews in Maryland today for a three-day trip to Poland and Romania for meetings about Ukraine. Newly arrived refugees seek assistance from Polish army soldiers after crossing the border from Ukraine into Poland at the Medyka border crossing, eastern Poland. Soldiers arrive to reinforce one of the final checkpoints before the frontlines where Ukrainian forces are battling invading Russian forces near Brovary, Ukraine. A person is carried in Romanivka, Ukraine. A man and his dog walk past a fire caused by a Russian bombardment on a storage facility, sending a dark plume of smoke into the forested area on the edge of Kalynivka, Ukraine. Ukrainian president, Volodymyr Zelensky, addressing MPs in the British Parliament yesterday via videolink. Am image from a handout video by the Russian Defence Ministry purportedly showing a Russian servicemen guard in front of the Chernobyl nuclear power plant in Pripyat, Ukraine on Monday. Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s territorial defence force help evacuate an elderly woman from Irpin, near Kyiv, yesterday. US president Joe Biden speaking yesterday in the White House as he announced a ban on US imports of Russian oil and gas. Ukrainian refugees in Palanca, Moldova, yesterday. Ukrainian refugees sleep in a temporary shelter in an abandoned Tesco supermarket in Przemysl, Poland yesterday. Soldiers arrive to reinforce one of the final checkpoints before the frontlines where Ukrainian forces were battling Russian forces near Brovary, Ukraine yesterday. A child is carried by a member of the Ukrainian defence force as residents of Iripin attempted to flee the city yesterday. Ukrainian refugees sleeping at a train station in Prezmysl, Poland today. Ukrainian soldiers near Brovary on the outskirts of Kyiv. Civilians flee Sumy the city after temporary ceasefire announced on 8 March Civilians flee Sumy Soldiers at a checkpoint near the frontlines where Ukrainian forces are battling invading Russian forces at Brovary. The Australian securities exchange in Sydney.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220309ei39000gp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
