\par\par \uc2 Television & radio\par \b \uc2 John Oliver: sex work regulation in the US is \u8216\'20\'18confusing and counter-productive\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff \par \uc2 586 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 March 2022\par 12:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Last Week Tonight host discussed how US sex workers are often demonised, patronised or mistreated by the system\par \par \uc2 John Oliver addressed the issue of sex work and how it\u8217\'20\'19s treated within the US on his weekly HBO show Last Week Tonight.\par \par \uc2 The host started by saying that sex is \u8220\'20\'1Ca topic that historically we\u8217\'20\'19ve not been very good at talking about\u8221\'20\'1D but that sex work is poorly handled in America as a result of local, state and federal laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEverything about the way we regulate sex work in this country is confusing and counter-productive,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. It\u8217\'20\'19s either \u8220\'20\'1Cdemonising, patronising or just plain wrong\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Sex work has \u8220\'20\'1Calways been a part of society\u8221\'20\'1D and sex workers \u8220\'20\'1Care not a monolith\u8221\'20\'1D but that\u8217\'20\'19s often not taken into consideration.\par \par \uc2 While police \u8220\'20\'1Cposition themselves as saviours for sex workers\u8221\'20\'1D, they are mostly \u8220\'20\'1Carresting and jailing them\u8221\'20\'1D. He then showed footage of an interview that implied that sex workers should be thankful for police intervention but \u8220\'20\'1Cthere isn\u8217\'20\'19t a thank you section in Hallmark called \u8216\'20\'18for your arresting officer\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He used examples of police who have had sex with sex workers during sex operations and said that between 2016 and 2020, almost everyone arrested by the \uc2 NYPD\uc2  for selling sex was a person of color.\par \par \uc2 Police often use loitering for the purpose of prostitution as a reason to arrest which is \u8220\'20\'1Cbasically a stop and frisk policy for sex workers\u8221\'20\'1D and based on vague judgments. Cops have also seized condoms as evidence and criminalising condoms has led them to go without. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a crime to carry condoms sounds like the name of a Christian boy band\u8217\'20\'19s self-released album,\u8221\'20\'1D he joked.\par \par \uc2 Sex workers have also had to register as sex offenders.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want to paint too rosy a picture here,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CSex work can be dangerous and we need to be talking constructively about how to make it safer in every possible way.\u8221\'20\'1D But too often it\u8217\'20\'19s conflated with sex trafficking and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe implicit suggestion is that no sex worker has ever entered the trade by choice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 One woman was charged with trafficking herself, while shutting down sex workers on sites like \uc2 Craigslist\uc2  and Backpage has removed a much safer route to get clients. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is no surprise that many workers who have been robbed or abused by clients report that they feel they can\u8217\'20\'19t turn to the police for help,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 While the Nordic model, used in Sweden, Norway and France, criminalises the buying of sex but not the selling, it makes it difficult to vet clients.\par \par \uc2 Legalisation, used in Amsterdam and some counties in Nevada, turn sex workers into independent contractors but they have to work at regulated brothels that often take as much as 60% of earnings.\par \par \uc2 He believes the solution is decriminalisation, used in New Zealand, which gives sex workers fundamental rights and is a direction for the US to strive toward.\par \par \uc2 There is always the concern that some people feel economically pushed into sex work but \u8220\'20\'1Cthe only way to make sure people have a choice in how they earn money is to make housing affordable, healthcare accessible and to not burden marginalised people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 1 March 2022 to remove Finland from a list of some of the countries that have adopted \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Nordic model\u8221\'20\'1D approach to sex work.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220228ei2s002bm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
