\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 US Amazon warehouse workers prepare for historic union vote\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,042 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 February 2022\par 09:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Labor board overturned first election over company\u8217\'20\'19s unfair conduct, giving workers another chance to be the first \uc2 Amazon\uc2  facility in US to unionize\par \par \uc2 Workers at the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse in Bessemer, Alabama, have begun the rerun of a historic union election after the US labor regulator ruled \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s conduct had interfered with a previous election in 2021 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/amazon-alabama-facility-ordered-re-run-union-election-us-labor-board-2021-11-29/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ordered}}}\uc2  a new vote.\par \par \uc2 The union drive comes as other large US employers including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/feb/11/starbucks-union-organizing-drives-across-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starbucks}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/feb/10/target-directs-managers-prevent-workers-from-unionizing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Target }}}\uc2  are fighting off union drives. If successful, the warehouse would be the first \uc2 Amazon\uc2  facility to unionize in the US. Employees said that \uc2 Amazon\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which now employs more than 1 million people in the US \u8211\'20\'13 is fighting hard to make sure this vote also fails, but some are feeling more confident the second time around.\par \par \uc2 Darryl Richardson, an employee at the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse in Bessemer for two years, said workers and organizers are now more apt to resist \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s union-busting efforts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re still using the same scare tactics they used last time, but due to the first election, you have employees who understand and know that \uc2 Amazon\uc2  isn\u8217\'20\'19t telling them the truth,\u8221\'20\'1D said Richardson. \u8220\'20\'1CI feel better this time than I did the first time. Employees have been voicing their opinions and standing strong this election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More than 6,100 workers are eligible to vote in the union election, which will determine if workers will be represented by the Retail, Wholesale and Department Store Union (RWDSU). Due to high employee turnover, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-01-25/high-amazon-turnover-could-shift-alabama-union-election-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 almost half }}}\uc2  of the eligible workers in this election were not working at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  during the first union election.\par \par \uc2 Ballots were sent to Alabama workers on 4 February, with ballots due to be returned by 25 March. Results will be tallied beginning on 28 March.\par \par \uc2 Two other \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouses, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Furldefense.com%2Fv3%2F__https%3A%2Fwww.nlrb.gov%2Fcase%2F29-RC-288020__%3B!!Iwwt!E6VIhvp6zm6l-w00CmAs1FNmDO4QWDdEGorta2RrD2unfGoSOteyCueZ33Y0Xw%24&data=04%7C01%7CKayla.Blado%40nlrb.gov%7C5674d84313df46e081f008d9e1299f4b%7C5e453ed8e33843bb90754ed5b8a8caa4%7C0%7C0%7C637788391169959396%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000&sdata=YMlzMi3o6XNaLK%2Bl29tkSrpMDysl1LNBVI8n9Aex7fw%3D&reserved=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JFK8}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Furldefense.com%2Fv3%2F__https%3A%2Fwww.nlrb.gov%2Fcase%2F29-RC-288020__%3B!!Iwwt!E6VIhvp6zm6l-w00CmAs1FNmDO4QWDdEGorta2RrD2unfGoSOteyCueZ33Y0Xw%24&data=04%7C01%7CKayla.Blado%40nlrb.gov%7C5674d84313df46e081f008d9e1299f4b%7C5e453ed8e33843bb90754ed5b8a8caa4%7C0%7C0%7C637788391169959396%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000&sdata=YMlzMi3o6XNaLK%2Bl29tkSrpMDysl1LNBVI8n9Aex7fw%3D&reserved=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LDJ5 }}}\uc2  in Staten Island, New York, have filed petitions to hold union elections with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ), though election dates have not been set by the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  regional director.\par \par \uc2 Perry Connelly, 59, who has worked in outbound stowing at the Bessemer warehouse for two years, said that organizing ahead of the first union election started off well, with a majority of workers signing union authorization cards, but that \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s aggressive anti-union campaign and promises of improvements confused or deterred many workers from voting at all or persuaded them to vote against the union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe just want \uc2 Amazon\uc2  to be held accountable for all the things that make the job, the workplace, unbearable,\u8221\'20\'1D said Connelly. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we do and what we put out, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  can pay a lot better and not have such a high rate of turnover of employees. A lot of people come in and they\u8217\'20\'19re not there for six or seven months, they don\u8217\'20\'19t make it that long because of the working conditions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rerun union elections are relatively rare, with unions prevailing in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/amazon-worker-union-drive-faces-steep-odds-in-election-do-over"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slim majority}}}\uc2  of those elections in recent years. But Connelly claimed this time around, there\u8217\'20\'19s more support for the union. He said many workers switched from voting no in the first election to supporting it, because \uc2 Amazon\uc2  didn\u8217\'20\'19t fulfill the promises they made during the first election, and the union organizing campaign has expanded to handing out union T-shirts, door-knocking efforts that weren\u8217\'20\'19t possible earlier in the Covid-19 pandemic, and partnering with other local unions and community groups.\par \par \uc2 Connelly cited issues such as better pay, better promotional opportunities, more respect from management toward workers and less hostility toward productivity rates as a few of the reasons he is supporting the union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not asking for a lot. We\u8217\'20\'19re just asking for better conditions and less work hassle. We feel like we\u8217\'20\'19re in a hostile work environment day in and day out,\u8221\'20\'1D said Connelly. \u8220\'20\'1CWorking for \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , no one should be worried about paying bills when you work for a multibillionaire, and we just want what we think is fair.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 US businesses have fought hard against union drives in recent years. A 2019 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/unlawful-employer-opposition-to-union-election-campaigns/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Economic Policy Institute\uc2  found that 41.5% of employers had violated federal labor law in union election campaigns and employers spend about $340m annually on union avoidance, issues that have driven campaigns for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/how-pro-act-will-help-employees-advocate-improvements-work"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal labor law reforms}}}\uc2  to expand workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights and steepen penalties for employers violating labor laws.\par \par \uc2 As part of the new election ruling, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  reached a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/business-national-labor-relations-board-523e6836eeb618755e44a4d9454592ef"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 settlement}}}\uc2  with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 , agreeing to refrain from threatening workers with discipline or calling the police on workers engaging in union activity outside the warehouse. If \uc2 Amazon\uc2  is found to violate the settlement, the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  could more easily sue the company.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  is once again aggressively opposing the unionization effort at the warehouse, with regular {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/technology-business-alabama-national-labor-relations-board-c98220996649c7cbb14a29468f053edc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 anti-union meetings}}}\uc2  where outside consultants and managers are encouraging workers to vote against the union. A worker at the Bessemer warehouse has already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/10-CA-289418"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed }}}\uc2  unfair labor practice charges with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  against \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.engadget.com/amazon-bessemer-retaliation-ulp-rwdsu-025525584.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alleging}}}\uc2  the settlement was violated because he claims management warned him about speaking with co-workers about the union.\par \par \uc2 During the first union election, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  installed a \uc2 United States Postal Service\uc2  mailbox in front of the warehouse, surrounded by signs encouraging workers to vote no in the election. That mailbox was a significant factor in the first union election being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/11/29/business/amazon-bessemer-alabama-election.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 . The union has already made a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fapps.nlrb.gov%2Flink%2Fdocument.aspx%2F09031d4583673e76&data=04%7C01%7CKayla.Blado%40nlrb.gov%7C68e646b46e664864600008d9e819f47d%7C5e453ed8e33843bb90754ed5b8a8caa4%7C0%7C0%7C637796020434888754%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000&sdata=CBXwyoVTe%2Ff9sPVDlP%2BFyC9KRw6GFHDEw1p1RjHwiLM%3D&reserved=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 request for review}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  of objectionable conduct over the mailbox, as it remains on site at the warehouse, but was just moved to a different location.\par \par \uc2 The union argued the mailbox undermined the election as it is subject to constant surveillance by the company, and the stigma surrounding the mailbox as employer-controlled remains. The \uc2 NLRB{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fapps.nlrb.gov%2Flink%2Fdocument.aspx%2F09031d458368ee07&data=04%7C01%7CKayla.Blado%40nlrb.gov%7C68e646b46e664864600008d9e819f47d%7C5e453ed8e33843bb90754ed5b8a8caa4%7C0%7C0%7C637796020434888754%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000&sdata=rZRwXs5FdNU9c5qCuGIGQWxg3fGQK8ucbN2WpKs1d2k%3D&reserved=0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled }}}\uc2  the claims would be resolved after the new election.\par \par \uc2 Contacted by the Guardian, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  did not comment on how its conduct this election has changed from the previous one.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson said in an email: \u8220\'20\'1COur employees have always had the choice of whether or not to join a union, and they overwhelmingly chose not to join the RWDSU last year. We look forward to our team in BHM1 having their voices heard again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220215ei2f0018h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
