\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Yoga, nature walks: \uc2 Salesforce\uc2  opens luxe \u8216\'20\'18ranch\u8217\'20\'19 to help remote workers connect\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 581 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 February 2022\par 01:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In an internal survey, employees asked company to find \u8216\'20\'18ways to connect\u8217\'20\'19 which the 75-acre Trailblazer ranch will provide plenty of\par \par \uc2 Salesforce\uc2  employees will soon be able to hold meetings in California\u8217\'20\'19s redwood forests after the company announced plans to open its own luxury ranch to help staff \u8220\'20\'1Cconnect\u8221\'20\'1D after two years of remote working.\par \par \uc2 The 75-acre property known as Trailblazer Ranch is located near Santa Cruz, California, and boasts an outdoor amphitheater, a communal kitchen, fitness and learning centers and conference rooms. The property also features sleeping pods and suites equipped with fireplaces and employees will be able to partake in guided nature walks, yoga sessions, garden tours, group cooking classes, art journaling and meditation.\par \par \uc2 The company says \uc2 Salesforce\uc2  workers will be able to visit the property from next month for onboarding, training, skills building and talent development.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince the pandemic began, we\u8217\'20\'19ve onboarded tens of thousands of employees remotely. Those employees have never met their manager or teams in person. And many of our existing employees haven\u8217\'20\'19t seen their colleagues face-to-face in two years,\u8221\'20\'1D the company said in a statement on Thursday. \uc2 Salesforce\uc2  said that, according to an internal survey, the number one thing employees asked for was \u8220\'20\'1Cfinding ways to connect\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Covid-19 pandemic brought a temporary hiatus to Silicon Valley\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/artanddesign/2016/may/22/nap-pods-and-rooftop-parks-how-silicon-valley-is-reinventing-the-office"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  famously over the top office spaces }}}\uc2  as thousands of tech workers went remote. And while the pandemic fueled speculation that this could spell the end for Silicon Valley, the recent reopening of office spaces appears to prove otherwise.\par \par \uc2 Some companies are starting to coax people back and companies, including \uc2 Google\uc2  and \uc2 Facebook\uc2  , are taking out leases on even more offices. Last year, Silicon Valley witnessed a building boom that led to the most office construction in six years. In December, \uc2 Meta\uc2  rented 719,000 sq ft at a campus in Sunnyvale in what was the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfchronicle.com/tech/article/Facebook-parent-Meta-signs-biggest-U-S-office-16667757.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largest private-sector office lease }}}\uc2  of 2021.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSilicon Valley remains the global center of innovation and its importance will continue to grow even as other innovation hubs emerge,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mercurynews.com/2021/12/01/meta-facebook-lease-tech-campus-sunnyvale-office-real-estate-job-covid/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  Tishman Speyer, a veteran developer who bought the campus seven months before \uc2 Facebook\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s purchase.\par \par \uc2 Other new construction {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.siliconvalley.com/2022/02/09/silicon-valley-office-build-boom-real-estate-develop-tech-covid/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 projects }}}\uc2  that were completed in 2021 include a 657,000 sq ft \uc2 Yahoo\uc2  office campus in San Jose, as well as a 611,000 sq ft \uc2 Google\uc2  office campus nearby.\par \par \uc2 Salesforce\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s new ranch reaffirms the company\u8217\'20\'19s \u8211\'20\'13 and Silicon Valley\u8217\'20\'19s \u8211\'20\'13 continued belief in the importance of working in person. \u8220\'20\'1CTrailblazer Ranch is an exciting new gathering place where employees can forge trusted relationships with their colleagues, learn from one another, get inspired, grow in their career, get trained on the company, and give back to the community in a fun and safe environment,\u8221\'20\'1D the company said.\par \par \uc2 Salesforce\uc2  said the ranch is an \u8220\'20\'1Copportunity to disconnect from technology and connect with each other\u8221\'20\'1D. The company went on to cite a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/focus/human-capital-trends/2021/workforce-trends-2020.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study }}}\uc2  by \uc2 Deloitte\uc2  that revealed employees are working three more hours a day compared with before the pandemic. Moreover, 80% of the study\u8217\'20\'19s respondents listed wellbeing as important or very important to their company\u8217\'20\'19s success.\par \par \uc2 The ranch is temporarily located at 1440 Multiversity in the town of Scotts Valley, as the company solidifies its long-term Trailblazer Ranch site. The ranch space will also be open to local non-profits and the surrounding community, the company said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220212ei2c0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
