\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Unions benefit all of us\u8217\'20\'19: new Biden plan encourages federal workers to unionize\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 729 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 February 2022\par 14:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Taskforce sets recommendations \u8216\'20\'18to promote my policy of support for worker power, worker organizing and collective bargaining\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration set out 70 recommendations to encourage union membership in the US on Monday, including making it easier for many federal employees to join unions and eliminating barriers for union organizers to talk with workers on federal property.\par \par \uc2 The report, compiled by the White House Task Force on Worker Organizing and Empowerment, reiterates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/may/02/joe-biden-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s robust backing of unions}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAt its core,\u8221\'20\'1D the report says, \u8220\'20\'1Cit is our administration\u8217\'20\'19s belief that unions benefit all of us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It adds: \u8220\'20\'1CResearchers have found that today\u8217\'20\'19s union households earn up to 20% more than non-union households, with an even greater union advantage for workers with less formal education and workers of color.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The report comes amid a surge in interest in unions in the US and follows a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/23/striketober-unions-strikes-workers-lasting-change"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wave of high-profile industrial actions }}}\uc2  last year.\par \par \uc2 The taskforce, which includes 13 members of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet and is chaired by Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , calls for stepping up enforcement to ensure that money going to federal contractors \u8211\'20\'13 whether manufacturers, food-processing companies or other contractors \u8211\'20\'13 is not spent on anti-union campaigns.\par \par \uc2 The taskforce calls for requiring disclosure of any instances when federal contractors use anti-union consultants or lawyers to persuade employees working on a federal contract not to unionize.\par \par \uc2 While corporations typically prohibit union organizers from setting foot on company property \u8211\'20\'13 as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/jan/12/amazon-union-warehouse-workers-alabama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amazon has done recently in Alabama}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the taskforce recommends removing many barriers that block union organizers from being able to talk with employees on federal property about the benefits of unionizing. This applies not just to federal employees, but also to employees of private contractors on federal property, such as a grocery store on a military base or in a national park.\par \par \uc2 Biden said the taskforce\u8217\'20\'19s charge was to identify executive branch policies, practices and programs that could be used \u8220\'20\'1Cto promote my administration\u8217\'20\'19s policy of support for worker power, worker organizing, and collective bargaining\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The taskforce said the range of policies and programs \u8220\'20\'1Cthat can be leveraged is significant\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Its recommendations include making the federal government a model employer in terms of shaping jobs, ensuring that federal employees know their labor rights, and improving labor-management communications. The federal government is the nation\u8217\'20\'19s largest employer, with more than 2.1 million non-postal employees. Of those, 1.2 million are represented by unions, but only 33% of those workers pay union dues \u8211\'20\'13 that small percentage limits the power of federal employee unions.\par \par \uc2 Noting that screeners for the \uc2 Transportation Security Administration\uc2  (TSA) are largely excluded from having the collective bargaining rights available to other non-military federal employees, the taskforce instructed the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  to issue expanded bargaining rights for TSA\u8217\'20\'19s screening workforce.\par \par \uc2 The report is likely to strengthen the notion that Biden is the most pro-union president since \uc2 Franklin Roosevelt\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and perhaps the most pro-union president in US history. That might help Biden when he seeks to persuade and mobilize union members to vote for Democrats this November. At the same time, the report\u8217\'20\'19s pro-union tone and substance might result in more opposition from business.\par \par \uc2 In its first sentence, the report says: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Biden-Harris administration believes that increasing worker organizing and empowerment is critical to growing the middle class, building an economy that puts workers first, and strengthening our democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D The report catalogues several executive orders and other pro-union steps by the president and his administration.\par \par \uc2 It reads: \u8220\'20\'1CUnions have fought for and helped win many aspects of our work lives many of us take for granted today, like the 40-hour work week and the weekend, as well as landmark programs like Medicare.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The report adds that research has shown that increased economic inequality, growing pay gaps for women and workers of color, and the declining voice of working-class Americans in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s politics \u8220\'20\'1Care all caused, in part, by the declining percentage of workers represented by unions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The taskforce calls on the Department of Labor \u8211\'20\'13 whose secretary, \uc2 Martin Walsh\uc2 , is the taskforce\u8217\'20\'19s vice-chair \u8211\'20\'13 to become a resource center that provides materials on the advantages of union representation and collective bargaining.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220207ei27001s0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
