\par\par \uc2 Environment\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Our raises have been pennies\u8217\'20\'19: US cake-makers strike for fair deal as company makes billions\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 986 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 February 2022\par 15:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers at the Jon Donaire plant in California are struggling to cope \u8211\'20\'13 so why won\u8217\'20\'19t the factory\u8217\'20\'19s owner raise its offer?\par \par \uc2 More than 150 workers at the Jon Donaire Desserts plant in Santa Fe Springs, California, have been on strike since early November over wages, healthcare coverage and working conditions.\par \par \uc2 The dispute centers on food workers, hailed as heroes early in the pandemic, who are struggling to cope with spiraling costs of living as the company that employs them posts billion-dollar revenues.\par \par \uc2 Workers at the plant, which makes ice-cream cakes for companies such as \uc2 Baskin-Robbins\uc2 , \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and \uc2 Safeway\uc2 , are asking for a $1 an hour raise every year for three years with no cuts to their healthcare costs.\par \par \uc2 Rich Products Corporation\uc2 , the plant\u8217\'20\'19s owner, has made two offers to the \uc2 Bakery, Confectionery, Tobacco Workers and Grain Millers\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 International Union, which represents the workers. One proposed a 50\u162\'00\'A2 raise over one year and 55\u162\'00\'A2 raises for the following two years. The other offered an overall wage increase of $4.10 an hour, but included significant increases to the cost of workers\u8217\'20\'19 healthcare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, we\u8217\'20\'19re paying around $130 a month for healthcare. They want to increase it to $480 for a single person and $780 for a family plan,\u8221\'20\'1D said Miguel Perez, who has worked at the Jon Donaire plant for 12 years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Rich Corporation is not fulfilling its obligation to take care of its employees. They had us working through the whole pandemic. Everybody showed up to work. We all met our quotas as far as production [is concerned], and now that the contract is up they\u8217\'20\'19re trying to nickel-and-dime us into an unacceptable raise.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers have highlighted the company owners\u8217\'20\'19 immense wealth and profits in their pressure to secure the raises they are on strike to receive. The chief executive and owner of Rich Products, Robert Rich Jr, has a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/profile/robert-rich-jr/?sh=586357ce3bff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 net worth}}}\uc2  of $4.9bn. In the first year of the pandemic, Rich Products reported more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/companies/rich-products/?sh=1ab76bc87ccd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $4bn}}}\uc2  in revenue.\par \par \uc2 Perez also described workplace grievances, including being informed of forced overtime with just a few minutes left at the end of a shift, often being denied permissions to take time off from work to go to a doctor\u8217\'20\'19s appointment, and the treatment of a workforce that is roughly 90% women by supervisors who are mostly men.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery week we see a woman coming out of the office crying, because she felt like she was disrespected,\u8221\'20\'1D added Perez. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a lot of that going on. Sometimes the male supervisors are cursing at them, yelling at them, or even making inappropriate gestures.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jon Donaire denied these allegations, claiming the union has never addressed these grievances with the company. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are unfortunately many stories with baseless claims that we\u8217\'20\'19ve had to refute throughout this process \u8211\'20\'13 and we will continue to do so,\u8221\'20\'1D said a spokesperson.\par \par \uc2 It also cited long tenures of employees and an internal survey of workers in March last year, where 80% of Santa Fe Springs\u8217\'20\'19 employees said they would recommend Rich\u8217\'20\'19s to others as a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat place to work\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Cristina Lujan has worked at the Jon Donaire plant for 19 years. Most recently she was on the cake assembly line, decorating cakes at a rate of around 13 a minute.\par \par \uc2 Throughout her time at the plant Lujan said production demands have gotten higher and higher but her pay has not kept up with the increased demands on her nor with the costs of living in the Los Angeles area.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I started, I was well above minimum wage,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lujan. \u8220\'20\'1CNow, 19 years later, I\u8217\'20\'19m barely above minimum wage. Our raises have been pennies every contract.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers at the plant make on average less than $17 an hour, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bass.house.gov/media-center/press-releases/rep-bass-joins-calls-jon-donaire-desserts-engage-good-faith-negations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 compared}}}\uc2  to workers at a Rich Products\u8217\'20\'19 facility in Tennessee, who are paid on average $6 an hour more.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think he [Robert Rich Jr] can afford to pay us the $1 more that we\u8217\'20\'19re asking for,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lujan. \u8220\'20\'1CEverything is going up, gas, food, rent and we\u8217\'20\'19re living paycheck to paycheck. Everybody\u8217\'20\'19s tired of feeling that frustration and stress daily. Their big company model is based on family first, but the way they treat us, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think that\u8217\'20\'19s the way you treat family.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On 17 December, workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bctgm.org/2021/12/18/bctgm-local-37-members-at-jon-donaire-overwhelmingly-reject-contract-proposal-strike-continues/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected}}}\uc2  the company\u8217\'20\'19s contract offer, continuing the strike. Rich Products responded by declaring an impasse in new union contract negotiations and enacting the wage increases they proposed to workers who crossed the picket line, which the company said amounts to almost 60 workers. The company also paid workers who crossed picket lines back pay and a gain sharing bonus.\par \par \uc2 The union has filed unfair labor practice charges against the company for imposing a contract on the unionized workforce that was voted down by workers, which is currently under review at the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 . Several elected officials, including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mynewsla.com/business/2021/12/21/la-county-board-backs-union-in-cake-workers-strike/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles County Board of Supervisors}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bctgm.org/2022/01/24/25-u-s-representatives-urge-rich-products-ceo-to-bargain-in-good-faith-reach-an-agreement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 25 congressional representatives }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sanders.senate.gov/wp-content/uploads/JonDonaireStrike_Letter_011022.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seven US senators}}}\uc2 , have called on the Rich Corporation to bargain in good faith with the union and reach a fair contract.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRich\u8217\'20\'19s is especially concerned about what the strike has meant for striking associates who have now gone weeks without a paycheck, are not eligible for state unemployment benefits, and will soon forfeit the high-quality healthcare they told the company they wanted to retain,\u8221\'20\'1D said a spokesperson for Rich Products.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are pleased many of our associates have continued to come to work since the strike began and plant production has continued. They deserve the wage increase we proposed and to retain their uninterrupted high-quality healthcare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe welcome back all striking workers with open arms and will provide the same considerations to them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220205ei2500209\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
