\par\par \uc2 Media\par \b \uc2 Leaked messages reveal \uc2 New York Times\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 aggressive anti-union strategy\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 849 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 February 2022\par 22:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Company\u8217\'20\'19s chief executive warned a union would be \u8216\'20\'18an unproven experiment with permanent consequences\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Internal documents and \uc2 Slack\uc2  messages obtained by the Guardian reveal senior executives at the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  are heavily leaning on workers to vote no in a union election for more than 600 tech employees.\par \par \uc2 Meredith Kopit Levien\uc2  , the chief executive of the \uc2 New York Times Company\uc2  , wrote a memo on 19 January circulated to staff titled \u8220\'20\'1CWhy a Tech Union Isn\u8217\'20\'19t Right for Us\u8221\'20\'1D on the tech workers\u8217\'20\'19 union election at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytco.com/press/georg-petschnigg-joins-the-times-as-head-of-product-design/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XFun  }}}\uc2 , the group within the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  responsible for product development operations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn short, we don\u8217\'20\'19t believe unionizing in XFun is the right move. But that\u8217\'20\'19s not because I\u8217\'20\'19m anti-union,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kopit Levien.\par \par \uc2 In the memo, Kopit Levien cited the origin of the XFun group and its growth, and attributed any disconnect workers might be feeling to working apart during the pandemic. She also cited Wirecutter\u8217\'20\'19s union as a warning sign for unionization.\par \par \uc2 Workers at Wirecutter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gizmodo.com/dont-cross-the-wirecutter-picket-line-1848112947"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walked out  }}}\uc2  on Black Friday weekend in late November and called on the public to boycott the publication, in protest of unfair labor practices and alleging that the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  was bargaining in bad faith. Shortly after the walkout, an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/14/business/media/wirecutter-union-contract.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreement  }}}\uc2  was reached between the union and Times management.\par \par \uc2 Kopit Levien said in the memo: \u8220\'20\'1CIt took Wirecutter two years to reach an agreement with the NewsGuild. And the result of those prolonged Wirecutter negotiations was a set of terms that are, in most ways, what the rest of the company already enjoys. This was two years of uncertainty and discord to negotiate terms that were largely in line with what they and their non-union colleagues already had in place.\par \par \uc2 She emphasized the relationship between management and workers, alleging the relationship would be disrupted by a union, and that the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 diversity, equity and inclusion goals would also be disrupted by a union.\par \par \uc2 Kopit Levien wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is an unproven experiment with permanent consequences.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In \uc2 Slack\uc2  messages, Times chief product officer Alexandra Hardiman and chief growth officer Hannah Yang posted messages urging workers to vote no in the union election. Yang reshared Kopit Leviten\u8217\'20\'19s letter to workers, prompting workers to see it on the company\u8217\'20\'19s internal election resources hub.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA union is not a silver bullet,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Hardiman, urging workers to vote no. \u8220\'20\'1CIt will introduce another layer into our process that we believe will make it harder to work \u8211\'20\'13 and achieve \u8211\'20\'13 together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Yang argued that a union would \u8220\'20\'1Cdilute\u8221\'20\'1D the voice of smaller teams within the group of workers. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you have any concerns about how your voice will be represented in negotiations, we urge you to vote no for the union,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe encourage you to vote no,\u8221\'20\'1D a leaflet distributed by the Times to workers said. It cited three reasons: \u8220\'20\'1Cweakening relationships between employees and managers\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Clengthy negotiating processes and inflexible multi-year agreements\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Creducing your flexibility to learn new skills\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Slack\uc2  messages from the executive were quickly flooded by negative emojis. Only a select few workers can post in the staff-wide \uc2 Slack\uc2  channels, so emojis are often the only way most workers can respond to the posts.\par \par \uc2 Ballots for the mail-in election were sent out on 24 January and are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NYTGuildTech/status/1481352719885651974"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 due  }}}\uc2  on 28 February. Vote tallies are to be counted on 7 March.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Labor Relations Board{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/transactional/new-york-times-loses-bid-block-union-election-tech-workers-2022-01-12/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected  }}}\uc2  the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 attempt to stop the election, alleging the bargaining unit was improper. The company had previously declined to voluntarily recognize the union and immediately began {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/88nxv3/new-york-times-workers-are-fed-up-with-the-new-york-times-union-busting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 holding  }}}\uc2  anti-union captive audience meetings with workers.\par \par \uc2 The NewsGuild of New York {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2022/01/juneteenth-is-a-pretty-aggressive-holiday-to-take-hostages-with-nyt-union-views-new-holidays-as-latest-union-busting-bid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed  }}}\uc2  a complaint earlier this month with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  , accusing the Times of violating federal labor law by adding new paid days off to the company holiday calendar for non-union employees only \u8211\'20\'13 which was viewed as a tactic to dissuade workers from voting for the union.\par \par \uc2 After the complaint was filed, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NYTimesGuild/status/1486408492118335502"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 similar changes  }}}\uc2  to its bereavement policy, making it applicable only to non-union workers. The union is collecting signatures as part of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://actionnetwork.org/letters/new-york-times-stop-union-busting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 public petition  }}}\uc2  demanding the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  stop what it calls union-busting.\par \par \uc2 On 5 January, the \uc2 NLRB{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/01/05/business/media/times-tech-guild-nlrb.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed  }}}\uc2  a complaint against the Times, ruling the company violated federal labor law by telling some employees they could not show support for tech workers seeking to unionize.\par \par \uc2 If successful, the tech workers at the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  would form the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/transactional/new-york-times-loses-bid-block-union-election-tech-workers-2022-01-12/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largest bargaining unit of tech workers in the US  }}}\uc2 , according to the union.\par \par \uc2 In an email to the Guardian, a spokesperson for the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Times Company has a long history of productive relationships with our unions. However, we do not believe a union would be best for the individuals or teams in the proposed tech and digital product unit, and could stifle innovation and collaboration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlso, a union among tech and digital workers would be an unproven experiment with lasting implications.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220201ei2100163\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
