\par\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Alabama coalminers on strike for 10 months vow not to be \u8216\'20\'18starved out\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,038 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 January 2022\par 10:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 State troopers escort strikebreakers to the mines and local courts grant injunctions to limit pickets\par \par \uc2 About 1,100 coalminers in Alabama have entered 2022 still on strike, more than 10 months since they walked out back in April last year, making it the longest strike in the US since the Covid-19 pandemic began and the longest in Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s history.\par \par \uc2 Workers started the unfair labor practice strike over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.al.com/news/2021/08/warrior-met-coals-strike-practices-could-bring-national-labor-relations-board-complaint.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims }}}\uc2  of bad faith bargaining by \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2  over a new union contract. In the previous contract settled in 2016, miners accepted several concessions, including a $6-an-hour pay cut and reductions in health insurance and other benefits as the mines switched employers in the wake of a bankruptcy.\par \par \uc2 The miners on strike have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.alreporter.com/2021/12/15/elizabeth-warren-sherrod-brown-back-striking-warrior-met-coal-mine-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received support }}}\uc2  from US politicians such as Senators Bernie Sanders, Elizabeth Warren, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sanders.senate.gov/wp-content/uploads/BlackRock_WarriorMet_Letter_011322.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tammy Baldwin}}}\uc2  and Sherrod Brown, and received {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://umwa.org/umwa-2021-strike-fund-contributors/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 donations }}}\uc2  to their strike fund from dozens of labor unions across the US.\par \par \uc2 Over the past 10 months they have held {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tuscaloosanews.com/story/news/2021/08/04/united-mine-workers-rally-support-coal-mine-strike-brookwood/5480898001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rallies }}}\uc2  and extended {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.alreporter.com/2021/11/19/miners-demonstrate-at-capitol-against-trooper-escorting-strikebreakers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 protests}}}\uc2  to the Alabama state capitol to criticize the use of public resources for state troopers escorting strikebreaking replacement workers to the mines throughout the strike. Miners have also held rallies in New York City outside the offices of BlackRock Investment Group, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-07-28/blackrock-support-sought-in-bid-to-end-5-month-coal-mine-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largest shareholder}}}\uc2  of \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2 . As of 2 November, the strike has cost the company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.al.com/business/2021/11/warrior-met-coal-strike-has-cost-company-69-million.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  $6.9m}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMost of us are working other jobs and receiving strike pay but some have crossed the line,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rily Hughlett, a miner at \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2 , who has worked as a roof bolter in the mines for 13 years and believes that workers will win the strike. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not going anywhere. The scabs and the bosses are all humored but he who laughs last laughs loudest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2  took over the mines, the company has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://companiesmarketcap.com/warrior-met-coal/revenue/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2  billions of dollars in revenue. A tentative agreement was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tuscaloosanews.com/story/news/2021/04/06/united-mine-workers-america-end-alabama-warrior-met-coal-strike/7103872002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached }}}\uc2  in the first week of the strike, but overwhelmingly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://umwa.org/news-media/news/warrior-met-coals-strike-practices-could-bring-national-labor-relations-board-complaint/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected}}}\uc2  by workers, and a new agreement has yet to be reached.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat they\u8217\'20\'19ve said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/striking-miner-claims-company-said-they-would-starve-workers-out-before-giving-raises-1666900"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 openly}}}\uc2  in negotiations is that they\u8217\'20\'19re just going to starve us out. They\u8217\'20\'19ve said \u8230\'20\'26 and this on record, that \u8216\'20\'18we have the money to pay what you\u8217\'20\'19re asking, we do not have the desire to.\u8217\'20\'19 That\u8217\'20\'19s the kind of company these guys have been working for,\u8221\'20\'1D said Haeden Wright, president of the \uc2 United Mine Workers of America\uc2  auxiliary for two of the striking locals and the wife of a striking miner. \u8220\'20\'1CThrough the journey, most of us are still holding out and trying to hold on, but it is hard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The unions\u8217\'20\'19 auxiliary has focused on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://umwa.org/news-media/journal/warrior-met-strikers-fighting-for-families/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 receiving and distributing}}}\uc2  weekly groceries to miners and their families throughout the strike and assisting families with needs such as bills. It recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tuscaloosathread.com/striking-miners-christmas-toy-drive/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 organized }}}\uc2  a Christmas gift drive for miners\u8217\'20\'19 families to ensure their children were taken care of over the holidays.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor it to last this long and to have state troopers and to watch your tax dollars escort scabs into your job, that\u8217\'20\'19s a hard pill to swallow,\u8221\'20\'1D added Wright. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s hard to watch and not be able to do anything about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Wright says that the strike has been hard but it has forced union members to strengthen their support systems with one another, and they have been able to spend a lot more time with their children and families after working 12-hour days, six or seven days a week in the mines.\par \par \uc2 Those long and demanding work schedules are one point of contention for workers in a new union contract. Wright\u8217\'20\'19s husband, Braxton, has taken a temporary job during the strike at Amazon in Bessemer, Alabama, where he has become involved in supporting the unionization efforts at the warehouse. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/jan/12/amazon-union-warehouse-workers-alabama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new union election}}}\uc2  ordered by the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  is scheduled to begin next month.\par \par \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/business-alabama-tuscaloosa-strikes-united-mine-workers-of-america-ae76d7d627cdbb90f8845c7a6ce29c9f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  several court injunctions throughout the strike to severely limit or prevent striking miners from picketing outside the mines. Several union members and supporters have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://umwa.org/news-media/press/more-company-violence-on-the-warrior-met-picket-line/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported incidents}}}\uc2  where vehicles have hit or nearly missed individuals on the picket lines. The injunctions have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/picketing-alabama-miners-stopped-by-rare-non-federal-court-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 characterized}}}\uc2  as a rare move, an attempt by \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2  to circumventthe \uc2 NLRB\uc2  and instead seek rulings from favorable local courts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re still negotiating with them. We still have not reached an agreement but we\u8217\'20\'19re hopeful that we can get something pretty soon here,\u8221\'20\'1D said Larry Spencer, the District 20 field representative for the UMWA in Alabama.\par \par \uc2 He said the surge in Omicron cases during the pandemic and the holidays have made it more difficult to schedule negotiations on both sides, and the unions have paused picket lines temporarily to figure out how to comply with the court injunctions while ensuring members are kept safe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWorkers have fought really hard to try to stay united and keep solidarity out there. We have a rally once a week and we\u8217\'20\'19ve had a good showing of members and their families come out,\u8221\'20\'1D added Spencer. \u8220\'20\'1CThe key is the membership. They are the ones pulling together and really fighting hard to make sure they get what they deserve through this company and get back to work as soon as possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Department of Labor\uc2  did not comment on whether its secretary, \uc2 Marty Walsh\uc2 , intended to intervene to assist in negotiations as he did with the 10-month-long nurses strike at St Vincent hospital in Worcester, Massachusetts, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fiercehealthcare.com/hospitals/nurses-strike-tenet-healthcare-st-vincent-hospital-vote-to-end-10-month-strike-at-tenet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  ended}}}\uc2  with an agreement on 3 January.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the labor department said: \u8220\'20\'1CWorkers with unions have the power to advocate collectively for the working conditions they deserve, like fair wages and safety on the job. Workplaces are safer and more productive when workers have a seat at the table. We encourage businesses and unions to come together and work toward solutions in good faith.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Warrior Met Coal\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://warriormetcoalfacts.com/strike-misinformation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disputed }}}\uc2  claims that specific terms of previous contracts would be restored during the 2016 contract negotiations, and have rejected claims from workers and the union throughout the strike, but said it continued to negotiate in pursuit of a resolution.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220125ei1p001jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
