\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse workers have new chance to form union next month\b0\par\par\uc2 Dani Anguiano and agencies \par \uc2 657 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 January 2022\par 14:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Fresh election in Alabama comes after US official finds company violated labor law in last year\u8217\'20\'19s vote\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers at an Alabama warehouse will get another chance to unionize next month, after a federal labor board set a February date for the rerun election.\par \par \uc2 The fresh vote comes after an official at the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) found that \uc2 Amazon\uc2  had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/nov/29/amazon-union-election-bessemer-alabama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 violated labor law}}}\uc2  in the union election held last year and ruled in November that workers must get another chance to vote.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  said on Tuesday that workers at the plant in Bessemer would vote by mail in the new election. Ballots will be mailed out on 4 February and must be returned by 25 March. Counting starts three days later.\par \par \uc2 The second election is a blow to \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , the US\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest private employer, after \uc2 Walmart\uc2 . The company fought for a year to stop workers from forming its \uc2 first union\uc2 . Workers at the Bessemer plant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/apr/09/amazon-union-vote-result-latest-news-bessemer-alabama-plant"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ultimately voted}}}\uc2  1,798 to 738 to reject the Retail, Wholesale and Department Store Union (RWDSU).\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has about 750,000 warehouse workers in the US, and the company has come under fire over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2020/feb/05/amazon-workers-protest-unsafe-grueling-conditions-warehouse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 working conditions}}}\uc2 . Pro-union Bessemer workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/nov/29/amazon-union-election-bessemer-alabama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  they spent 10-hour shifts on their feet in the warehouse and didn\u8217\'20\'19t have enough time to take breaks.\par \par \uc2 The company aggressively opposed organizing efforts, sought to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/jan/27/amazon-seeks-to-block-workers-from-voting-by-mail-in-landmark-union-drive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 postpone}}}\uc2  the election and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/feb/03/amazon-intensifies-severe-effort-discourage-first-warehouse-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bombarded}}}\uc2  workers with anti-union messaging.\par \par \uc2 The RWDSU accused the company of illegal misconduct during last year\u8217\'20\'19s vote. An NLRB officer who presided over the case later determined that \uc2 Amazon\uc2  violated labor law and recommended that the regional director set aside the results and order another election.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NLRB\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision, announced in November, further highlighted issues including \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s installation of a \uc2 US Postal Service\uc2  mailbox at the main employee entrance, which the federal board said may have created the false impression that the company was the one conducting the election process. Lisa Henderson, the NLRB regional director who made the rare decision, rejected \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s argument that it was making voting easier and was trying to encourage as high a turnout as possible.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur employees have always had the choice of whether or not to join a union, and they overwhelmingly chose not to join the RWDSU last year,\u8221\'20\'1D Barbara Agrait, an Amazon spokesperson, said in an emailed statement on Tuesday, adding that she looked forward to having its team in Bessemer \u8216\'20\'18\u8221\'20\'1Dhaving their voices heard again\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The RWDSU has taken issue with \uc2 NLRB\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to hold an election by mail.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are deeply concerned that the decision fails to adequately prevent \uc2 Amazon\uc2  from continuing its objectionable behavior in a new election,\u8221\'20\'1D the union said in a statement. The union is pushing for an in-person election, which it feels could make the process fairer to workers.\par \par \uc2 Labor experts have warned that a union victory is a long shot and the RWDSU faces an uphill battle to unionize workers given high turnover rates that hamper efforts to organize. But \uc2 Amazon\uc2  did reach a settlement with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  last month to allow its employees to freely organize \u8211\'20\'13 and without retaliation.\par \par \uc2 The online behemoth said it would reach out to its warehouse workers \u8211\'20\'13 former and current \u8211\'20\'13 who were on the job anytime from 22 March of last year to notify them of their organizing rights, according to the settlement.\par \par \uc2 The settlement outlined that \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers, would have more room to organize within the buildings. The company previously banned workers from areas around facilities for 15 minutes before or after their shifts, making it difficult for workers to organize, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2021/12/23/technology/amazon-labor-deal.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Amazon\uc2  pledged it would not threaten workers with discipline or call the police when they are engaging in union activity in exterior non-work areas during non-work time.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220117ei1h002s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
