\par\par \uc2 Environment\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We have people living out of their cars\u8217\'20\'19: 8,000 \uc2 Kroger\uc2  workers strike over wages\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 995 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 January 2022\par 19:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers at nearly 80 grocery stores accuse corporation of making big profits during pandemic while not paying employees enough\par \par \uc2 More than 8,000 workers at nearly 80 \uc2 Kroger\uc2 -owned King Soopers grocery stores around Colorado {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/transactional/workers-nearly-80-krogers-king-soopers-go-strike-talks-stall-2022-01-12/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 started a three-week strike}}}\uc2  on Wednesday as new union contract negotiations stalled.\par \par \uc2 The dispute is the latest in which workers have accused a corporation of making {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/retail-consumer/kroger-raises-profit-forecast-at-home-cooking-sustains-grocery-demand-2021-12-02/#:~:text=Register%20now%20for%20FREE%20unlimited%20access%20to%20Reuters.com,-Register&text=Kroger%20said%20it%20expects%20full,forecast%20of%20%243.25%20to%20%243.35."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 big profits}}}\uc2  during the pandemic while not paying high enough wages.\par \par \uc2 Kenny Sanchez, a King Soopers worker in Broomfield, Colorado, for 10 years has attended new contract negotiation meetings with the United Food and Commercial Workers Local 7 union and \uc2 Kroger\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and said there was a gulf between the two sides.\par \par \uc2 Sanchez said the lawyers from out of state acting on behalf of \uc2 Kroger\uc2  don\u8217\'20\'19t get that the cost of living in Colorado has been soaring, and the workers\u8217\'20\'19 wages aren\u8217\'20\'19t keeping up with it. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not making a living wage. We have people living out of their cars and struggling to pay bills,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanchez. \u8220\'20\'1CThis company does not get it. We can\u8217\'20\'19t survive on what they\u8217\'20\'19re paying out here and the competition is paying more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Union members voted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.9news.com/article/news/local/king-soopers-employees-strike/73-439c3d5e-eaa0-4f2e-b5a7-b2fb58496156"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly unanimously}}}\uc2  to authorize the strike over unfair labor practices against \uc2 Kroger\uc2 , as the company\u8217\'20\'19s last, best and final offer included several concessions such as permitting the company to lower wages, use non-union gig workers, shortening leave of absence periods, relying on a part-time workforce, and offering only a $0.13 wage increase for some workers.\par \par \uc2 Workers have pushed for a $6-an-hour wage increase for all employees, while the final proposal only included wage increases up to $4.50 an hour based on job classification and tenure, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/kroger-faces-strike-threat-from-thousands-of-colorado-grocery-workers_n_61ddaf5de4b0bb04a64ab2c5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a $16-an-hour floor}}}\uc2 , just $0.13 higher than minimum wage in Denver.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA pay raise is nice, but if you\u8217\'20\'19re forking out a bunch more for health insurance, then there is no raise. That\u8217\'20\'19s why it\u8217\'20\'19s a crooked deal,\u8221\'20\'1D added Sanchez. \u8220\'20\'1CHealthcare costs around the country have been going up and we need the company to put a little extra money into our health insurance to keep it affordable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kim Cordova\uc2 , president of UFCW Local 7, said the unfair labor practice charges the union filed against \uc2 Kroger\uc2  included refusal to furnish information necessary for bargaining over issues such as safety, and the company directly contacting workers and threatening to discipline or send home workers from wearing anything that identifies them as a union supporter.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe strike is over unfair labor practices, but we\u8217\'20\'19re far apart over the issues of negotiations,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cordova. \u8220\'20\'1CThe CEO was bragging to the shareholders on Wall Street about how well \uc2 Kroger\uc2  has done during the pandemic while restaurants and businesses were shut down. They thrived, they made record profits, their investors were the recipients of about a billion and a half dollars in stock buybacks and then they come to the bargaining table and say, \u8216\'20\'18we can\u8217\'20\'19t afford it.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kroger\uc2  has also brought in outside workers and hired temporary staff to continue operations during the strike, while King Soopers had already been operating with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsbreak.com/news/2483150169126/union-declines-best-final-offer-from-king-soopers-strike-is-imminent"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2,400 fewer employees}}}\uc2  than normal due to attrition.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s an insult. Our workers are paid $16 an hour to start with or less. Then they offered to pay temporary workers $18 to do our jobs that we\u8217\'20\'19ve been doing, and they expected us to train temporary workers to do our jobs for less money,\u8221\'20\'1D said Carol McMillan, a King Soopers worker in Aurora, Colorado, for seven years.\par \par \uc2 She explained that through the pandemic, grocery workers have faced staffing shortages and long hours, and been treated poorly by employers and customers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the beginning of the pandemic we were heroes and then we were kind of forgotten,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CWe just need them to recognize that without us they can\u8217\'20\'19t run their stores.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A survey of over 10,000 \uc2 Kroger\uc2  workers in California, Washington and Colorado {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://economicrt.org/publication/hungry-at-the-table/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published }}}\uc2  on 11 January by the Economic Roundtable found 14% of \uc2 Kroger\uc2  workers experienced homelessness in the past year. Food insecurity among workers surveyed was rampant, as 34% reported skipping or reducing meals because they couldn\u8217\'20\'19t afford food and 14% of workers rely on Snap assistance.\par \par \uc2 34 percent of \uc2 Kroger\uc2  workers reported skipping or reducing meals because they couldn't afford food. 14 percent of workers reported relying on SNAP assistance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UUrw5xYdBQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UUrw5xYdBQ}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 Michael Sainato (@msainat1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/msainat1/status/1480775595395096582?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 11, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 Kroger\uc2 , the largest supermarket chain in the US, have seen profits and sales soar through the pandemic. The company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cincinnati.com/story/money/2021/03/04/how-much-kroger-profit-during-pandemic/4507949001/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  a profit of $2.6bn in 2020 and the Kroger CEO, \uc2 Rodney McMullen\uc2 , received a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cincinnati.com/story/money/2021/05/17/how-does-kroger-pay-workers-compared-its-ceo/5125727001/#:~:text=Kroger%20CEO%20Rodney%20McMullen's%202020,COVID%2D19%20pandemic%20last%20year."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wage increase of 45%}}}\uc2  to $20.6m. The company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marketwatch.com/story/kroger-stock-rises-after-new-1-billion-stock-buyback-program-authorized-2021-12-30"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 authorized}}}\uc2  another $1bn toward stock buybacks at the end of 2021, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.yahoo.com/now/kroger-kr-boosts-shareholder-returns-192907869.html#:~:text=The%20Kroger%20Co.&text=The%20new%20buyback%20program%20replaces,as%20of%20Dec%2029%2C%202021.&text=During%20the%20third%20quarter%20of,repurchased%20%241%20billion%20of%20shares."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repurchasing $1bn}}}\uc2  in stocks through the first three quarters of 2021. In their latest quarterly earnings, \uc2 Kroger\uc2  reported an increase of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.retail-insight-network.com/news/kroger-q3-2021-results/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 7.2% }}}\uc2  in sales compared with 2020, and saw sales {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supermarketnews.com/retail-financial/kroger-beats-street-q2-despite-identical-digital-sales-declines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increase 1.3%}}}\uc2  over the first two quarters of 2021.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Brookings Institution{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brookings.edu/blog/the-avenue/2021/12/13/with-inflation-surging-big-companies-wage-upticks-arent-nearly-enough/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysis }}}\uc2  published in December 2021 found \uc2 Kroger\uc2  raised average wages from $15 an hour in January 2020 to $16.25 an hour in October 2021, but with recent inflation rates the wage gain equates to just $0.17 an hour.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ir.kroger.com/CorporateProfile/press-releases/press-release/2022/King-Soopers-and-City-Market-Open-for-Customers/default.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 press release}}}\uc2 , the Kroger-owned King Soopers and City Market president, Joe Kelley, criticized the strike and filed unfair labor practice claims against the union after the union had filed unfair labor practice charges with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time for \uc2 Kim Cordova\uc2  to put our associates, her members, first instead of denying them the opportunity to vote on this unprecedented investment. Creating more disruption for our associates, their families, and Coloradans rather than negotiating for a peaceful resolution is irresponsible and undemocratic,\u8221\'20\'1D Kelley said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220113ei1d003jw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
