\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  to terminate unvaccinated workers under \u8216\'20\'18no jab, no job\u8217\'20\'19 policy\b0\par\par\uc2 Edward Helmore in New York \par \uc2 517 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 January 2022\par 19:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bank becomes first on Wall Street to implement a mandate after saying in October it would require all US employees to get vaccine\par \par \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  is set to begin enforcing its \u8220\'20\'1Cno jab, no job\u8221\'20\'1D policy next week, making it the first Wall Street bank to implement a vaccine mandate.\par \par \uc2 The New York-headquartered bank said in October that it would require all US employees to be vaccinated against Covid as a condition of their employment in line with a Biden administration policy requiring workers supporting government contracts to be fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 The Biden policy has been widely challenged in the courts, and is currently before the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  following requests by Republican state officials and business groups to block it.\par \par \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  also said it would examine requests for exemptions on religious or medical grounds, or any other accommodation by state or local law, on a case-by-case basis.\par \par \uc2 More than 90% of \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  staff have so far complied with the mandate and that figure is rising rapidly, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-01-07/citigroup-confronts-vaccine-holdouts-in-no-jab-no-job-mandate?sref=6flipp83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg reported}}}\uc2 , citing a Citigroup spokeswoman. \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 , the news agency said, will place workers who do not comply on unpaid leave, with their last day of employment at the end of the month.\par \par \uc2 The enforcement of \u8220\'20\'1Cno jab, no job\u8221\'20\'1D on 14 January comes as Covid infections have surged in New York to five times last winter\u8217\'20\'19s numbers \u8211\'20\'13 59% thought to be of the highly transmissable Omicron variant.\par \par \uc2 The decision to enforce the mandate comes as Wall Street banks have struggled to get employees back to their office desks after close to two years of remote working.\par \par \uc2 Last month, \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 , the largest US bank, told unvaccinated staff based in Manhattan to work remotely \u8220\'20\'1Cuntil alternative solutions are considered\u8221\'20\'1D and said it was increasing restrictions on unvaccinated workers.\par \par \uc2 In a memo sent to staff, first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/exclusive-jpmorgan-tells-unvaccinated-manhattan-staff-work-home-2021-12-14/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported}}}\uc2  by Reuters, \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  also urged bankers to get Covid vaccines and to receive booster shots, while relaxing mask policy to require they are worn requiring in lobby areas, elevators and in cafes when not eating.\par \par \uc2 The memo, issued during a relative lull between the Delta variant and Omicron surge, said \u8220\'20\'1Cit seems {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/exclusive-jpmorgan-tells-unvaccinated-manhattan-staff-work-home-2021-12-14/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  unfair}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D for vaccinated workers to wear face coverings indoors, adding that doing so would slow down its efforts for a return to normalcy.\par \par \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s move comes as New York\u8217\'20\'19s leadership announced a policy designed to hasten workers\u8217\'20\'19 return to their desks in office buildings that are estimated to be just 30% full.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, New York City\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, Eric Adams, standing beside the state governor, \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2 , proposed easing workers back into businesses with a three-day working week and then expanding to five days in New York City.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI say let\u8217\'20\'19s start out with a three-day week, to let people see how safe it is to come back to work, then we cycle back into a five-day week,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can do this within a three-week period and be up and operating in our city.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020220107ei17002xr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
