\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 WHO warns Omicron could overwhelm health systems as cases rise to record highs in Europe\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agenices \par \uc2 1,064 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 December 2021\par 00:57 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Restrictions return in China, South Africa and Germany as countries around the world struggle to contain new variantCoronavirus \u8211\'20\'13 latest updatesSee all our coronavirus coverage\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2  has warned that the Omicron coronavirus variant could lead to overwhelmed healthcare systems even though early studies suggest it sparks milder disease, as daily case records fell across Europe and the US while China, South Africa and Germany brought back tough restrictions to stamp out infections.\par \par \uc2 Covid-19 surges have wreaked havoc around the world, forcing many nations to make tough choices between economically punishing restrictions and controlling the spread of the virus.\par \par \uc2 The United States{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/28/cdc-people-positive-ovid-asymptomatic-isolate-five-days"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has halved the isolation period}}}\uc2  for asymptomatic cases to try and blunt the disruption, while France has ordered companies to have employees work from home at least three days a week.\par \par \uc2 Contact restrictions were in place in Germany for the second year in a row heading into the New Year, as Europe\u8217\'20\'19s biggest economy shuttered nightclubs and forced sports competitions behind closed doors.\par \par \uc2 Despite facing a much smaller outbreak compared with global virus hotspots, China has not relaxed its \u8220\'20\'1Czero Covid\u8221\'20\'1D strategy, imposing stay-at-home orders in many parts of the city of Yan\u8217\'20\'19an.\par \par \uc2 The hundreds of thousands of affected residents there joined the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/27/covid-cases-rise-in-xian-as-china-battles-biggest-community-outbreak-since-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 13 million people in the city of Xi\u8217\'20\'19an}}}\uc2 , who entered a sixth day of home confinement as China battled its highest daily case numbers in 21 months.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m about to be starved to death,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote one Xi\u8217\'20\'19an resident on the \uc2 Twitter\uc2 -like Weibo platform.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no food, my housing compound won\u8217\'20\'19t let me out, and I\u8217\'20\'19m about to run out of instant noodles \u8230\'20\'26 please help!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many Xi\u8217\'20\'19an residents have similarly complained on social media about the restrictions, which include a ban on driving and only one member of a household permitted to go outside for groceries every three days.\par \par \uc2 This lockdown is the most sweeping in China since the similar-sized city Wuhan was cut off from the world in the early days of the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 South Africa said it would reinstate efforts to trace the contacts of people infected with coronavirus after a backlash over plans to scrap the measure.\par \par \uc2 Health authorities said on Thursday they would stop contact tracing everywhere except places like prisons and schools, as they believed most of the population had already been exposed to the virus through vaccination or infection.\par \par \uc2 Those protocols will be recalled after the Department of Health was inundated with media, stakeholders and public enquiries and comments following the release of the revised regulations.\par \par \uc2 The surges in many countries have been propelled by the highly transmissible Omicron variant, with the Netherlands and Switzerland both saying Tuesday that it has now become the dominant strain in their countries.\par \par \uc2 Greece meanwhile reported a new daily record of 21,657 cases, which health authorities said was linked to the rise of Omicron.\par \par \uc2 The WHO warned against complacency even though preliminary findings suggest that Omicron could lead to milder disease.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA rapid growth of Omicron \u8230\'20\'26 even if combined with a slightly milder disease, will still result in large numbers of hospitalisations, particularly amongst unvaccinated groups, and cause widespread disruption to health systems and other critical services,\u8221\'20\'1D warned WHO Europe\u8217\'20\'19s Covid incident manager, Catherine Smallwood.\par \par \uc2 However, the WHO highlighted the 29% decrease in the incidence of cases observed in South Africa - the country which first reported the variant to the WHO on 24 November.\par \par \uc2 It said early data from Britain, South Africa and Denmark - which currently has the world\u8217\'20\'19s highest rate of infection per person - suggested there was a reduced risk of hospitalisation for Omicron compared to Delta.\par \par \uc2 However, further data was needed to understand Omicron\u8217\'20\'19s severity in terms of clinical markers, including the use of oxygen, mechanical ventilation and death. More data was also required on how the severity might be being impacted by previous Covid infection, or vaccination.\par \par \uc2 To hold back the tide, European nations brought back {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/19/netherlands-to-enter-lockdown-as-nations-across-europe-tighten-curbs-to-slow-omicron-spread"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 curbs with painful economic and social consequences}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Facing record-high infections, France stopped short of issuing a stay-at-home order but called on employers to make staff work from home three days a week where possible.\par \par \uc2 Finland on Tuesday said it would bar unvaccinated foreign travellers from entering. Only residents, essential workers or diplomats will be exempt.\par \par \uc2 Sweden had begun requiring negative tests for incoming non-resident travellers from Tuesday, a day after Denmark \u8211\'20\'13 which currently has the world\u8217\'20\'19s highest rate of infection per capita \u8211\'20\'13 applied the same measure.\par \par \uc2 In Germany, private gatherings are now limited to 10 vaccinated people \u8211\'20\'13 or two households where any unvaccinated people are present \u8211\'20\'13 and nightclubs have been closed. All sports competitions will now be held behind closed doors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSomething has to be done to bring the infection figures down,\u8221\'20\'1D a Berlin resident told AFP TV.\par \par \uc2 But not all accepted the measures.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of protesters went on the march across Germany late Monday against the curbs, with some hurling fireworks or bottles at police and leaving at least 12 officers injured.\par \par \uc2 Beyond social strife, the pandemic has been punishing economically, in particular for sectors like travel.\par \par \uc2 Some 11,500 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/dec/24/christmas-eve-travel-chaos-as-airlines-cancel-more-than-2000-flights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flights have been scrapped}}}\uc2  worldwide since Friday, and tens of thousands more delayed, during one of the year\u8217\'20\'19s busiest travel periods.\par \par \uc2 Multiple airlines have blamed staffing shortages caused by spikes of Omicron cases.\par \par \uc2 The surge in the US has been fuelled by the Omicron variant, as well as large pockets of unvaccinated residents and a lack of access to quick and easy testing.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said Monday some US hospitals could be \u8220\'20\'1Coverrun\u8221\'20\'1D but that the country was generally well prepared.\par \par \uc2 He stressed that Omicron would not have the same impact as the initial Covid outbreak or the Delta variant surge this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COmicron is a source of concern, but it should not be a source of panic,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 In an effort to prevent mass labour shortages during the surge, the \uc2 US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  on Monday cut the isolation period for asymptomatic cases from 10 to five days.\par \par \uc2 The US is the nation hit hardest by the pandemic, and is closing in on its daily high of 250,000 cases recorded last January.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 With Agence France-Presse\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020211229ehct0002u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
